B: $\text{Ti} < \text{V} < \text{Mn}$ — Number of oxidation states
C: $\ce{Cr^{2+}} < \ce{Mn^{2+}} < \ce{Fe^{2+}}$ — Paramagnetic behaviour
D: $\text{Sc} > \text{Cr} > \text{Fe}$ — Density', '$\ce{Mn^{2+}}$ ($3d^5$, 5 unpaired electrons) is more paramagnetic than $\ce{Fe^{2+}}$ ($3d^6$, 4 unpaired), so the order $\ce{Cr^{2+}} < \ce{Mn^{2+}} < \ce{Fe^{2+}}$ for paramagnetic behaviour is wrong.
