D: ', 'Insoluble in $\ce{NaHCO3}$ but soluble in NaOH + $\ce{FeCl3}$ colour → compound is a phenol.
Tribromo derivative ($\ce{C7H5OBr3}$) means three positions on the ring are brominated, consistent with o-cresol where ortho and para positions to $\ce{-OH}$ are available.
