B: *Penicillium*
C: *Fusarium*
D: *Colletotrichum*', 'Both *Aspergillus* (aflatoxin) and *Penicillium* (yellow rice toxins) produce toxins in stored grains/seeds; the answer key marks (a,b) but primary answer is *Aspergillus*.
Hence option (a) is correct (also b accepted).', NULL, 'Requires human/source review; not approved for automatic correction', 'Yes', '2026-10-18T08:47:53.969Z'::timestamptz, '2026-10-18T12:34:15.495Z'::timestamptz, 'https://app.ilearn-india.com/admin/questions/3353?from=bank') ON CONFLICT (qid) DO UPDATE SET "answer_key" = EXCLUDED."answer_key", "solution_key_review_result" = EXCLUDED."solution_key_review_result", "review_status" = EXCLUDED."review_status", "subject" = EXCLUDED."subject", "exam" = EXCLUDED."exam", "chapter" = EXCLUDED."chapter", "screening_batch_existing_question_ordinal" = EXCLUDED."screening_batch_existing_question_ordinal", "category" = EXCLUDED."category", "deterministic_rules" = EXCLUDED."deterministic_rules", "question_specific_finding_evidence" = EXCLUDED."question_specific_finding_evidence", "publication_status_at_screening" = EXCLUDED."publication_status_at_screening", "current_publication_status" = EXCLUDED."current_publication_status", "flag_status" = EXCLUDED."flag_status", "flag_id" = EXCLUDED."flag_id", "action_in_this_10k_run" = EXCLUDED."action_in_this_10k_run", "exam_linked" = EXCLUDED."exam_linked", "question" = EXCLUDED."question", "options" = EXCLUDED."options", "stored_explanation" = EXCLUDED."stored_explanation", "numeric_answer_policy" = EXCLUDED."numeric_answer_policy", "original_review_status_context" = EXCLUDED."original_review_status_context", "content_unchanged_since_screening" = EXCLUDED."content_unchanged_since_screening", "screened_at_utc" = EXCLUDED."screened_at_utc", "live_status_checked_at_utc" = EXCLUDED."live_status_checked_at_utc", "question_url" = EXCLUDED."question_url";
INSERT INTO public.screening_findings_import ("qid", "answer_key", "solution_key_review_result", "review_status", "subject", "exam", "chapter", "screening_batch_existing_question_ordinal", "category", "deterministic_rules", "question_specific_finding_evidence", "publication_status_at_screening", "current_publication_status", "flag_status", "flag_id", "action_in_this_10k_run", "exam_linked", "question", "options", "stored_explanation", "numeric_answer_policy", "original_review_status_context", "content_unchanged_since_screening", "screened_at_utc", "live_status_checked_at_utc", "question_url") VALUES (3503, 'A: *Osmunda* and *Equisetum*', 'Ectophloic/amphiphloic terminology mismatch', 'Human validation required; screening is not an Answer Audit', 'Biology', 'NEET', '3. Plant Kingdom', '1-5000', 'Unsupported adjustment / explanation defect; key not proven wrong', NULL, 'Question asks ectophloic; explanation describes the saved pair as amphiphloic and appeals to source key. Botanical source review needed.', 'published', 'draft', 'open', 1479, 'Historical finding; no status change in this run', 'Yes', 'Ectophloic siphonostele is found in', 'A: *Osmunda* and *Equisetum*
B: *Marsilea* and *Botrychium*
C: *Adiantum* and Cucurbitaceae
D: *Dicksonia* and Maiden hair fern', 'In ectophloic siphonostele, central pith is surrounded by xylem then phloem outward. Amphiphloic siphonostele (phloem on both sides of xylem) is found in *Osmunda* and *Equisetum* — but the answer key marks (a) as correct per the book.
Hence option (a) is correct.', NULL, 'Requires human/source review; not approved for automatic correction', 'Yes', '2026-10-18T08:47:53.969Z'::timestamptz, '2026-10-18T12:34:15.495Z'::timestamptz, 'https://app.ilearn-india.com/admin/questions/3503?from=bank') ON CONFLICT (qid) DO UPDATE SET "answer_key" = EXCLUDED."answer_key", "solution_key_review_result" = EXCLUDED."solution_key_review_result", "review_status" = EXCLUDED."review_status", "subject" = EXCLUDED."subject", "exam" = EXCLUDED."exam", "chapter" = EXCLUDED."chapter", "screening_batch_existing_question_ordinal" = EXCLUDED."screening_batch_existing_question_ordinal", "category" = EXCLUDED."category", "deterministic_rules" = EXCLUDED."deterministic_rules", "question_specific_finding_evidence" = EXCLUDED."question_specific_finding_evidence", "publication_status_at_screening" = EXCLUDED."publication_status_at_screening", "current_publication_status" = EXCLUDED."current_publication_status", "flag_status" = EXCLUDED."flag_status", "flag_id" = EXCLUDED."flag_id", "action_in_this_10k_run" = EXCLUDED."action_in_this_10k_run", "exam_linked" = EXCLUDED."exam_linked", "question" = EXCLUDED."question", "options" = EXCLUDED."options", "stored_explanation" = EXCLUDED."stored_explanation", "numeric_answer_policy" = EXCLUDED."numeric_answer_policy", "original_review_status_context" = EXCLUDED."original_review_status_context", "content_unchanged_since_screening" = EXCLUDED."content_unchanged_since_screening", "screened_at_utc" = EXCLUDED."screened_at_utc", "live_status_checked_at_utc" = EXCLUDED."live_status_checked_at_utc", "question_url" = EXCLUDED."question_url";
INSERT INTO public.screening_findings_import ("qid", "answer_key", "solution_key_review_result", "review_status", "subject", "exam", "chapter", "screening_batch_existing_question_ordinal", "category", "deterministic_rules", "question_specific_finding_evidence", "publication_status_at_screening", "current_publication_status", "flag_status", "flag_id", "action_in_this_10k_run", "exam_linked", "question", "options", "stored_explanation", "numeric_answer_policy", "original_review_status_context", "content_unchanged_since_screening", "screened_at_utc", "live_status_checked_at_utc", "question_url") VALUES (3586, 'D: *Aurelia* – Cnidoblasts; Organ level of organization – Coelenterata', 'No entirely correct option according to solution', 'Human validation required; screening is not an Answer Audit', 'Biology', 'NEET', '4. Animal Kingdom', '1-5000', 'No-valid-option assertion with a saved option', NULL, 'Explanation identifies tissue/organ-level mismatch in the saved Aurelia pairing, but records it as closest.', 'published', 'draft', 'open', 1480, 'Historical finding; no status change in this run', 'Yes', 'In which one of the following the genus name, its two characters and its class/phylum are correctly matched?

![184](https://pub-46f930544d71428a9520666ac871983d.r2.dev/question-assets/8f9d3881-b73d-4519-aee9-b448002db141.webp)', 'A: *Ascaris* – Body segmented; Males and females distinct – Annelida
B: *Salamandra* – A tympanum represents ear; Fertilization is external – Amphibia
C: *Pteropus* – Skin possesses hair; Oviparous – Mammalia
D: *Aurelia* – Cnidoblasts; Organ level of organization – Coelenterata', 'None of the options is entirely correct per the answer key (marked *).
