D: Cyclopentyl ring with $\ce{OH}$ and two $\ce{CH3}$ groups, $\ce{C=O}$ remaining

![img78d](https://pub-46f930544d71428a9520666ac871983d.r2.dev/question-assets/dfc4fcb5-4adc-456b-9381-0257206fc8f4.webp)', 'Excess $\ce{CH3MgBr}$ first adds to the ketone $\ce{C=O}$ giving a tertiary alcohol; the CN group is not attacked by Grignard under these conditions.
