B: ![8b](https://pub-46f930544d71428a9520666ac871983d.r2.dev/question-assets/ad66a1d1-25d9-4d4d-8836-ddeea500c7f8.webp)
C: ![8c](https://pub-46f930544d71428a9520666ac871983d.r2.dev/question-assets/b372c058-c8be-40a3-84e3-d00f0204ad16.webp)
D: ![8d](https://pub-46f930544d71428a9520666ac871983d.r2.dev/question-assets/acdfdac0-6c87-45bd-8c80-c0a21b77e2f3.webp)', 'Photocurrent is proportional to the number of photons per second (intensity/power), so $I$ decreases linearly as power decreases.
Stopping potential depends only on the frequency (energy) of photons, not on intensity — frequency is unchanged.
So $|V|$ remains constant while $I$ falls linearly.
Hence option (1) is correct.', NULL, 'Potential candidate — human review required; no correction approved', 'Yes', '2026-10-18T11:00:20.276Z'::timestamptz, '2026-10-18T12:34:15.495Z'::timestamptz, 'https://app.ilearn-india.com/admin/questions/10924?from=bank') ON CONFLICT (qid) DO UPDATE SET "answer_key" = EXCLUDED."answer_key", "solution_key_review_result" = EXCLUDED."solution_key_review_result", "review_status" = EXCLUDED."review_status", "subject" = EXCLUDED."subject", "exam" = EXCLUDED."exam", "chapter" = EXCLUDED."chapter", "screening_batch_existing_question_ordinal" = EXCLUDED."screening_batch_existing_question_ordinal", "category" = EXCLUDED."category", "deterministic_rules" = EXCLUDED."deterministic_rules", "question_specific_finding_evidence" = EXCLUDED."question_specific_finding_evidence", "publication_status_at_screening" = EXCLUDED."publication_status_at_screening", "current_publication_status" = EXCLUDED."current_publication_status", "flag_status" = EXCLUDED."flag_status", "flag_id" = EXCLUDED."flag_id", "action_in_this_10k_run" = EXCLUDED."action_in_this_10k_run", "exam_linked" = EXCLUDED."exam_linked", "question" = EXCLUDED."question", "options" = EXCLUDED."options", "stored_explanation" = EXCLUDED."stored_explanation", "numeric_answer_policy" = EXCLUDED."numeric_answer_policy", "original_review_status_context" = EXCLUDED."original_review_status_context", "content_unchanged_since_screening" = EXCLUDED."content_unchanged_since_screening", "screened_at_utc" = EXCLUDED."screened_at_utc", "live_status_checked_at_utc" = EXCLUDED."live_status_checked_at_utc", "question_url" = EXCLUDED."question_url";
INSERT INTO public.screening_findings_import ("qid", "answer_key", "solution_key_review_result", "review_status", "subject", "exam", "chapter", "screening_batch_existing_question_ordinal", "category", "deterministic_rules", "question_specific_finding_evidence", "publication_status_at_screening", "current_publication_status", "flag_status", "flag_id", "action_in_this_10k_run", "exam_linked", "question", "options", "stored_explanation", "numeric_answer_policy", "original_review_status_context", "content_unchanged_since_screening", "screened_at_utc", "live_status_checked_at_utc", "question_url") VALUES (10948, 'No exact option identity: ![32b](https://pub-46f930544d71428a9520666ac871983d.r2.dev/question-assets/6f470a0b-f750-427b-9ef4-f5f91cbe5bfa.webp)', 'Not independently determined; inspect the stored solution', 'Human validation required; screening is not an Answer Audit', 'Physics', 'NEET', '6. Electromagnetic Induction', '10001-15000', 'Saved key/current-option identity mismatch', 'answer_identity', 'The saved answer text/image identity is absent from the current options. This can be an identity/scoring defect even if the images look equivalent; no visual equivalence or replacement key has been assumed.', 'published', 'published', 'open', 1681, 'Historical finding; no status change in this run', 'Yes', 'A conducting loop of finite resistance lies on the $x$-$y$ plane. There is a constant magnetic field in the $z$ direction. The area of the loop varies with time $t$, as $A = A_0(1 + \sin t)$ in appropriate units. The figure that correctly indicates the qualitative behaviour of the power $P$ dissipated in the loop as a function of time is:', 'A: ![32a](https://pub-46f930544d71428a9520666ac871983d.r2.dev/question-assets/34bc6cfd-d8ca-4e53-9231-859dd08261cf.webp)
B: ![32b](https://pub-46f930544d71428a9520666ac871983d.r2.dev/question-assets/398d2f8f-71f1-43b0-9446-a482c5cba789.webp)
C: ![32c](https://pub-46f930544d71428a9520666ac871983d.r2.dev/question-assets/592ad685-1c23-4688-8ec8-ab7fa5a983ed.webp)
D: ![32d](https://pub-46f930544d71428a9520666ac871983d.r2.dev/question-assets/d0e6335e-6227-44f7-aa69-36c42c03110c.webp)', 'Induced EMF $\varepsilon = -B\dfrac{dA}{dt} = -BA_0\cos t$; power $P = \varepsilon^2/R \propto \cos^2 t$.
$\cos^2 t = \frac{1+\cos 2t}{2}$: this oscillates between 0 and a maximum, giving two complete peaks in one full period, i.e. the graph with two humps.
But the graphs shown suggest option (2) is a single decreasing arch followed by rise — the correct $\cos^2 t$ shape starting from $P = $ max at $t=0$, dipping to zero and rising.
Hence option (2) is correct.', NULL, 'Potential candidate — human review required; no correction approved', 'Yes', '2026-10-18T11:00:20.276Z'::timestamptz, '2026-10-18T12:34:15.495Z'::timestamptz, 'https://app.ilearn-india.com/admin/questions/10948?from=bank') ON CONFLICT (qid) DO UPDATE SET "answer_key" = EXCLUDED."answer_key", "solution_key_review_result" = EXCLUDED."solution_key_review_result", "review_status" = EXCLUDED."review_status", "subject" = EXCLUDED."subject", "exam" = EXCLUDED."exam", "chapter" = EXCLUDED."chapter", "screening_batch_existing_question_ordinal" = EXCLUDED."screening_batch_existing_question_ordinal", "category" = EXCLUDED."category", "deterministic_rules" = EXCLUDED."deterministic_rules", "question_specific_finding_evidence" = EXCLUDED."question_specific_finding_evidence", "publication_status_at_screening" = EXCLUDED."publication_status_at_screening", "current_publication_status" = EXCLUDED."current_publication_status", "flag_status" = EXCLUDED."flag_status", "flag_id" = EXCLUDED."flag_id", "action_in_this_10k_run" = EXCLUDED."action_in_this_10k_run", "exam_linked" = EXCLUDED."exam_linked", "question" = EXCLUDED."question", "options" = EXCLUDED."options", "stored_explanation" = EXCLUDED."stored_explanation", "numeric_answer_policy" = EXCLUDED."numeric_answer_policy", "original_review_status_context" = EXCLUDED."original_review_status_context", "content_unchanged_since_screening" = EXCLUDED."content_unchanged_since_screening", "screened_at_utc" = EXCLUDED."screened_at_utc", "live_status_checked_at_utc" = EXCLUDED."live_status_checked_at_utc", "question_url" = EXCLUDED."question_url";
INSERT INTO public.screening_findings_import ("qid", "answer_key", "solution_key_review_result", "review_status", "subject", "exam", "chapter", "screening_batch_existing_question_ordinal", "category", "deterministic_rules", "question_specific_finding_evidence", "publication_status_at_screening", "current_publication_status", "flag_status", "flag_id", "action_in_this_10k_run", "exam_linked", "question", "options", "stored_explanation", "numeric_answer_policy", "original_review_status_context", "content_unchanged_since_screening", "screened_at_utc", "live_status_checked_at_utc", "question_url") VALUES (11012, 'A: $\vec{M} \times \vec{B}$', 'Not independently determined; inspect the stored solution', 'Human validation required; screening is not an Answer Audit', 'Physics', 'NEET', '5. Magnetism and Matter', '10001-15000', 'Multiple accepted answers or inconsistent conclusion', 'answer_set', 'The solution says A and D are equivalent torque expressions and both correct, but only A is saved.', 'published', 'published', 'open', 1682, 'Historical finding; no status change in this run', 'Yes', 'A bar magnet of magnetic moment $\vec{M}$, is placed in a magnetic field of induction $\vec{B}$. The torque exerted on it is', 'A: $\vec{M} \times \vec{B}$
B: $-\vec{M} \cdot \vec{B}$
C: $\vec{M} \cdot \vec{B}$
D: $-\vec{B} \times \vec{M}$', 'The torque on a magnetic dipole in a field is $\vec{\tau} = \vec{M} \times \vec{B}$.
Note that $\vec{M}\times\vec{B} = -\vec{B}\times\vec{M}$, so options (a) and (d) have equal magnitude (both accepted in key).
Hence options (a) and (d) are both correct.', NULL, 'Potential candidate — human review required; no correction approved', 'Yes', '2026-10-18T11:00:20.276Z'::timestamptz, '2026-10-18T12:34:15.495Z'::timestamptz, 'https://app.ilearn-india.com/admin/questions/11012?from=bank') ON CONFLICT (qid) DO UPDATE SET "answer_key" = EXCLUDED."answer_key", "solution_key_review_result" = EXCLUDED."solution_key_review_result", "review_status" = EXCLUDED."review_status", "subject" = EXCLUDED."subject", "exam" = EXCLUDED."exam", "chapter" = EXCLUDED."chapter", "screening_batch_existing_question_ordinal" = EXCLUDED."screening_batch_existing_question_ordinal", "category" = EXCLUDED."category", "deterministic_rules" = EXCLUDED."deterministic_rules", "question_specific_finding_evidence" = EXCLUDED."question_specific_finding_evidence", "publication_status_at_screening" = EXCLUDED."publication_status_at_screening", "current_publication_status" = EXCLUDED."current_publication_status", "flag_status" = EXCLUDED."flag_status", "flag_id" = EXCLUDED."flag_id", "action_in_this_10k_run" = EXCLUDED."action_in_this_10k_run", "exam_linked" = EXCLUDED."exam_linked", "question" = EXCLUDED."question", "options" = EXCLUDED."options", "stored_explanation" = EXCLUDED."stored_explanation", "numeric_answer_policy" = EXCLUDED."numeric_answer_policy", "original_review_status_context" = EXCLUDED."original_review_status_context", "content_unchanged_since_screening" = EXCLUDED."content_unchanged_since_screening", "screened_at_utc" = EXCLUDED."screened_at_utc", "live_status_checked_at_utc" = EXCLUDED."live_status_checked_at_utc", "question_url" = EXCLUDED."question_url";
