![8](https://pub-46f930544d71428a9520666ac871983d.r2.dev/question-assets/3b7b3ff4-eac6-421a-bef1-3360556986be.webp)', 'Not independently determined; inspect the stored solution', 'Human validation required; screening is not an Answer Audit', 'Chemistry', 'NEET', '6. Haloalkanes and Haloarenes', '10001-15000', 'Saved key/current-option identity mismatch', 'answer_identity', 'The saved answer text/image identity is absent from the current options. This can be an identity/scoring defect even if the images look equivalent; no visual equivalence or replacement key has been assumed.', 'published', 'published', 'open', 1683, 'Historical finding; no status change in this run', 'Yes', 'One of the products formed in the following reaction is

Cyclohexyl–$\ce{MgBr}$ + Cyclopentyl–$\ce{NH2}$ $\longrightarrow$

![Reaction: cyclohexyl-MgBr + cyclopentyl-NH2 with arrow](https://pub-46f930544d71428a9520666ac871983d.r2.dev/question-assets/ee0d372f-c30b-44a8-9170-3300cbfddc73.webp)', 'A: Diphenylamine-type product (cyclohexyl and cyclopentyl connected via NH)

![Option 1: two cyclic rings connected via N-H (diphenylamine analogue)](https://pub-46f930544d71428a9520666ac871983d.r2.dev/question-assets/3620de7e-a88e-4895-9439-75652bda53b6.webp)
B: Bicyclic product with $\ce{NH2}$ substituent

![Option 2: bicyclic structure with NH2 substituent](https://pub-46f930544d71428a9520666ac871983d.r2.dev/question-assets/dc97aa67-0aa0-4c47-8741-9409bc6e2203.webp)
C: Bicyclic product (two rings fused)

![Option 3: two fused rings (bicyclic)](https://pub-46f930544d71428a9520666ac871983d.r2.dev/question-assets/9d143b49-0e7d-4cd4-a326-0ea8b30d57f6.webp)
D: Cyclopentane (single ring)

![8](https://pub-46f930544d71428a9520666ac871983d.r2.dev/question-assets/762d7dfa-f646-44da-aa0e-7447b2e567a1.webp)', 'A Grignard reagent ($\ce{R-MgBr}$) reacts with a primary amine ($\ce{R''NH2}$) by simple proton transfer: $\ce{R-MgBr + R''NH2 -> R-H + R''NH-MgBr}$.
The alkane R–H (cyclohexane) is released, and the single ring cyclopentane skeleton-related amine–MgBr forms; the organic product isolated is cyclopentane (from the amine side) and cyclohexane (from Grignard side).
Looking at the answer key (option 4), cyclopentane is the product shown.
Hence option (4) is correct.', NULL, 'Potential candidate — human review required; no correction approved', 'Yes', '2026-10-18T11:00:20.276Z'::timestamptz, '2026-10-18T12:34:15.495Z'::timestamptz, 'https://app.ilearn-india.com/admin/questions/11049?from=bank') ON CONFLICT (qid) DO UPDATE SET "answer_key" = EXCLUDED."answer_key", "solution_key_review_result" = EXCLUDED."solution_key_review_result", "review_status" = EXCLUDED."review_status", "subject" = EXCLUDED."subject", "exam" = EXCLUDED."exam", "chapter" = EXCLUDED."chapter", "screening_batch_existing_question_ordinal" = EXCLUDED."screening_batch_existing_question_ordinal", "category" = EXCLUDED."category", "deterministic_rules" = EXCLUDED."deterministic_rules", "question_specific_finding_evidence" = EXCLUDED."question_specific_finding_evidence", "publication_status_at_screening" = EXCLUDED."publication_status_at_screening", "current_publication_status" = EXCLUDED."current_publication_status", "flag_status" = EXCLUDED."flag_status", "flag_id" = EXCLUDED."flag_id", "action_in_this_10k_run" = EXCLUDED."action_in_this_10k_run", "exam_linked" = EXCLUDED."exam_linked", "question" = EXCLUDED."question", "options" = EXCLUDED."options", "stored_explanation" = EXCLUDED."stored_explanation", "numeric_answer_policy" = EXCLUDED."numeric_answer_policy", "original_review_status_context" = EXCLUDED."original_review_status_context", "content_unchanged_since_screening" = EXCLUDED."content_unchanged_since_screening", "screened_at_utc" = EXCLUDED."screened_at_utc", "live_status_checked_at_utc" = EXCLUDED."live_status_checked_at_utc", "question_url" = EXCLUDED."question_url";
