Statement-II: Density of the solution changes when percentage by mass of solution changes.', 'A: Statement-I and Statement-II both are correct.
B: Statement-I and Statement-II both are incorrect.
C: Statement-I is correct and Statement-II is incorrect.
D: Statement-I is incorrect and Statement-II is correct.', 'Molarity $M = \frac{n}{V}$ depends on solution volume, which is affected by density.
Molality $m = \frac{n}{\text{mass of solvent}}$ is independent of temperature and density.
Density changes with temperature and solute mass percentage, affecting both molarity and solution properties.
Statement-I is partially incorrect (molality does not change with density).
Hence option (c) is correct.', NULL, 'Potential candidate — human review required; no correction approved', 'Yes', '2026-10-18T11:00:20.276Z'::timestamptz, '2026-10-18T12:34:15.495Z'::timestamptz, 'https://app.ilearn-india.com/admin/questions/12456?from=bank') ON CONFLICT (qid) DO UPDATE SET "answer_key" = EXCLUDED."answer_key", "solution_key_review_result" = EXCLUDED."solution_key_review_result", "review_status" = EXCLUDED."review_status", "subject" = EXCLUDED."subject", "exam" = EXCLUDED."exam", "chapter" = EXCLUDED."chapter", "screening_batch_existing_question_ordinal" = EXCLUDED."screening_batch_existing_question_ordinal", "category" = EXCLUDED."category", "deterministic_rules" = EXCLUDED."deterministic_rules", "question_specific_finding_evidence" = EXCLUDED."question_specific_finding_evidence", "publication_status_at_screening" = EXCLUDED."publication_status_at_screening", "current_publication_status" = EXCLUDED."current_publication_status", "flag_status" = EXCLUDED."flag_status", "flag_id" = EXCLUDED."flag_id", "action_in_this_10k_run" = EXCLUDED."action_in_this_10k_run", "exam_linked" = EXCLUDED."exam_linked", "question" = EXCLUDED."question", "options" = EXCLUDED."options", "stored_explanation" = EXCLUDED."stored_explanation", "numeric_answer_policy" = EXCLUDED."numeric_answer_policy", "original_review_status_context" = EXCLUDED."original_review_status_context", "content_unchanged_since_screening" = EXCLUDED."content_unchanged_since_screening", "screened_at_utc" = EXCLUDED."screened_at_utc", "live_status_checked_at_utc" = EXCLUDED."live_status_checked_at_utc", "question_url" = EXCLUDED."question_url";
INSERT INTO public.screening_findings_import ("qid", "answer_key", "solution_key_review_result", "review_status", "subject", "exam", "chapter", "screening_batch_existing_question_ordinal", "category", "deterministic_rules", "question_specific_finding_evidence", "publication_status_at_screening", "current_publication_status", "flag_status", "flag_id", "action_in_this_10k_run", "exam_linked", "question", "options", "stored_explanation", "numeric_answer_policy", "original_review_status_context", "content_unchanged_since_screening", "screened_at_utc", "live_status_checked_at_utc", "question_url") VALUES (12460, 'B: Statement-I and Statement-II both are incorrect.', 'Not independently determined; inspect the stored solution', 'Human validation required; screening is not an Answer Audit', 'Chemistry', 'NEET', '1. Some Basic Concepts of Chemistry', '10001-15000', 'Unsupported adjustment / explanation defect; key not proven wrong', NULL, 'The explanation labels Statement II true under its n-factor argument, then declares both statements incorrect to match saved B. Its pure-water molarity argument also needs review.', 'published', 'published', 'open', 1718, 'Historical finding; no status change in this run', 'No', 'Statement-I: Molarity and normality of pure water are different.

Statement-II: Molecular mass and equivalent mass of $\ce{H2O}$ are same.', 'A: Statement-I and Statement-II both are correct.
B: Statement-I and Statement-II both are incorrect.
C: Statement-I is correct and Statement-II is incorrect.
D: Statement-I is incorrect and Statement-II is correct.', 'Pure water: $K_w = 10^{-14}$; $[\ce{H+}] = 10^{-7}$ M → molarity ≈ $10^{-7}$ M.
For water as amphoteric: n-factor = 1 (can donate or accept one proton in neutralization).
Normality = Molarity × n-factor = $10^{-7} \times 1 = 10^{-7}$ N (same as molarity).
Statement-I is false (they are equal, not different).
Statement-II: MW of $\ce{H2O}$ = 18 g/mol; equivalent mass = 18/1 = 18 g/equiv (true for hydration/dehydration, but context matters).
Both statements are effectively incorrect as stated.
Hence option (b) is correct.', NULL, 'Potential candidate — human review required; no correction approved', 'Yes', '2026-10-18T11:00:20.276Z'::timestamptz, '2026-10-18T12:34:15.495Z'::timestamptz, 'https://app.ilearn-india.com/admin/questions/12460?from=bank') ON CONFLICT (qid) DO UPDATE SET "answer_key" = EXCLUDED."answer_key", "solution_key_review_result" = EXCLUDED."solution_key_review_result", "review_status" = EXCLUDED."review_status", "subject" = EXCLUDED."subject", "exam" = EXCLUDED."exam", "chapter" = EXCLUDED."chapter", "screening_batch_existing_question_ordinal" = EXCLUDED."screening_batch_existing_question_ordinal", "category" = EXCLUDED."category", "deterministic_rules" = EXCLUDED."deterministic_rules", "question_specific_finding_evidence" = EXCLUDED."question_specific_finding_evidence", "publication_status_at_screening" = EXCLUDED."publication_status_at_screening", "current_publication_status" = EXCLUDED."current_publication_status", "flag_status" = EXCLUDED."flag_status", "flag_id" = EXCLUDED."flag_id", "action_in_this_10k_run" = EXCLUDED."action_in_this_10k_run", "exam_linked" = EXCLUDED."exam_linked", "question" = EXCLUDED."question", "options" = EXCLUDED."options", "stored_explanation" = EXCLUDED."stored_explanation", "numeric_answer_policy" = EXCLUDED."numeric_answer_policy", "original_review_status_context" = EXCLUDED."original_review_status_context", "content_unchanged_since_screening" = EXCLUDED."content_unchanged_since_screening", "screened_at_utc" = EXCLUDED."screened_at_utc", "live_status_checked_at_utc" = EXCLUDED."live_status_checked_at_utc", "question_url" = EXCLUDED."question_url";
INSERT INTO public.screening_findings_import ("qid", "answer_key", "solution_key_review_result", "review_status", "subject", "exam", "chapter", "screening_batch_existing_question_ordinal", "category", "deterministic_rules", "question_specific_finding_evidence", "publication_status_at_screening", "current_publication_status", "flag_status", "flag_id", "action_in_this_10k_run", "exam_linked", "question", "options", "stored_explanation", "numeric_answer_policy", "original_review_status_context", "content_unchanged_since_screening", "screened_at_utc", "live_status_checked_at_utc", "question_url") VALUES (12468, 'C: $1.2 \times 10^{23}$', 'Not independently determined; inspect the stored solution', 'Human validation required; screening is not an Answer Audit', 'Chemistry', 'NEET', '1. Some Basic Concepts of Chemistry', '10001-15000', 'No-valid-option assertion with a saved option', NULL, 'The volume ratio gives 1.2×10^21 molecules; saved C is 1.2×10^23. The solution invokes a typo/different premise to keep C.', 'published', 'published', 'open', 1719, 'Historical finding; no status change in this run', 'No', '500 mL of $\ce{NH3}$ contains $6.0 \times 10^{21}$ molecules at STP. How many molecules are present in 100 mL of $\ce{CO2}$ at STP?', 'A: $6 \times 10^{21}$
B: $1.5 \times 10^{23}$
C: $1.2 \times 10^{23}$
D: None of these', 'At STP, equal volumes of gases contain equal number of molecules (Avogadro''s law).
500 mL $\ce{NH3}$ → $6.0 \times 10^{21}$ molecules.
100 mL $\ce{CO2}$ → $(100/500) \times 6.0 \times 10^{21}$ = $1.2 \times 10^{21}$ molecules.
But if problem intends 100 mL at STP from standard 22400 mL = 1 mol condition:
