B: F⁻ < O²⁻ < N³⁻
C: Na < Li < K
D: Fe³⁺ < Fe²⁺ < Fe⁴⁺', 'N < Be < B: incorrect (N is period 2, Be and B are also period 2; B > Be > N in size). Wrong.
F⁻ < O²⁻ < N³⁻: all are isoelectronic (10 electrons). Ionic radius increases with decreasing nuclear charge: F⁻ (Z=9) < O²⁻ (Z=8) < N³⁻ (Z=7). Correct.
Na < Li < K: incorrect (Na and K are groups 1, but K > Na > Li in size). Wrong.
Fe³⁺ < Fe²⁺ < Fe⁴⁺: incorrect (more positive charge = smaller radius, so Fe⁴⁺ << Fe³⁺ < Fe²⁺). Wrong.
Hence option (b) is correct.', NULL, 'Potential candidate — human review required; no correction approved', 'Yes', '2026-10-18T11:00:20.276Z'::timestamptz, '2026-10-18T12:34:15.495Z'::timestamptz, 'https://app.ilearn-india.com/admin/questions/12680?from=bank') ON CONFLICT (qid) DO UPDATE SET "answer_key" = EXCLUDED."answer_key", "solution_key_review_result" = EXCLUDED."solution_key_review_result", "review_status" = EXCLUDED."review_status", "subject" = EXCLUDED."subject", "exam" = EXCLUDED."exam", "chapter" = EXCLUDED."chapter", "screening_batch_existing_question_ordinal" = EXCLUDED."screening_batch_existing_question_ordinal", "category" = EXCLUDED."category", "deterministic_rules" = EXCLUDED."deterministic_rules", "question_specific_finding_evidence" = EXCLUDED."question_specific_finding_evidence", "publication_status_at_screening" = EXCLUDED."publication_status_at_screening", "current_publication_status" = EXCLUDED."current_publication_status", "flag_status" = EXCLUDED."flag_status", "flag_id" = EXCLUDED."flag_id", "action_in_this_10k_run" = EXCLUDED."action_in_this_10k_run", "exam_linked" = EXCLUDED."exam_linked", "question" = EXCLUDED."question", "options" = EXCLUDED."options", "stored_explanation" = EXCLUDED."stored_explanation", "numeric_answer_policy" = EXCLUDED."numeric_answer_policy", "original_review_status_context" = EXCLUDED."original_review_status_context", "content_unchanged_since_screening" = EXCLUDED."content_unchanged_since_screening", "screened_at_utc" = EXCLUDED."screened_at_utc", "live_status_checked_at_utc" = EXCLUDED."live_status_checked_at_utc", "question_url" = EXCLUDED."question_url";
INSERT INTO public.screening_findings_import ("qid", "answer_key", "solution_key_review_result", "review_status", "subject", "exam", "chapter", "screening_batch_existing_question_ordinal", "category", "deterministic_rules", "question_specific_finding_evidence", "publication_status_at_screening", "current_publication_status", "flag_status", "flag_id", "action_in_this_10k_run", "exam_linked", "question", "options", "stored_explanation", "numeric_answer_policy", "original_review_status_context", "content_unchanged_since_screening", "screened_at_utc", "live_status_checked_at_utc", "question_url") VALUES (12681, 'B: Br₂ < F₂ < Cl₂ : electron affinity', 'Not independently determined; inspect the stored solution', 'Human validation required; screening is not an Answer Audit', 'Chemistry', 'NEET', '3. Classification of Elements and Periodicity in Properties', '10001-15000', 'Derivation/key contradiction', NULL, 'The explanation labels Br<F<Cl electron affinity incorrect while stating the equivalent Cl>F>Br as the actual order, and saves B as the incorrect arrangement.', 'published', 'published', 'open', 1733, 'Historical finding; no status change in this run', 'No', 'Which one of the following arrangements does not truly represent the property indicated against it?', 'A: Br₂ < Cl₂ < F₂ : electronegativity
B: Br₂ < F₂ < Cl₂ : electron affinity
C: Br₂ < Cl₂ < F₂ : bond energy
D: Br₂ < Cl₂ < F₂ : oxidizing power', 'Br₂ < Cl₂ < F₂ (electronegativity): correct.
Br₂ < F₂ < Cl₂ (electron affinity): electron affinity order is Cl > F > Br (Cl has the highest, not F). This is incorrect.
Br₂ < Cl₂ < F₂ (bond energy): correct (F–F bond is strongest).
Br₂ < Cl₂ < F₂ (oxidizing power): correct.
