(ii) In $\ce{C3O2}$ the oxidation states of carbon are +2, 0, +2.
(iii) Oxidation number of sulphur in $\ce{H2SO5}$ is +8.
(iv) Oxidation number of chromium in $\ce{CrO5}$ is +6.', 'A: (i), (ii)
B: (i), (iii)
