B: Bond angle ∠HBH is greater than ∠HtBHt.
C: Bond length B···Hb is greater than B – Ht.
D: Bond angle ∠HbBHt is lesser than ∠HtBHt.', 'In diborane, terminal H–B–H angles ($\ce{∠HtBHt}$ ~122°) are actually smaller than bridging H–B–H angles ($\ce{∠HbBHb}$ ~150°).
Statement (b) reverses this relationship and is thus incorrect.
All other statements about $\ce{sp^3}$ hybridisation, longer bridge bonds, and angle relationships are correct.
Hence option (b) is correct.', NULL, 'Potential candidate — human review required; no correction approved', 'Yes', '2026-10-18T11:00:20.276Z'::timestamptz, '2026-10-18T12:34:15.495Z'::timestamptz, 'https://app.ilearn-india.com/admin/questions/13571?from=bank') ON CONFLICT (qid) DO UPDATE SET "answer_key" = EXCLUDED."answer_key", "solution_key_review_result" = EXCLUDED."solution_key_review_result", "review_status" = EXCLUDED."review_status", "subject" = EXCLUDED."subject", "exam" = EXCLUDED."exam", "chapter" = EXCLUDED."chapter", "screening_batch_existing_question_ordinal" = EXCLUDED."screening_batch_existing_question_ordinal", "category" = EXCLUDED."category", "deterministic_rules" = EXCLUDED."deterministic_rules", "question_specific_finding_evidence" = EXCLUDED."question_specific_finding_evidence", "publication_status_at_screening" = EXCLUDED."publication_status_at_screening", "current_publication_status" = EXCLUDED."current_publication_status", "flag_status" = EXCLUDED."flag_status", "flag_id" = EXCLUDED."flag_id", "action_in_this_10k_run" = EXCLUDED."action_in_this_10k_run", "exam_linked" = EXCLUDED."exam_linked", "question" = EXCLUDED."question", "options" = EXCLUDED."options", "stored_explanation" = EXCLUDED."stored_explanation", "numeric_answer_policy" = EXCLUDED."numeric_answer_policy", "original_review_status_context" = EXCLUDED."original_review_status_context", "content_unchanged_since_screening" = EXCLUDED."content_unchanged_since_screening", "screened_at_utc" = EXCLUDED."screened_at_utc", "live_status_checked_at_utc" = EXCLUDED."live_status_checked_at_utc", "question_url" = EXCLUDED."question_url";
INSERT INTO public.screening_findings_import ("qid", "answer_key", "solution_key_review_result", "review_status", "subject", "exam", "chapter", "screening_batch_existing_question_ordinal", "category", "deterministic_rules", "question_specific_finding_evidence", "publication_status_at_screening", "current_publication_status", "flag_status", "flag_id", "action_in_this_10k_run", "exam_linked", "question", "options", "stored_explanation", "numeric_answer_policy", "original_review_status_context", "content_unchanged_since_screening", "screened_at_utc", "live_status_checked_at_utc", "question_url") VALUES (13584, 'B: 1, 2, 3', 'Not independently determined; inspect the stored solution', 'Human validation required; screening is not an Answer Audit', 'Chemistry', 'NEET', '3. Classification of Elements and Periodicity in Properties', '10001-15000', 'Derivation/key contradiction', NULL, 'The solution endorses statements 2,3,4, but the saved answer text is 1,2,3. The statements were incorrectly placed inside the first answer option, shifting labels.', 'published', 'published', 'open', 1767, 'Historical finding; no status change in this run', 'Yes', 'Which of the following statement is/are correct regarding B–F bond in BF₃?', 'A: (1) The unusual shortness and strength of the bonds may be explained by a pπ–dπ interaction between boron and fluoride. (2) The unusual shortness and strength of the BF bond may be explained by pπ–pπ interaction between boron and fluorine atoms. (3) All the three B–F bond lengths are equal and each of them is shorter than the sum of the covalent radii of boron and fluoride. (4) The bond energy of the B–F bond is very high, higher than for any other single bond.
B: 1, 2, 3
C: (b) 1, 3, 4
D: (c) 2, 3, 4', 'The B–F bond in $\ce{BF3}$ exhibits back-bonding via p(π)–p(π) overlap (not p–d, as boron has no available d-orbitals in the valence shell).
Statement 1 is incorrect; statement 2 is correct (p–p π-bonding).
All three B–F bonds are equivalent and shorter than expected for single bonds (statement 3 ✓).
The B–F bond has exceptionally high strength, among the strongest single bonds (statement 4 ✓).
Hence option (b) is correct.', NULL, 'Potential candidate — human review required; no correction approved', 'Yes', '2026-10-18T11:00:20.276Z'::timestamptz, '2026-10-18T12:34:15.495Z'::timestamptz, 'https://app.ilearn-india.com/admin/questions/13584?from=bank') ON CONFLICT (qid) DO UPDATE SET "answer_key" = EXCLUDED."answer_key", "solution_key_review_result" = EXCLUDED."solution_key_review_result", "review_status" = EXCLUDED."review_status", "subject" = EXCLUDED."subject", "exam" = EXCLUDED."exam", "chapter" = EXCLUDED."chapter", "screening_batch_existing_question_ordinal" = EXCLUDED."screening_batch_existing_question_ordinal", "category" = EXCLUDED."category", "deterministic_rules" = EXCLUDED."deterministic_rules", "question_specific_finding_evidence" = EXCLUDED."question_specific_finding_evidence", "publication_status_at_screening" = EXCLUDED."publication_status_at_screening", "current_publication_status" = EXCLUDED."current_publication_status", "flag_status" = EXCLUDED."flag_status", "flag_id" = EXCLUDED."flag_id", "action_in_this_10k_run" = EXCLUDED."action_in_this_10k_run", "exam_linked" = EXCLUDED."exam_linked", "question" = EXCLUDED."question", "options" = EXCLUDED."options", "stored_explanation" = EXCLUDED."stored_explanation", "numeric_answer_policy" = EXCLUDED."numeric_answer_policy", "original_review_status_context" = EXCLUDED."original_review_status_context", "content_unchanged_since_screening" = EXCLUDED."content_unchanged_since_screening", "screened_at_utc" = EXCLUDED."screened_at_utc", "live_status_checked_at_utc" = EXCLUDED."live_status_checked_at_utc", "question_url" = EXCLUDED."question_url";
