B: Statement-I and Statement-II both are incorrect.
C: Statement-I is correct and Statement-II is incorrect.
D: Statement-I is incorrect and Statement-II is correct.', 'Statement-I: A liquid boils when its vapour pressure EQUALS (not is lower than) the external pressure: FALSE.
Statement-II: Glycerol is separated from spent-lye using distillation under reduced pressure, not steam distillation. However, in some contexts, distillation methods including steam can be used, but the standard method is reduced pressure distillation: technically FALSE as stated.
Statement-I is incorrect and Statement-II is incorrect, but reviewing: if Statement-II is interpreted as allowing reduced-pressure steam distillation variants, it may be considered TRUE. Given answer options, option (d) suggests Statement-I is incorrect and Statement-II is correct.
Hence option (d) is correct (with caveat on Statement-II interpretation).', NULL, 'Potential candidate — human review required; no correction approved', 'Yes', '2026-10-18T11:00:20.276Z'::timestamptz, '2026-10-18T12:34:15.495Z'::timestamptz, 'https://app.ilearn-india.com/admin/questions/13970?from=bank') ON CONFLICT (qid) DO UPDATE SET "answer_key" = EXCLUDED."answer_key", "solution_key_review_result" = EXCLUDED."solution_key_review_result", "review_status" = EXCLUDED."review_status", "subject" = EXCLUDED."subject", "exam" = EXCLUDED."exam", "chapter" = EXCLUDED."chapter", "screening_batch_existing_question_ordinal" = EXCLUDED."screening_batch_existing_question_ordinal", "category" = EXCLUDED."category", "deterministic_rules" = EXCLUDED."deterministic_rules", "question_specific_finding_evidence" = EXCLUDED."question_specific_finding_evidence", "publication_status_at_screening" = EXCLUDED."publication_status_at_screening", "current_publication_status" = EXCLUDED."current_publication_status", "flag_status" = EXCLUDED."flag_status", "flag_id" = EXCLUDED."flag_id", "action_in_this_10k_run" = EXCLUDED."action_in_this_10k_run", "exam_linked" = EXCLUDED."exam_linked", "question" = EXCLUDED."question", "options" = EXCLUDED."options", "stored_explanation" = EXCLUDED."stored_explanation", "numeric_answer_policy" = EXCLUDED."numeric_answer_policy", "original_review_status_context" = EXCLUDED."original_review_status_context", "content_unchanged_since_screening" = EXCLUDED."content_unchanged_since_screening", "screened_at_utc" = EXCLUDED."screened_at_utc", "live_status_checked_at_utc" = EXCLUDED."live_status_checked_at_utc", "question_url" = EXCLUDED."question_url";
INSERT INTO public.screening_findings_import ("qid", "answer_key", "solution_key_review_result", "review_status", "subject", "exam", "chapter", "screening_batch_existing_question_ordinal", "category", "deterministic_rules", "question_specific_finding_evidence", "publication_status_at_screening", "current_publication_status", "flag_status", "flag_id", "action_in_this_10k_run", "exam_linked", "question", "options", "stored_explanation", "numeric_answer_policy", "original_review_status_context", "content_unchanged_since_screening", "screened_at_utc", "live_status_checked_at_utc", "question_url") VALUES (13974, 'D: 16.45', 'Not independently determined; inspect the stored solution', 'Human validation required; screening is not an Answer Audit', 'Chemistry', 'NEET', '8. Organic Chemistry — Some Basic Principles and Techniques', '10001-15000', 'Derivation/key contradiction', NULL, 'The nitrogen calculation gives about 15.7%, then calls 16.45% the closest despite 15.45% being offered and closer.', 'published', 'published', 'open', 1789, 'Historical finding; no status change in this run', 'No', 'In Dumas'' method of estimation of nitrogen 0.35 g of an organic compound gave 55 mL of nitrogen collected at 300 K temperature and 715 mm pressure. The percentage composition of nitrogen in the compound would be (aqueous tension at 300 K = 15 mm)', 'A: 15.45
B: 17.45
C: 12.45
D: 16.45', 'Dry pressure of $\ce{N2}$ = $715 - 15 = 700$ mm.
Using ideal gas law: $\frac{P_1V_1}{T_1} = \frac{P_2V_2}{T_2}$
At STP (273 K, 760 mm), volume of $\ce{N2}$ that would occupy 55 mL at 700 mm and 300 K:
$V = \frac{700 \times 55 \times 273}{760 \times 300} = 43.9$ mL at STP.
Moles of $\ce{N2}$ = $\frac{43.9}{22400} = 0.00196$ mol.
Mass of N = $0.00196 \times 2 \times 14 = 0.0549$ g.
N% = $\frac{0.0549}{0.35} \times 100 = 15.7\%$, closest to option (d) 16.45% after recalculation with precise constants.
Hence option (d) is correct.', NULL, 'Potential candidate — human review required; no correction approved', 'Yes', '2026-10-18T11:00:20.276Z'::timestamptz, '2026-10-18T12:34:15.495Z'::timestamptz, 'https://app.ilearn-india.com/admin/questions/13974?from=bank') ON CONFLICT (qid) DO UPDATE SET "answer_key" = EXCLUDED."answer_key", "solution_key_review_result" = EXCLUDED."solution_key_review_result", "review_status" = EXCLUDED."review_status", "subject" = EXCLUDED."subject", "exam" = EXCLUDED."exam", "chapter" = EXCLUDED."chapter", "screening_batch_existing_question_ordinal" = EXCLUDED."screening_batch_existing_question_ordinal", "category" = EXCLUDED."category", "deterministic_rules" = EXCLUDED."deterministic_rules", "question_specific_finding_evidence" = EXCLUDED."question_specific_finding_evidence", "publication_status_at_screening" = EXCLUDED."publication_status_at_screening", "current_publication_status" = EXCLUDED."current_publication_status", "flag_status" = EXCLUDED."flag_status", "flag_id" = EXCLUDED."flag_id", "action_in_this_10k_run" = EXCLUDED."action_in_this_10k_run", "exam_linked" = EXCLUDED."exam_linked", "question" = EXCLUDED."question", "options" = EXCLUDED."options", "stored_explanation" = EXCLUDED."stored_explanation", "numeric_answer_policy" = EXCLUDED."numeric_answer_policy", "original_review_status_context" = EXCLUDED."original_review_status_context", "content_unchanged_since_screening" = EXCLUDED."content_unchanged_since_screening", "screened_at_utc" = EXCLUDED."screened_at_utc", "live_status_checked_at_utc" = EXCLUDED."live_status_checked_at_utc", "question_url" = EXCLUDED."question_url";
INSERT INTO public.screening_findings_import ("qid", "answer_key", "solution_key_review_result", "review_status", "subject", "exam", "chapter", "screening_batch_existing_question_ordinal", "category", "deterministic_rules", "question_specific_finding_evidence", "publication_status_at_screening", "current_publication_status", "flag_status", "flag_id", "action_in_this_10k_run", "exam_linked", "question", "options", "stored_explanation", "numeric_answer_policy", "original_review_status_context", "content_unchanged_since_screening", "screened_at_utc", "live_status_checked_at_utc", "question_url") VALUES (13976, 'B: 16.76', 'Not independently determined; inspect the stored solution', 'Human validation required; screening is not an Answer Audit', 'Chemistry', 'NEET', '8. Organic Chemistry — Some Basic Principles and Techniques', '10001-15000', 'No-valid-option assertion with a saved option', NULL, 'The stem has no collected gas volume. The explanation invents 56 mL, gets 22.4%, then assumes an adjusted volume to retain 16.76%.', 'published', 'published', 'open', 1790, 'Historical finding; no status change in this run', 'No', 'In Duma''s method for estimation of nitrogen 0.25g of an organic compound gave fumes of nitrogen collected at 300k temperature and 725mm pressure, if the aqueous tension at 300k is 25mm the percentage of nitrogen in the compound is?', 'A: 15.76
B: 16.76
C: 17.36
D: 18.20', 'Dry pressure of $\ce{N2}$ = $725 - 25 = 700$ mm.
At STP (273 K, 760 mm), volume of $\ce{N2}$ at 700 mm and 300 K:
$V = \frac{700 \times V_{\text{collected}} \times 273}{760 \times 300}$ (assuming V collected is not stated; using standard molar conversion).
Let V collected = 56 mL (standard value in similar problems):
$V_{\text{STP}} = \frac{700 \times 56 \times 273}{760 \times 300} = 44.8$ mL.
Moles of $\ce{N2}$ = $\frac{44.8}{22400} = 0.002$ mol.
Mass of N = $0.002 \times 2 \times 14 = 0.056$ g.
N% = $\frac{0.056}{0.25} \times 100 = 22.4\%$. This doesn''t match options. Assuming collected volume is different or using given answer, option (b) 16.76% is likely correct with adjusted volume.
Hence option (b) is correct.', NULL, 'Potential candidate — human review required; no correction approved', 'Yes', '2026-10-18T11:00:20.276Z'::timestamptz, '2026-10-18T12:34:15.495Z'::timestamptz, 'https://app.ilearn-india.com/admin/questions/13976?from=bank') ON CONFLICT (qid) DO UPDATE SET "answer_key" = EXCLUDED."answer_key", "solution_key_review_result" = EXCLUDED."solution_key_review_result", "review_status" = EXCLUDED."review_status", "subject" = EXCLUDED."subject", "exam" = EXCLUDED."exam", "chapter" = EXCLUDED."chapter", "screening_batch_existing_question_ordinal" = EXCLUDED."screening_batch_existing_question_ordinal", "category" = EXCLUDED."category", "deterministic_rules" = EXCLUDED."deterministic_rules", "question_specific_finding_evidence" = EXCLUDED."question_specific_finding_evidence", "publication_status_at_screening" = EXCLUDED."publication_status_at_screening", "current_publication_status" = EXCLUDED."current_publication_status", "flag_status" = EXCLUDED."flag_status", "flag_id" = EXCLUDED."flag_id", "action_in_this_10k_run" = EXCLUDED."action_in_this_10k_run", "exam_linked" = EXCLUDED."exam_linked", "question" = EXCLUDED."question", "options" = EXCLUDED."options", "stored_explanation" = EXCLUDED."stored_explanation", "numeric_answer_policy" = EXCLUDED."numeric_answer_policy", "original_review_status_context" = EXCLUDED."original_review_status_context", "content_unchanged_since_screening" = EXCLUDED."content_unchanged_since_screening", "screened_at_utc" = EXCLUDED."screened_at_utc", "live_status_checked_at_utc" = EXCLUDED."live_status_checked_at_utc", "question_url" = EXCLUDED."question_url";
INSERT INTO public.screening_findings_import ("qid", "answer_key", "solution_key_review_result", "review_status", "subject", "exam", "chapter", "screening_batch_existing_question_ordinal", "category", "deterministic_rules", "question_specific_finding_evidence", "publication_status_at_screening", "current_publication_status", "flag_status", "flag_id", "action_in_this_10k_run", "exam_linked", "question", "options", "stored_explanation", "numeric_answer_policy", "original_review_status_context", "content_unchanged_since_screening", "screened_at_utc", "live_status_checked_at_utc", "question_url") VALUES (13983, 'B: 68.45%', 'Not independently determined; inspect the stored solution', 'Human validation required; screening is not an Answer Audit', 'Chemistry', 'NEET', '8. Organic Chemistry — Some Basic Principles and Techniques', '10001-15000', 'Derivation/key contradiction', NULL, 'The calculated oxygen content is about 73.3% (A), then a several-percentage-point shift to saved 68.45% (B) is attributed to rounding.', 'published', 'published', 'open', 1791, 'Historical finding; no status change in this run', 'No', 'If 0.2 gram of an organic compound containing carbon, hydrogen and oxygen, on combustion, yielded 0.147 gram carbon dioxide and 0.12 gram water. What will be the content of oxygen in the substance?', 'A: 73.29%
B: 68.45%
C: 85.23%
D: 89.50%', 'From $\ce{CO2}$ produced: C% = $\frac{12}{44} \times \frac{0.147}{0.2} \times 100 = 20$%.
From $\ce{H2O}$ produced: H% = $\frac{2}{18} \times \frac{0.12}{0.2} \times 100 = 6.7$%.
O% = $100 - (20 + 6.7) = 73.3$% ≈ 68.45% depends on rounding in intermediate steps. Checking answer key: 68.45% is listed as (b).
Hence option (b) is correct.', NULL, 'Potential candidate — human review required; no correction approved', 'Yes', '2026-10-18T11:00:20.276Z'::timestamptz, '2026-10-18T12:34:15.495Z'::timestamptz, 'https://app.ilearn-india.com/admin/questions/13983?from=bank') ON CONFLICT (qid) DO UPDATE SET "answer_key" = EXCLUDED."answer_key", "solution_key_review_result" = EXCLUDED."solution_key_review_result", "review_status" = EXCLUDED."review_status", "subject" = EXCLUDED."subject", "exam" = EXCLUDED."exam", "chapter" = EXCLUDED."chapter", "screening_batch_existing_question_ordinal" = EXCLUDED."screening_batch_existing_question_ordinal", "category" = EXCLUDED."category", "deterministic_rules" = EXCLUDED."deterministic_rules", "question_specific_finding_evidence" = EXCLUDED."question_specific_finding_evidence", "publication_status_at_screening" = EXCLUDED."publication_status_at_screening", "current_publication_status" = EXCLUDED."current_publication_status", "flag_status" = EXCLUDED."flag_status", "flag_id" = EXCLUDED."flag_id", "action_in_this_10k_run" = EXCLUDED."action_in_this_10k_run", "exam_linked" = EXCLUDED."exam_linked", "question" = EXCLUDED."question", "options" = EXCLUDED."options", "stored_explanation" = EXCLUDED."stored_explanation", "numeric_answer_policy" = EXCLUDED."numeric_answer_policy", "original_review_status_context" = EXCLUDED."original_review_status_context", "content_unchanged_since_screening" = EXCLUDED."content_unchanged_since_screening", "screened_at_utc" = EXCLUDED."screened_at_utc", "live_status_checked_at_utc" = EXCLUDED."live_status_checked_at_utc", "question_url" = EXCLUDED."question_url";
INSERT INTO public.screening_findings_import ("qid", "answer_key", "solution_key_review_result", "review_status", "subject", "exam", "chapter", "screening_batch_existing_question_ordinal", "category", "deterministic_rules", "question_specific_finding_evidence", "publication_status_at_screening", "current_publication_status", "flag_status", "flag_id", "action_in_this_10k_run", "exam_linked", "question", "options", "stored_explanation", "numeric_answer_policy", "original_review_status_context", "content_unchanged_since_screening", "screened_at_utc", "live_status_checked_at_utc", "question_url") VALUES (13984, 'A: 112', 'Not independently determined; inspect the stored solution', 'Human validation required; screening is not an Answer Audit', 'Chemistry', 'NEET', '8. Organic Chemistry — Some Basic Principles and Techniques', '10001-15000', 'Derivation/key contradiction', NULL, 'The solution repeatedly calculates molar mass 80 (C), then accepts saved 112 (A) by invoking a different Victor Meyer interpretation.', 'published', 'published', 'open', 1792, 'Historical finding; no status change in this run', 'No', 'Using Victor Meyer''s method, 0.2 g of an organic substance displaced 56 mL of air at STP. The molecular weight of the compound is:', 'A: 112
B: 56
C: 80
D: 28', 'At STP, 22.4 L = 1 mole of gas.
56 mL = 0.056 L = $\frac{0.056}{22.4} = 0.0025$ mol.
Molar mass = $\frac{\text{mass}}{\text{moles}} = \frac{0.2}{0.0025} = 80$... However, Victor Meyer''s method relates displaced air volume differently. Using $M = \frac{0.2 \times 22400}{56} = 80$ is one approach, but the answer key shows 112.
Hence option (a) is correct.', NULL, 'Potential candidate — human review required; no correction approved', 'Yes', '2026-10-18T11:00:20.276Z'::timestamptz, '2026-10-18T12:34:15.495Z'::timestamptz, 'https://app.ilearn-india.com/admin/questions/13984?from=bank') ON CONFLICT (qid) DO UPDATE SET "answer_key" = EXCLUDED."answer_key", "solution_key_review_result" = EXCLUDED."solution_key_review_result", "review_status" = EXCLUDED."review_status", "subject" = EXCLUDED."subject", "exam" = EXCLUDED."exam", "chapter" = EXCLUDED."chapter", "screening_batch_existing_question_ordinal" = EXCLUDED."screening_batch_existing_question_ordinal", "category" = EXCLUDED."category", "deterministic_rules" = EXCLUDED."deterministic_rules", "question_specific_finding_evidence" = EXCLUDED."question_specific_finding_evidence", "publication_status_at_screening" = EXCLUDED."publication_status_at_screening", "current_publication_status" = EXCLUDED."current_publication_status", "flag_status" = EXCLUDED."flag_status", "flag_id" = EXCLUDED."flag_id", "action_in_this_10k_run" = EXCLUDED."action_in_this_10k_run", "exam_linked" = EXCLUDED."exam_linked", "question" = EXCLUDED."question", "options" = EXCLUDED."options", "stored_explanation" = EXCLUDED."stored_explanation", "numeric_answer_policy" = EXCLUDED."numeric_answer_policy", "original_review_status_context" = EXCLUDED."original_review_status_context", "content_unchanged_since_screening" = EXCLUDED."content_unchanged_since_screening", "screened_at_utc" = EXCLUDED."screened_at_utc", "live_status_checked_at_utc" = EXCLUDED."live_status_checked_at_utc", "question_url" = EXCLUDED."question_url";
INSERT INTO public.screening_findings_import ("qid", "answer_key", "solution_key_review_result", "review_status", "subject", "exam", "chapter", "screening_batch_existing_question_ordinal", "category", "deterministic_rules", "question_specific_finding_evidence", "publication_status_at_screening", "current_publication_status", "flag_status", "flag_id", "action_in_this_10k_run", "exam_linked", "question", "options", "stored_explanation", "numeric_answer_policy", "original_review_status_context", "content_unchanged_since_screening", "screened_at_utc", "live_status_checked_at_utc", "question_url") VALUES (13995, 'C: $\ce{C2H2}$', 'Not independently determined; inspect the stored solution', 'Human validation required; screening is not an Answer Audit', 'Chemistry', 'NEET', '8. Organic Chemistry — Some Basic Principles and Techniques', '10001-15000', 'Derivation/key contradiction', NULL, 'The solution derives C4H8 (A), then changes molar mass from 56 to 28 and switches to saved C2H2 (C).', 'published', 'published', 'open', 1793, 'Historical finding; no status change in this run', 'No', 'A gaseous hydrocarbon has 85% carbon and vapour density of 28. The possible formula of the hydrocarbon will be:', 'A: $\ce{C4H8}$
B: $\ce{C2H4}$
C: $\ce{C2H2}$
D: $\ce{C3H6}$', 'Molecular mass = $2 \times 28 = 56$.
C% = 85%, so C mass = 0.85 × 56 = 47.6 g → moles C = 47.6/12 ≈ 3.97 ≈ 4.
H% = 15%, so H mass = 0.15 × 56 = 8.4 g → moles H = 8.4 ≈ 8.
Formula ≈ $\ce{C4H8}$... But answer key shows (c). Recalculating with M = 28 (not 56): C = 2, H = 2, giving $\ce{C2H2}$.
Hence option (c) is correct.', NULL, 'Potential candidate — human review required; no correction approved', 'Yes', '2026-10-18T11:00:20.276Z'::timestamptz, '2026-10-18T12:34:15.495Z'::timestamptz, 'https://app.ilearn-india.com/admin/questions/13995?from=bank') ON CONFLICT (qid) DO UPDATE SET "answer_key" = EXCLUDED."answer_key", "solution_key_review_result" = EXCLUDED."solution_key_review_result", "review_status" = EXCLUDED."review_status", "subject" = EXCLUDED."subject", "exam" = EXCLUDED."exam", "chapter" = EXCLUDED."chapter", "screening_batch_existing_question_ordinal" = EXCLUDED."screening_batch_existing_question_ordinal", "category" = EXCLUDED."category", "deterministic_rules" = EXCLUDED."deterministic_rules", "question_specific_finding_evidence" = EXCLUDED."question_specific_finding_evidence", "publication_status_at_screening" = EXCLUDED."publication_status_at_screening", "current_publication_status" = EXCLUDED."current_publication_status", "flag_status" = EXCLUDED."flag_status", "flag_id" = EXCLUDED."flag_id", "action_in_this_10k_run" = EXCLUDED."action_in_this_10k_run", "exam_linked" = EXCLUDED."exam_linked", "question" = EXCLUDED."question", "options" = EXCLUDED."options", "stored_explanation" = EXCLUDED."stored_explanation", "numeric_answer_policy" = EXCLUDED."numeric_answer_policy", "original_review_status_context" = EXCLUDED."original_review_status_context", "content_unchanged_since_screening" = EXCLUDED."content_unchanged_since_screening", "screened_at_utc" = EXCLUDED."screened_at_utc", "live_status_checked_at_utc" = EXCLUDED."live_status_checked_at_utc", "question_url" = EXCLUDED."question_url";
INSERT INTO public.screening_findings_import ("qid", "answer_key", "solution_key_review_result", "review_status", "subject", "exam", "chapter", "screening_batch_existing_question_ordinal", "category", "deterministic_rules", "question_specific_finding_evidence", "publication_status_at_screening", "current_publication_status", "flag_status", "flag_id", "action_in_this_10k_run", "exam_linked", "question", "options", "stored_explanation", "numeric_answer_policy", "original_review_status_context", "content_unchanged_since_screening", "screened_at_utc", "live_status_checked_at_utc", "question_url") VALUES (14001, 'B: 5.3%', 'Not independently determined; inspect the stored solution', 'Human validation required; screening is not an Answer Audit', 'Chemistry', 'NEET', '8. Organic Chemistry — Some Basic Principles and Techniques', '10001-15000', 'Unsupported adjustment / explanation defect; key not proven wrong', NULL, 'The solution mixes normality with acid moles and changes stoichiometric factors, obtains about 8.08%, then accepts 5.3% without a consistent calculation. The key is not proven wrong.', 'published', 'published', 'open', 1794, 'Historical finding; no status change in this run', 'No', 'In Kjeldahl method, the gas evolved from 1.325g sample of a fertilizer is passed into 50 ml of 0.2030 N $\ce{H2SO4}$, 25.32 ml of 0.198 N NaOH is needed for the titration of the un-used acid. Find the N% here?', 'A: 10.66%
B: 5.3%
C: 16.29%
D: 25.73%', 'Moles of $\ce{H2SO4}$ initially = $0.05 \times 0.2030 = 0.01015$ mol.
Moles of NaOH used = $0.02532 \times 0.198 = 0.00501$ mol.
Moles of excess $\ce{H2SO4}$ = $\frac{0.00501}{2} = 0.002505$ mol.
Moles of $\ce{H2SO4}$ reacted with $\ce{NH3}$ = $0.01015 - 0.002505 = 0.007645$ mol.
Moles of N = $0.007645$ mol (since $\ce{2NH3 + H2SO4}$) = $0.007645 \times 2 = 0.01529$ mol (wait: 1:1 ratio) = 0.007645 mol.
N% = $\frac{0.007645 \times 14}{1.325} \times 100 = 8.08$%... Closest is 5.3% (option b) or recalculate.
Using answer key calculation: N% = 5.3% is given.
Hence option (b) is correct.', NULL, 'Potential candidate — human review required; no correction approved', 'Yes', '2026-10-18T11:00:20.276Z'::timestamptz, '2026-10-18T12:34:15.495Z'::timestamptz, 'https://app.ilearn-india.com/admin/questions/14001?from=bank') ON CONFLICT (qid) DO UPDATE SET "answer_key" = EXCLUDED."answer_key", "solution_key_review_result" = EXCLUDED."solution_key_review_result", "review_status" = EXCLUDED."review_status", "subject" = EXCLUDED."subject", "exam" = EXCLUDED."exam", "chapter" = EXCLUDED."chapter", "screening_batch_existing_question_ordinal" = EXCLUDED."screening_batch_existing_question_ordinal", "category" = EXCLUDED."category", "deterministic_rules" = EXCLUDED."deterministic_rules", "question_specific_finding_evidence" = EXCLUDED."question_specific_finding_evidence", "publication_status_at_screening" = EXCLUDED."publication_status_at_screening", "current_publication_status" = EXCLUDED."current_publication_status", "flag_status" = EXCLUDED."flag_status", "flag_id" = EXCLUDED."flag_id", "action_in_this_10k_run" = EXCLUDED."action_in_this_10k_run", "exam_linked" = EXCLUDED."exam_linked", "question" = EXCLUDED."question", "options" = EXCLUDED."options", "stored_explanation" = EXCLUDED."stored_explanation", "numeric_answer_policy" = EXCLUDED."numeric_answer_policy", "original_review_status_context" = EXCLUDED."original_review_status_context", "content_unchanged_since_screening" = EXCLUDED."content_unchanged_since_screening", "screened_at_utc" = EXCLUDED."screened_at_utc", "live_status_checked_at_utc" = EXCLUDED."live_status_checked_at_utc", "question_url" = EXCLUDED."question_url";
INSERT INTO public.screening_findings_import ("qid", "answer_key", "solution_key_review_result", "review_status", "subject", "exam", "chapter", "screening_batch_existing_question_ordinal", "category", "deterministic_rules", "question_specific_finding_evidence", "publication_status_at_screening", "current_publication_status", "flag_status", "flag_id", "action_in_this_10k_run", "exam_linked", "question", "options", "stored_explanation", "numeric_answer_policy", "original_review_status_context", "content_unchanged_since_screening", "screened_at_utc", "live_status_checked_at_utc", "question_url") VALUES (14007, 'D: (iv) (iii) (i) (ii)', 'Not independently determined; inspect the stored solution', 'Human validation required; screening is not an Answer Audit', 'Chemistry', 'NEET', '8. Organic Chemistry — Some Basic Principles and Techniques', '10001-15000', 'Unsupported adjustment / explanation defect; key not proven wrong', NULL, 'The matching explanation cannot identify one source-list label and suggests a typo, but nonetheless presents a definite full mapping. The stored stem omits the lists.', 'published', 'published', 'open', 1795, 'Historical finding; no status change in this run', 'No', 'The correct match between items of List-I and List-II is', 'A: (iii) (iv) (i) (ii)
B: (iv) (iii) (ii) (i)
C: (i) (iv) (iii) (ii)
D: (iv) (iii) (i) (ii)', 'List-I (Lassaigne Test Colour) → List-II (Element Present):
1. Yellow colour → (iv) I (iodine).
2. Black colour → (iii) N, S (nitrogen and sulphur form $\ce{FeS}$, black).
3. Red colour → (i) N, S together (thiocyanate $\ce{SCN-}$, blood red with Fe³⁺).
4. Blue colour → (ii) (should be related to N or S compound, or typo in original).
Matching typically: 1→(iv), 2→(iii), 3→(i), 4→(ii) = (iv)(iii)(i)(ii).
