![Four candidate aromatic structures numbered 1-4](https://pub-46f930544d71428a9520666ac871983d.r2.dev/question-assets/dd3c4265-5fa1-4897-890a-3dcd0ae5527c.webp)', 'A: 3 only
B: 1, 3
C: 3, IV (or 3, 4)
D: 1, 3, 2', 'Aromaticity requires (by Hückel''s rule): planar molecule with $4n+2$ π electrons (n = 0, 1, 2, ...).
Common aromatic examples: benzene (6 π e⁻), cyclopentadienyl anion (6 π e⁻), cycloheptatrienyl cation (6 π e⁻).
Without viewing the specific structures, aromatic compounds typically include benzene derivatives and heterocycles like pyridine.
Based on the answer key, option (b) (1, 3) is listed as correct, suggesting structures 1 and 3 satisfy aromaticity criteria.
Hence option (b) is correct.', NULL, 'Potential candidate — human review required; no correction approved', 'Yes', '2026-10-18T11:00:20.276Z'::timestamptz, '2026-10-18T12:34:15.495Z'::timestamptz, 'https://app.ilearn-india.com/admin/questions/14106?from=bank') ON CONFLICT (qid) DO UPDATE SET "answer_key" = EXCLUDED."answer_key", "solution_key_review_result" = EXCLUDED."solution_key_review_result", "review_status" = EXCLUDED."review_status", "subject" = EXCLUDED."subject", "exam" = EXCLUDED."exam", "chapter" = EXCLUDED."chapter", "screening_batch_existing_question_ordinal" = EXCLUDED."screening_batch_existing_question_ordinal", "category" = EXCLUDED."category", "deterministic_rules" = EXCLUDED."deterministic_rules", "question_specific_finding_evidence" = EXCLUDED."question_specific_finding_evidence", "publication_status_at_screening" = EXCLUDED."publication_status_at_screening", "current_publication_status" = EXCLUDED."current_publication_status", "flag_status" = EXCLUDED."flag_status", "flag_id" = EXCLUDED."flag_id", "action_in_this_10k_run" = EXCLUDED."action_in_this_10k_run", "exam_linked" = EXCLUDED."exam_linked", "question" = EXCLUDED."question", "options" = EXCLUDED."options", "stored_explanation" = EXCLUDED."stored_explanation", "numeric_answer_policy" = EXCLUDED."numeric_answer_policy", "original_review_status_context" = EXCLUDED."original_review_status_context", "content_unchanged_since_screening" = EXCLUDED."content_unchanged_since_screening", "screened_at_utc" = EXCLUDED."screened_at_utc", "live_status_checked_at_utc" = EXCLUDED."live_status_checked_at_utc", "question_url" = EXCLUDED."question_url";
INSERT INTO public.screening_findings_import ("qid", "answer_key", "solution_key_review_result", "review_status", "subject", "exam", "chapter", "screening_batch_existing_question_ordinal", "category", "deterministic_rules", "question_specific_finding_evidence", "publication_status_at_screening", "current_publication_status", "flag_status", "flag_id", "action_in_this_10k_run", "exam_linked", "question", "options", "stored_explanation", "numeric_answer_policy", "original_review_status_context", "content_unchanged_since_screening", "screened_at_utc", "live_status_checked_at_utc", "question_url") VALUES (14117, 'D: ![287](https://pub-46f930544d71428a9520666ac871983d.r2.dev/question-assets/98740e95-c1b7-46ab-a977-787bff1aa56e.webp)', 'Not independently determined; inspect the stored solution', 'Human validation required; screening is not an Answer Audit', 'Chemistry', 'NEET', '8. Organic Chemistry — Some Basic Principles and Techniques', '10001-15000', 'Unsupported adjustment / explanation defect; key not proven wrong', NULL, 'The solution invents alternative phenolic-OH replacement/ring bromination pathways and finally picks D because the key lists it. Review the actual reaction and product images.', 'published', 'published', 'open', 1808, 'Historical finding; no status change in this run', 'No', 'The reaction of:

![283](https://pub-46f930544d71428a9520666ac871983d.r2.dev/question-assets/935c31e1-e896-4526-b5d8-82933d789d48.webp)

with HBr gives:', 'A: ![284](https://pub-46f930544d71428a9520666ac871983d.r2.dev/question-assets/88b5e910-6165-4ee2-b9ae-c7501d38e81b.webp)
B: ![285](https://pub-46f930544d71428a9520666ac871983d.r2.dev/question-assets/415d65bc-c38a-4fc0-b705-5cf8aea972fd.webp)
C: ![286](https://pub-46f930544d71428a9520666ac871983d.r2.dev/question-assets/eb8721ac-2952-4c9f-9546-e6b660c33aac.webp)
D: ![287](https://pub-46f930544d71428a9520666ac871983d.r2.dev/question-assets/98740e95-c1b7-46ab-a977-787bff1aa56e.webp)', 'The compound is a phenolic alkene (a vinyl phenol, where the phenol ring is denoted by the circle/benzene symbol with OH attached).
Reaction with HBr: the alkene reacts with HBr via Markovnikov''s rule.
H adds to the less substituted carbon of the double bond (the carbon not bearing the phenyl group), and Br adds to the more substituted carbon (the one closer to the aromatic ring).
Also, the hydroxyl group on the aromatic ring activates the ring and can participate in rearrangement or further reactions, but the primary reaction is electrophilic addition to the C=C double bond.
Product: $\ce{CH3-CH2-CHBr-()-OH}$ if the OH remains on the ring (most likely), or $\ce{CH3-CH2-CHBr-()-Br}$ if a rearrangement occurs involving the aromatic OH.
Based on typical reactivity and the answer key, option (d) ($\ce{CH3-CH2-CHBr-()-Br}$) suggests the hydroxyl group is replaced or the aromatic ring is involved in the mechanism, leading to a dibromination.
Alternatively, if the OH is para/ortho-directing and the reaction involves the ring, bromination at the ring occurs as well.
Based on standard chemistry, option (b) or (d) is most likely; the answer key lists option (d) as correct, suggesting ring involvement or rearrangement.
