B: $F = \frac{6\pi\eta r}{v}$
C: $F = 6\pi\eta\sigma r$
D: $F = \frac{6\pi\eta}{vr}$', 'By dimensional analysis, viscous force $F$ must depend on $\eta$, $r$, and $v$.
Let $F = k\eta^a r^b v^c$ where $k = 6\pi$ (dimensionless constant).
Dimensions: $[MLT^{-2}] = [ML^{-1}T^{-1}]^a [L]^b [LT^{-1}]^c$.
Matching powers: $M$: $a = 1$; $L$: $-a + b + c = 1$; $T$: $-a - c = -2$.
