B: $1$
C: $-1$
D: $2$', 'Angular momentum is conserved when $\frac{d\vec{L}}{dt} = \vec{\tau} = 0$, meaning $\vec{r} \times \vec{F} = \vec{0}$.
This requires $\vec{F}$ parallel to $\vec{r}$: $\vec{F} = \lambda \vec{r}$ for some scalar $\lambda$.
$(a\vec{i}+3\vec{j}+6\vec{k}) = \lambda(2\vec{i}-6\vec{j}-12\vec{k})$.
From the $\vec{j}$ and $\vec{k}$ components: $3 = -6\lambda$ and $6 = -12\lambda$, both giving $\lambda = -\frac{1}{2}$.
