Screening trigger: Broad lexical screen matched: closest
Prior contextual-review reason: The small -86.5 versus -86.3 difference follows 273.15 versus 273 Kelvin reference conventions; saved C is the legitimate nearest value.
Validate the current key and retained explanation; preserve correct answers, normal approximations and resolved self-corrections.', 'published', 'published', 'open', 2323, 'Historical finding; no status change in this run', 'Yes', 'On a temperature scale Y, water freezes at $-160°$ Y and boils at $-50°$ Y. On this Y scale, a temperature of 340 K would be read as', 'A: -106.3°Y
B: -96.3°Y
C: -86.3°Y
D: -76.3°Y', 'On Y scale: ice point = $-160°$ Y, steam point = $-50°$ Y, range = 110°.
In Kelvin: ice = 273.15 K, steam = 373.15 K, range = 100 K.
