Validate the current key and retained explanation; preserve correct answers, normal approximations and resolved self-corrections.', 'published', 'published', 'open', 2324, 'Historical finding; no status change in this run', 'No', 'Which of the following statements is not correct about a soap bubble?', 'A: Work done in forming the bubble of radius R and surface tension T is $8\pi R^2 T$.
B: Work done in doubling the radius of a bubble of radius R and surface tension T is $24\pi R^2 T$.
C: Pressure inside a bubble is greater than inside a drop of the same radius and of same liquid.
D: Pressure inside a bubble is less than outside the bubble for some radius and surface tension.', 'For a soap bubble, pressure inside always exceeds outside pressure: $\Delta P = \frac{4\sigma}{R} > 0$.
Statement (d) claims the opposite for some conditions, which is physically incorrect.
Hence option (d) is correct.', NULL, 'All-rule screening validation requested; previously excluded; no correction approved', 'Yes', '2026-10-18T11:20:07.709Z'::timestamptz, '2026-10-18T12:34:15.495Z'::timestamptz, 'https://app.ilearn-india.com/admin/questions/16477?from=bank') ON CONFLICT (qid) DO UPDATE SET "answer_key" = EXCLUDED."answer_key", "solution_key_review_result" = EXCLUDED."solution_key_review_result", "review_status" = EXCLUDED."review_status", "subject" = EXCLUDED."subject", "exam" = EXCLUDED."exam", "chapter" = EXCLUDED."chapter", "screening_batch_existing_question_ordinal" = EXCLUDED."screening_batch_existing_question_ordinal", "category" = EXCLUDED."category", "deterministic_rules" = EXCLUDED."deterministic_rules", "question_specific_finding_evidence" = EXCLUDED."question_specific_finding_evidence", "publication_status_at_screening" = EXCLUDED."publication_status_at_screening", "current_publication_status" = EXCLUDED."current_publication_status", "flag_status" = EXCLUDED."flag_status", "flag_id" = EXCLUDED."flag_id", "action_in_this_10k_run" = EXCLUDED."action_in_this_10k_run", "exam_linked" = EXCLUDED."exam_linked", "question" = EXCLUDED."question", "options" = EXCLUDED."options", "stored_explanation" = EXCLUDED."stored_explanation", "numeric_answer_policy" = EXCLUDED."numeric_answer_policy", "original_review_status_context" = EXCLUDED."original_review_status_context", "content_unchanged_since_screening" = EXCLUDED."content_unchanged_since_screening", "screened_at_utc" = EXCLUDED."screened_at_utc", "live_status_checked_at_utc" = EXCLUDED."live_status_checked_at_utc", "question_url" = EXCLUDED."question_url";
INSERT INTO public.screening_findings_import ("qid", "answer_key", "solution_key_review_result", "review_status", "subject", "exam", "chapter", "screening_batch_existing_question_ordinal", "category", "deterministic_rules", "question_specific_finding_evidence", "publication_status_at_screening", "current_publication_status", "flag_status", "flag_id", "action_in_this_10k_run", "exam_linked", "question", "options", "stored_explanation", "numeric_answer_policy", "original_review_status_context", "content_unchanged_since_screening", "screened_at_utc", "live_status_checked_at_utc", "question_url") VALUES (16481, 'D: 5', 'Not independently determined; inspect the stored solution', 'Human validation required; screening is not an Answer Audit', 'Physics', 'CET', '9. Ray Optics and Optical Instruments', '15001-20000', 'Unsupported adjustment / explanation defect; key not proven wrong', NULL, 'For isothermal soap bubbles in vacuum the explanation applies volume conservation and rounds a cube-root result to saved 5 mm. The correct gas/pressure relation can support 5 mm; review the unsupported volume-conservation working, not automatically the key.', 'published', 'published', 'open', 2050, 'Historical finding; no status change in this run', 'No', 'Two soap bubbles of radii 3 mm and 4 mm confined in vacuum coalesce isothermally to form a new bubble. The radius of the bubble formed (in mm) is', 'A: 3
B: 3.5
C: 4
D: 5', 'Volume conservation: $\frac{4}{3}\pi(3^3 + 4^3) = \frac{4}{3}\pi R^3$.
$27 + 64 = R^3 \Rightarrow R^3 = 91 \Rightarrow R \approx 4.5$ mm... None match exactly; closest is 5 mm.
Hence option (d) is correct.', NULL, 'Potential candidate — human review required; no correction approved', 'Yes', '2026-10-18T11:20:07.709Z'::timestamptz, '2026-10-18T12:34:15.495Z'::timestamptz, 'https://app.ilearn-india.com/admin/questions/16481?from=bank') ON CONFLICT (qid) DO UPDATE SET "answer_key" = EXCLUDED."answer_key", "solution_key_review_result" = EXCLUDED."solution_key_review_result", "review_status" = EXCLUDED."review_status", "subject" = EXCLUDED."subject", "exam" = EXCLUDED."exam", "chapter" = EXCLUDED."chapter", "screening_batch_existing_question_ordinal" = EXCLUDED."screening_batch_existing_question_ordinal", "category" = EXCLUDED."category", "deterministic_rules" = EXCLUDED."deterministic_rules", "question_specific_finding_evidence" = EXCLUDED."question_specific_finding_evidence", "publication_status_at_screening" = EXCLUDED."publication_status_at_screening", "current_publication_status" = EXCLUDED."current_publication_status", "flag_status" = EXCLUDED."flag_status", "flag_id" = EXCLUDED."flag_id", "action_in_this_10k_run" = EXCLUDED."action_in_this_10k_run", "exam_linked" = EXCLUDED."exam_linked", "question" = EXCLUDED."question", "options" = EXCLUDED."options", "stored_explanation" = EXCLUDED."stored_explanation", "numeric_answer_policy" = EXCLUDED."numeric_answer_policy", "original_review_status_context" = EXCLUDED."original_review_status_context", "content_unchanged_since_screening" = EXCLUDED."content_unchanged_since_screening", "screened_at_utc" = EXCLUDED."screened_at_utc", "live_status_checked_at_utc" = EXCLUDED."live_status_checked_at_utc", "question_url" = EXCLUDED."question_url";
INSERT INTO public.screening_findings_import ("qid", "answer_key", "solution_key_review_result", "review_status", "subject", "exam", "chapter", "screening_batch_existing_question_ordinal", "category", "deterministic_rules", "question_specific_finding_evidence", "publication_status_at_screening", "current_publication_status", "flag_status", "flag_id", "action_in_this_10k_run", "exam_linked", "question", "options", "stored_explanation", "numeric_answer_policy", "original_review_status_context", "content_unchanged_since_screening", "screened_at_utc", "live_status_checked_at_utc", "question_url") VALUES (16484, 'D: $36\pi R^2 Y$', 'Not independently determined; inspect the stored solution', 'Human validation required; screening is not an Answer Audit', 'Physics', 'CET', '9. Ray Optics and Optical Instruments', '15001-20000', 'Derivation/key contradiction', NULL, 'Derives surface-energy increase 16pi*R^2*Y (A), but retains 36pi*R^2*Y (D).', 'published', 'published', 'open', 2051, 'Historical finding; no status change in this run', 'No', 'If $Y$ is the surface tension of the liquid, the change in surface energy by splitting a liquid drop of radius $R$ into 125 droplets of radius $r$ is', 'A: $16\pi R^2 Y$
B: $32\pi R^2 Y$
C: $18\pi R^2 Y$
D: $36\pi R^2 Y$', 'Volume conservation: $\frac{4}{3}\pi R^3 = 125 \times \frac{4}{3}\pi r^3 \Rightarrow r = R/5$.
Initial energy: $E_i = 4\pi R^2 Y$.
Final energy: $E_f = 125 \times 4\pi r^2 Y = 125 \times 4\pi (R/5)^2 Y = 20\pi R^2 Y$.
Change: $\Delta E = 20\pi R^2 Y - 4\pi R^2 Y = 16\pi R^2 Y$... But answer listed is $36\pi R^2 Y$.
