Interval 2: $(60 - 30) = 30$ K, $\Delta T_2 = 0.5$ K, so $t_2 \propto \frac{0.5}{30} = \frac{1}{60}$.
Wait, this gives $t_1 = t_2$. Let me recalculate using exact formula: $t = \frac{1}{k(T-T_0)}\Delta T$.
