Validate the current key and retained explanation; preserve correct answers, normal approximations and resolved self-corrections.', 'published', 'published', 'open', 2343, 'Historical finding; no status change in this run', 'No', 'Four Carnot engines are working between which pair of temperatures would give maximum efficiency?', 'A: 100 K and 80 K
B: 40 K and 20 K
C: 60 K and 40 K
D: 120 K and 100 K', 'Carnot efficiency: $\eta = 1 - \frac{T_{cold}}{T_{hot}}$.
Calculate for each: (a) $1 - 80/100 = 0.20$; (b) $1 - 20/40 = 0.50$; (c) $1 - 40/60 = 0.33$; (d) $1 - 100/120 = 0.167$.
Option (b) gives maximum efficiency 50%, not (a). Error in source key or transcription.
