Validate the current key and retained explanation; preserve correct answers, normal approximations and resolved self-corrections.', 'published', 'published', 'open', 2349, 'Historical finding; no status change in this run', 'No', 'The pressure $P$ and $V$ of an ideal gas both increase in a process. Which of the following statements are correct?
(i) Such a process is not possible
(ii) The work done by the system is positive
(iii) The temperature of the system must increase
