D: Dipole moment is a scalar quantity and has magnitude equal to the potential energy of the system of charges.', 'Dipole moment is a vector quantity (not scalar), directed from negative to positive charge. Its magnitude equals $q \times d$ (charge times separation), not potential energy. Options (a), (b), and (c) are correct; option (d) is false on two counts.
Hence option (d) is correct.', NULL, 'All-rule screening validation requested; previously excluded; no correction approved', 'Yes', '2026-10-18T11:20:07.709Z'::timestamptz, '2026-10-18T12:34:15.495Z'::timestamptz, 'https://app.ilearn-india.com/admin/questions/17909?from=bank') ON CONFLICT (qid) DO UPDATE SET "answer_key" = EXCLUDED."answer_key", "solution_key_review_result" = EXCLUDED."solution_key_review_result", "review_status" = EXCLUDED."review_status", "subject" = EXCLUDED."subject", "exam" = EXCLUDED."exam", "chapter" = EXCLUDED."chapter", "screening_batch_existing_question_ordinal" = EXCLUDED."screening_batch_existing_question_ordinal", "category" = EXCLUDED."category", "deterministic_rules" = EXCLUDED."deterministic_rules", "question_specific_finding_evidence" = EXCLUDED."question_specific_finding_evidence", "publication_status_at_screening" = EXCLUDED."publication_status_at_screening", "current_publication_status" = EXCLUDED."current_publication_status", "flag_status" = EXCLUDED."flag_status", "flag_id" = EXCLUDED."flag_id", "action_in_this_10k_run" = EXCLUDED."action_in_this_10k_run", "exam_linked" = EXCLUDED."exam_linked", "question" = EXCLUDED."question", "options" = EXCLUDED."options", "stored_explanation" = EXCLUDED."stored_explanation", "numeric_answer_policy" = EXCLUDED."numeric_answer_policy", "original_review_status_context" = EXCLUDED."original_review_status_context", "content_unchanged_since_screening" = EXCLUDED."content_unchanged_since_screening", "screened_at_utc" = EXCLUDED."screened_at_utc", "live_status_checked_at_utc" = EXCLUDED."live_status_checked_at_utc", "question_url" = EXCLUDED."question_url";
INSERT INTO public.screening_findings_import ("qid", "answer_key", "solution_key_review_result", "review_status", "subject", "exam", "chapter", "screening_batch_existing_question_ordinal", "category", "deterministic_rules", "question_specific_finding_evidence", "publication_status_at_screening", "current_publication_status", "flag_status", "flag_id", "action_in_this_10k_run", "exam_linked", "question", "options", "stored_explanation", "numeric_answer_policy", "original_review_status_context", "content_unchanged_since_screening", "screened_at_utc", "live_status_checked_at_utc", "question_url") VALUES (17925, 'B: $\sigma_1 = \frac{5}{2}\sigma, \sigma_2 = \frac{5}{6}\sigma$', 'Not independently determined; inspect the stored solution', 'Human validation required; screening is not an Answer Audit', 'Physics', 'CET', '1. Electric Charges and Fields', '15001-20000', 'Derivation/key contradiction', NULL, 'After correcting the charge-distribution method, derives surface densities 5sigma/3 and 5sigma/6 (D), then retains B with 5sigma/2 for the first sphere.', 'published', 'published', 'open', 2141, 'Historical finding; no status change in this run', 'Yes', 'Two metal spheres, one of radius $R$ and the other of radius $2R$ respectively have the same surface charge density $\sigma$. They are brought in contact and separated. What will be the new surface charge densities on them?', 'A: $\sigma_1 = \frac{5}{6}\sigma, \sigma_2 = \frac{5}{2}\sigma$
B: $\sigma_1 = \frac{5}{2}\sigma, \sigma_2 = \frac{5}{6}\sigma$
C: $\sigma_1 = \frac{5}{2}\sigma, \sigma_2 = \frac{5}{3}\sigma$
D: $\sigma_1 = \frac{5}{3}\sigma, \sigma_2 = \frac{5}{6}\sigma$', 'Initial charge on sphere 1: $Q_1 = \sigma \cdot 4\pi R^2$. Initial charge on sphere 2: $Q_2 = \sigma \cdot 4\pi (2R)^2 = 16\pi\sigma R^2$. Total charge $Q_{total} = 4\pi\sigma R^2 + 16\pi\sigma R^2 = 20\pi\sigma R^2$. After contact, both reach same potential, so charge distributes by surface area: $Q_1'' = \frac{4\pi R^2}{4\pi R^2 + 16\pi R^2} \times 20\pi\sigma R^2 = \frac{4}{20} \times 20\pi\sigma R^2 = 4\pi\sigma R^2$. So $\sigma_1'' = \frac{4\pi\sigma R^2}{4\pi R^2} = \sigma$. Wait, re-calculate: $Q_1'' = \frac{1}{5} Q_{total} = 4\pi\sigma R^2$, giving $\sigma_1'' = \sigma$... Let me use correct approach: final charges are such that potentials are equal. $V = kQ/R$, so $\frac{Q_1''}{R} = \frac{Q_2''}{2R}$, giving $Q_2'' = 2Q_1''$. Also $Q_1'' + Q_2'' = 20\pi\sigma R^2$. Solving: $Q_1'' = \frac{20\pi\sigma R^2}{3}$, thus $\sigma_1'' = \frac{5}{3}\sigma$. And $Q_2'' = \frac{40\pi\sigma R^2}{3}$, thus $\sigma_2'' = \frac{40\pi\sigma R^2 / 3}{16\pi R^2} = \frac{5}{6}\sigma$... Discrepancy. Re-examine the source answer key.
Hence option (b) is correct.', NULL, 'Potential candidate — human review required; no correction approved', 'Yes', '2026-10-18T11:20:07.709Z'::timestamptz, '2026-10-18T12:34:15.495Z'::timestamptz, 'https://app.ilearn-india.com/admin/questions/17925?from=bank') ON CONFLICT (qid) DO UPDATE SET "answer_key" = EXCLUDED."answer_key", "solution_key_review_result" = EXCLUDED."solution_key_review_result", "review_status" = EXCLUDED."review_status", "subject" = EXCLUDED."subject", "exam" = EXCLUDED."exam", "chapter" = EXCLUDED."chapter", "screening_batch_existing_question_ordinal" = EXCLUDED."screening_batch_existing_question_ordinal", "category" = EXCLUDED."category", "deterministic_rules" = EXCLUDED."deterministic_rules", "question_specific_finding_evidence" = EXCLUDED."question_specific_finding_evidence", "publication_status_at_screening" = EXCLUDED."publication_status_at_screening", "current_publication_status" = EXCLUDED."current_publication_status", "flag_status" = EXCLUDED."flag_status", "flag_id" = EXCLUDED."flag_id", "action_in_this_10k_run" = EXCLUDED."action_in_this_10k_run", "exam_linked" = EXCLUDED."exam_linked", "question" = EXCLUDED."question", "options" = EXCLUDED."options", "stored_explanation" = EXCLUDED."stored_explanation", "numeric_answer_policy" = EXCLUDED."numeric_answer_policy", "original_review_status_context" = EXCLUDED."original_review_status_context", "content_unchanged_since_screening" = EXCLUDED."content_unchanged_since_screening", "screened_at_utc" = EXCLUDED."screened_at_utc", "live_status_checked_at_utc" = EXCLUDED."live_status_checked_at_utc", "question_url" = EXCLUDED."question_url";
INSERT INTO public.screening_findings_import ("qid", "answer_key", "solution_key_review_result", "review_status", "subject", "exam", "chapter", "screening_batch_existing_question_ordinal", "category", "deterministic_rules", "question_specific_finding_evidence", "publication_status_at_screening", "current_publication_status", "flag_status", "flag_id", "action_in_this_10k_run", "exam_linked", "question", "options", "stored_explanation", "numeric_answer_policy", "original_review_status_context", "content_unchanged_since_screening", "screened_at_utc", "live_status_checked_at_utc", "question_url") VALUES (17926, 'A: $\frac{\lambda}{2\sqrt{2}\pi\varepsilon_0 R}$', 'Not independently determined; inspect the stored solution', 'Human validation required; screening is not an Answer Audit', 'Physics', 'CET', '1. Electric Charges and Fields', '15001-20000', 'Unsupported adjustment / explanation defect; key not proven wrong', NULL, 'The explanation assumes a perpendicular distance and then an unspecified 45-degree factor to accept A, without establishing either from the actual figure. Verify source geometry; no independently proven alternative key is asserted.', 'published', 'published', 'open', 2142, 'Historical finding; no status change in this run', 'No', 'The electric field intensity at a point P due to long uniformly charged wire as shown in figure (charge per unit length is $\lambda$)

![109](https://pub-46f930544d71428a9520666ac871983d.r2.dev/question-assets/7cf4a4ff-5026-473c-a85d-fc88d70dbf23.webp)', 'A: $\frac{\lambda}{2\sqrt{2}\pi\varepsilon_0 R}$
B: $\frac{\lambda}{\sqrt{2}\pi\varepsilon_0 R}$
C: $\frac{2\lambda}{\sqrt{2}\pi\varepsilon_0 R}$
D: $\frac{\lambda}{4\sqrt{2}\pi\varepsilon_0 R}$', 'For a long straight wire, the field at perpendicular distance $r$ is $E = \frac{\lambda}{2\pi\varepsilon_0 r}$. If the point P is at perpendicular distance $R$ from the wire, then $E = \frac{\lambda}{2\pi\varepsilon_0 R}$. If there is a geometric factor (e.g., point not directly perpendicular, or wire at an angle), the expression may differ. Given options include factors of $\sqrt{2}$ suggesting a 45° geometry. If P is at 45° angle from the wire''s closest approach, the effective distance includes such factors.
Hence option (a) is correct.', NULL, 'Potential candidate — human review required; no correction approved', 'Yes', '2026-10-18T11:20:07.709Z'::timestamptz, '2026-10-18T12:34:15.495Z'::timestamptz, 'https://app.ilearn-india.com/admin/questions/17926?from=bank') ON CONFLICT (qid) DO UPDATE SET "answer_key" = EXCLUDED."answer_key", "solution_key_review_result" = EXCLUDED."solution_key_review_result", "review_status" = EXCLUDED."review_status", "subject" = EXCLUDED."subject", "exam" = EXCLUDED."exam", "chapter" = EXCLUDED."chapter", "screening_batch_existing_question_ordinal" = EXCLUDED."screening_batch_existing_question_ordinal", "category" = EXCLUDED."category", "deterministic_rules" = EXCLUDED."deterministic_rules", "question_specific_finding_evidence" = EXCLUDED."question_specific_finding_evidence", "publication_status_at_screening" = EXCLUDED."publication_status_at_screening", "current_publication_status" = EXCLUDED."current_publication_status", "flag_status" = EXCLUDED."flag_status", "flag_id" = EXCLUDED."flag_id", "action_in_this_10k_run" = EXCLUDED."action_in_this_10k_run", "exam_linked" = EXCLUDED."exam_linked", "question" = EXCLUDED."question", "options" = EXCLUDED."options", "stored_explanation" = EXCLUDED."stored_explanation", "numeric_answer_policy" = EXCLUDED."numeric_answer_policy", "original_review_status_context" = EXCLUDED."original_review_status_context", "content_unchanged_since_screening" = EXCLUDED."content_unchanged_since_screening", "screened_at_utc" = EXCLUDED."screened_at_utc", "live_status_checked_at_utc" = EXCLUDED."live_status_checked_at_utc", "question_url" = EXCLUDED."question_url";
INSERT INTO public.screening_findings_import ("qid", "answer_key", "solution_key_review_result", "review_status", "subject", "exam", "chapter", "screening_batch_existing_question_ordinal", "category", "deterministic_rules", "question_specific_finding_evidence", "publication_status_at_screening", "current_publication_status", "flag_status", "flag_id", "action_in_this_10k_run", "exam_linked", "question", "options", "stored_explanation", "numeric_answer_policy", "original_review_status_context", "content_unchanged_since_screening", "screened_at_utc", "live_status_checked_at_utc", "question_url") VALUES (17969, 'B: 66.6%', 'Not independently determined; inspect the stored solution', 'Human validation required; screening is not an Answer Audit', 'Physics', 'CET', '2. Electrostatic Potential and Capacitance', '15001-20000', 'Unsupported adjustment / explanation defect; key not proven wrong', NULL, 'The explanation assumes half-area parallel capacitors and derives 200 percent (D), but retains 66.6 percent (B) by invoking a different geometry. A half-thickness series geometry can support B; resolve the source geometry and explanation, not automatically the key.', 'published', 'published', 'open', 2143, 'Historical finding; no status change in this run', 'No', 'A parallel plate air capacitor has a capacitance C. When it is half filled along the length (with one plate) with a dielectric of dielectric constant 5, the percentage increase in the capacitance will be', 'A: 400%
B: 66.6%
C: 33.3%
D: 200%', 'When half the area is filled with dielectric (constant 5) and half remains air, we have two capacitors in parallel.
$C_{new} = \frac{A}{2} \cdot \frac{\epsilon_0 \cdot 5}{d} + \frac{A}{2} \cdot \frac{\epsilon_0}{d} = \frac{5C}{2} + \frac{C}{2} = 3C$.
Percentage increase: $\frac{3C - C}{C} \times 100 = 200$%, but answer key shows 66.6%. Let me reconsider: if only part of one plate region is filled, then $C_{new} = \frac{5C + C}{2} = 3C$, giving 200% increase. The answer key says (b) 66.6%, which corresponds to $C_{new} = 1.667C$, suggesting $\frac{C_{new}}{C} = \frac{5}{3}$, a different geometry.
Hence option (b) is correct per answer key.', NULL, 'Potential candidate — human review required; no correction approved', 'Yes', '2026-10-18T11:20:07.709Z'::timestamptz, '2026-10-18T12:34:15.495Z'::timestamptz, 'https://app.ilearn-india.com/admin/questions/17969?from=bank') ON CONFLICT (qid) DO UPDATE SET "answer_key" = EXCLUDED."answer_key", "solution_key_review_result" = EXCLUDED."solution_key_review_result", "review_status" = EXCLUDED."review_status", "subject" = EXCLUDED."subject", "exam" = EXCLUDED."exam", "chapter" = EXCLUDED."chapter", "screening_batch_existing_question_ordinal" = EXCLUDED."screening_batch_existing_question_ordinal", "category" = EXCLUDED."category", "deterministic_rules" = EXCLUDED."deterministic_rules", "question_specific_finding_evidence" = EXCLUDED."question_specific_finding_evidence", "publication_status_at_screening" = EXCLUDED."publication_status_at_screening", "current_publication_status" = EXCLUDED."current_publication_status", "flag_status" = EXCLUDED."flag_status", "flag_id" = EXCLUDED."flag_id", "action_in_this_10k_run" = EXCLUDED."action_in_this_10k_run", "exam_linked" = EXCLUDED."exam_linked", "question" = EXCLUDED."question", "options" = EXCLUDED."options", "stored_explanation" = EXCLUDED."stored_explanation", "numeric_answer_policy" = EXCLUDED."numeric_answer_policy", "original_review_status_context" = EXCLUDED."original_review_status_context", "content_unchanged_since_screening" = EXCLUDED."content_unchanged_since_screening", "screened_at_utc" = EXCLUDED."screened_at_utc", "live_status_checked_at_utc" = EXCLUDED."live_status_checked_at_utc", "question_url" = EXCLUDED."question_url";
INSERT INTO public.screening_findings_import ("qid", "answer_key", "solution_key_review_result", "review_status", "subject", "exam", "chapter", "screening_batch_existing_question_ordinal", "category", "deterministic_rules", "question_specific_finding_evidence", "publication_status_at_screening", "current_publication_status", "flag_status", "flag_id", "action_in_this_10k_run", "exam_linked", "question", "options", "stored_explanation", "numeric_answer_policy", "original_review_status_context", "content_unchanged_since_screening", "screened_at_utc", "live_status_checked_at_utc", "question_url") VALUES (17979, 'A: 5 J', 'Not independently determined; inspect the stored solution', 'Human validation required; screening is not an Answer Audit', 'Physics', 'CET', '2. Electrostatic Potential and Capacitance', '15001-20000', 'Derivation/key contradiction', 'derived_option', 'Both capacitor-energy calculations give 10 J (B), but saved A is 5 J.', 'published', 'published', 'open', 1909, 'Historical finding; no status change in this run', 'No', 'A capacitor is charged through a potential difference of 200 V, when 0.1 C charge is stored in it. The amount of energy released by it, when it is discharged is', 'A: 5 J
B: 10 J
C: 20 J
D: 2.5 J', 'Energy stored in a capacitor is $U = \frac{1}{2}QV = \frac{1}{2} \times 0.1 \times 200 = 10$ J.
Wait, that gives 10 J, not 5 J. Let me recalculate: $U = \frac{1}{2} \times 0.1 \times 200 = 10$ J. But answer key says (a) 5 J. Using $U = \frac{Q^2}{2C}$ or $U = \frac{1}{2}CV^2$: $C = Q/V = 0.1/200 = 5 \times 10^{-4}$ F = 0.5 mF, then $U = \frac{1}{2} \times 0.5 \times 10^{-3} \times (200)^2 = 10$ J.
The answer key states (a) 5 J; there may be an error in the problem or key. Following the key anyway.
Hence option (a) is correct per answer key.', NULL, 'Potential candidate — human review required; no correction approved', 'Yes', '2026-10-18T11:20:07.709Z'::timestamptz, '2026-10-18T12:34:15.495Z'::timestamptz, 'https://app.ilearn-india.com/admin/questions/17979?from=bank') ON CONFLICT (qid) DO UPDATE SET "answer_key" = EXCLUDED."answer_key", "solution_key_review_result" = EXCLUDED."solution_key_review_result", "review_status" = EXCLUDED."review_status", "subject" = EXCLUDED."subject", "exam" = EXCLUDED."exam", "chapter" = EXCLUDED."chapter", "screening_batch_existing_question_ordinal" = EXCLUDED."screening_batch_existing_question_ordinal", "category" = EXCLUDED."category", "deterministic_rules" = EXCLUDED."deterministic_rules", "question_specific_finding_evidence" = EXCLUDED."question_specific_finding_evidence", "publication_status_at_screening" = EXCLUDED."publication_status_at_screening", "current_publication_status" = EXCLUDED."current_publication_status", "flag_status" = EXCLUDED."flag_status", "flag_id" = EXCLUDED."flag_id", "action_in_this_10k_run" = EXCLUDED."action_in_this_10k_run", "exam_linked" = EXCLUDED."exam_linked", "question" = EXCLUDED."question", "options" = EXCLUDED."options", "stored_explanation" = EXCLUDED."stored_explanation", "numeric_answer_policy" = EXCLUDED."numeric_answer_policy", "original_review_status_context" = EXCLUDED."original_review_status_context", "content_unchanged_since_screening" = EXCLUDED."content_unchanged_since_screening", "screened_at_utc" = EXCLUDED."screened_at_utc", "live_status_checked_at_utc" = EXCLUDED."live_status_checked_at_utc", "question_url" = EXCLUDED."question_url";
INSERT INTO public.screening_findings_import ("qid", "answer_key", "solution_key_review_result", "review_status", "subject", "exam", "chapter", "screening_batch_existing_question_ordinal", "category", "deterministic_rules", "question_specific_finding_evidence", "publication_status_at_screening", "current_publication_status", "flag_status", "flag_id", "action_in_this_10k_run", "exam_linked", "question", "options", "stored_explanation", "numeric_answer_policy", "original_review_status_context", "content_unchanged_since_screening", "screened_at_utc", "live_status_checked_at_utc", "question_url") VALUES (17984, 'A: $10 \times 10^5 \text{ V}$', 'Not independently determined; inspect the stored solution', 'Human validation required; screening is not an Answer Audit', 'Physics', 'CET', '2. Electrostatic Potential and Capacitance', '15001-20000', 'Derivation/key contradiction', NULL, 'Derives potential 15000 V, absent from the choices, while saved A is 1e6 V; attempted power-of-ten reinterpretations do not reconcile the difference.', 'published', 'published', 'open', 2144, 'Historical finding; no status change in this run', 'No', 'The work done in bringing a 2 mC charge from infinity to a point is 30 J. Find the potential at that point.', 'A: $10 \times 10^5 \text{ V}$
B: $15 \times 10^6 \text{ V}$
C: $8 \times 10^3 \text{ V}$
D: $12 \times 10^4 \text{ V}$', 'Potential at a point is work done per unit charge: $V = \frac{W}{q}$.
$W = 30 \text{ J}$, $q = 2 \text{ mC} = 2 \times 10^{-3} \text{ C}$.
$V = \frac{30}{2 \times 10^{-3}} = 15 \times 10^3 = 1.5 \times 10^4 \text{ V}$.
This is $15000 \text{ V}$ or $10 \times 10^5 / 10 = 10000 \text{ V}$—checking option (a): $10 \times 10^5 = 10^6 \text{ V}$, which does not match. Likely typo in answer key or transcription.', NULL, 'Potential candidate — human review required; no correction approved', 'Yes', '2026-10-18T11:20:07.709Z'::timestamptz, '2026-10-18T12:34:15.495Z'::timestamptz, 'https://app.ilearn-india.com/admin/questions/17984?from=bank') ON CONFLICT (qid) DO UPDATE SET "answer_key" = EXCLUDED."answer_key", "solution_key_review_result" = EXCLUDED."solution_key_review_result", "review_status" = EXCLUDED."review_status", "subject" = EXCLUDED."subject", "exam" = EXCLUDED."exam", "chapter" = EXCLUDED."chapter", "screening_batch_existing_question_ordinal" = EXCLUDED."screening_batch_existing_question_ordinal", "category" = EXCLUDED."category", "deterministic_rules" = EXCLUDED."deterministic_rules", "question_specific_finding_evidence" = EXCLUDED."question_specific_finding_evidence", "publication_status_at_screening" = EXCLUDED."publication_status_at_screening", "current_publication_status" = EXCLUDED."current_publication_status", "flag_status" = EXCLUDED."flag_status", "flag_id" = EXCLUDED."flag_id", "action_in_this_10k_run" = EXCLUDED."action_in_this_10k_run", "exam_linked" = EXCLUDED."exam_linked", "question" = EXCLUDED."question", "options" = EXCLUDED."options", "stored_explanation" = EXCLUDED."stored_explanation", "numeric_answer_policy" = EXCLUDED."numeric_answer_policy", "original_review_status_context" = EXCLUDED."original_review_status_context", "content_unchanged_since_screening" = EXCLUDED."content_unchanged_since_screening", "screened_at_utc" = EXCLUDED."screened_at_utc", "live_status_checked_at_utc" = EXCLUDED."live_status_checked_at_utc", "question_url" = EXCLUDED."question_url";
