B: 1055 °C
C: 1155 °C
D: 1258 °C', 'At steady state: $R_{\text{hot}} = \frac{V}{I} = \frac{220}{2.8} = 78.57$ Ω.
Using $R_T = R_0[1 + \alpha(T - T_0)]$ with $R_0 = 65$ Ω at $T_0 = 20$ °C:
