Validate the current key and retained explanation; preserve correct answers, normal approximations and resolved self-corrections.', 'published', 'published', 'open', 2392, 'Historical finding; no status change in this run', 'No', 'An otherwise infinite, straight wire has two concentric loops of radii $a$ and $b$ carrying equal currents in opposite directions as shown in figure. The magnetic field at the common center is zero for

![62](https://pub-46f930544d71428a9520666ac871983d.r2.dev/question-assets/9da22f43-79eb-40e1-991a-c6191e423347.webp)', 'A: $\frac{a}{b} = \frac{\pi-1}{\pi}$
