Field due to outer loop (radius $b$) at centre: $B_b = \frac{\mu_0 I}{2b}$ (opposite direction).
For net field to be zero: $\frac{\mu_0 I}{2a} = \frac{\mu_0 I}{2b}$ is incorrect reasoning.
