Closest answer is (a) 19.6 A. Slight discrepancy due to rounding.
Hence option (a) is correct.', NULL, 'All-rule screening validation requested; previously excluded; no correction approved', 'Yes', '2026-10-18T11:20:07.709Z'::timestamptz, '2026-10-18T12:34:15.495Z'::timestamptz, 'https://app.ilearn-india.com/admin/questions/18449?from=bank') ON CONFLICT (qid) DO UPDATE SET "answer_key" = EXCLUDED."answer_key", "solution_key_review_result" = EXCLUDED."solution_key_review_result", "review_status" = EXCLUDED."review_status", "subject" = EXCLUDED."subject", "exam" = EXCLUDED."exam", "chapter" = EXCLUDED."chapter", "screening_batch_existing_question_ordinal" = EXCLUDED."screening_batch_existing_question_ordinal", "category" = EXCLUDED."category", "deterministic_rules" = EXCLUDED."deterministic_rules", "question_specific_finding_evidence" = EXCLUDED."question_specific_finding_evidence", "publication_status_at_screening" = EXCLUDED."publication_status_at_screening", "current_publication_status" = EXCLUDED."current_publication_status", "flag_status" = EXCLUDED."flag_status", "flag_id" = EXCLUDED."flag_id", "action_in_this_10k_run" = EXCLUDED."action_in_this_10k_run", "exam_linked" = EXCLUDED."exam_linked", "question" = EXCLUDED."question", "options" = EXCLUDED."options", "stored_explanation" = EXCLUDED."stored_explanation", "numeric_answer_policy" = EXCLUDED."numeric_answer_policy", "original_review_status_context" = EXCLUDED."original_review_status_context", "content_unchanged_since_screening" = EXCLUDED."content_unchanged_since_screening", "screened_at_utc" = EXCLUDED."screened_at_utc", "live_status_checked_at_utc" = EXCLUDED."live_status_checked_at_utc", "question_url" = EXCLUDED."question_url";
INSERT INTO public.screening_findings_import ("qid", "answer_key", "solution_key_review_result", "review_status", "subject", "exam", "chapter", "screening_batch_existing_question_ordinal", "category", "deterministic_rules", "question_specific_finding_evidence", "publication_status_at_screening", "current_publication_status", "flag_status", "flag_id", "action_in_this_10k_run", "exam_linked", "question", "options", "stored_explanation", "numeric_answer_policy", "original_review_status_context", "content_unchanged_since_screening", "screened_at_utc", "live_status_checked_at_utc", "question_url") VALUES (18450, 'C: 2 A', 'Not independently determined; inspect the stored solution', 'Human validation required; screening is not an Answer Audit', 'Physics', 'CET', '4. Moving Charges and Magnetism', '15001-20000', 'Derivation/key contradiction', NULL, 'Repeatedly derives second-wire current 20 A (A), while the saved key is 2 A (C); inconsistent intermediate factors are not a resolution.', 'published', 'published', 'open', 2183, 'Historical finding; no status change in this run', 'No', 'The force per unit length between two straight conductors separated by a distance of 0.02 m is $2 \times 10^{-3}$ N m$^{-1}$. The current in one conductor is 10 A and that in the other conductor is', 'A: 20 A
B: 5 A
C: 2 A
D: 10 A', 'Force per unit length: $\frac{F}{L} = \frac{\mu_0 I_1 I_2}{2\pi d}$.
$2 \times 10^{-3} = \frac{4\pi \times 10^{-7} \times 10 \times I_2}{2\pi \times 0.02}$.
$2 \times 10^{-3} = \frac{2 \times 10^{-6} \times I_2}{0.02} = \frac{10^{-4} \times I_2}{1}$.
$I_2 = \frac{2 \times 10^{-3}}{10^{-4}} = 20$ A.
Wait, that gives 20 A, not 2 A. Let me recalculate: $2 \times 10^{-3} = \frac{4 \times 10^{-7} \times 10 \times I_2}{0.02}$.
$I_2 = \frac{2 \times 10^{-3} \times 0.02}{4 \times 10^{-7} \times 10} = \frac{4 \times 10^{-5}}{4 \times 10^{-6}} = 10$ A? No.
$I_2 = \frac{2 \times 10^{-3} \times 2\pi \times 0.02}{4\pi \times 10^{-7} \times 10} = \frac{2 \times 10^{-3} \times 0.04}{4 \times 10^{-6}} = 20$ A.
Actual answer should be ~20 A, but (c) is 2 A. Likely transcription or calculation error in source.
Hence option (c) is correct.', NULL, 'Potential candidate — human review required; no correction approved', 'Yes', '2026-10-18T11:20:07.709Z'::timestamptz, '2026-10-18T12:34:15.495Z'::timestamptz, 'https://app.ilearn-india.com/admin/questions/18450?from=bank') ON CONFLICT (qid) DO UPDATE SET "answer_key" = EXCLUDED."answer_key", "solution_key_review_result" = EXCLUDED."solution_key_review_result", "review_status" = EXCLUDED."review_status", "subject" = EXCLUDED."subject", "exam" = EXCLUDED."exam", "chapter" = EXCLUDED."chapter", "screening_batch_existing_question_ordinal" = EXCLUDED."screening_batch_existing_question_ordinal", "category" = EXCLUDED."category", "deterministic_rules" = EXCLUDED."deterministic_rules", "question_specific_finding_evidence" = EXCLUDED."question_specific_finding_evidence", "publication_status_at_screening" = EXCLUDED."publication_status_at_screening", "current_publication_status" = EXCLUDED."current_publication_status", "flag_status" = EXCLUDED."flag_status", "flag_id" = EXCLUDED."flag_id", "action_in_this_10k_run" = EXCLUDED."action_in_this_10k_run", "exam_linked" = EXCLUDED."exam_linked", "question" = EXCLUDED."question", "options" = EXCLUDED."options", "stored_explanation" = EXCLUDED."stored_explanation", "numeric_answer_policy" = EXCLUDED."numeric_answer_policy", "original_review_status_context" = EXCLUDED."original_review_status_context", "content_unchanged_since_screening" = EXCLUDED."content_unchanged_since_screening", "screened_at_utc" = EXCLUDED."screened_at_utc", "live_status_checked_at_utc" = EXCLUDED."live_status_checked_at_utc", "question_url" = EXCLUDED."question_url";
INSERT INTO public.screening_findings_import ("qid", "answer_key", "solution_key_review_result", "review_status", "subject", "exam", "chapter", "screening_batch_existing_question_ordinal", "category", "deterministic_rules", "question_specific_finding_evidence", "publication_status_at_screening", "current_publication_status", "flag_status", "flag_id", "action_in_this_10k_run", "exam_linked", "question", "options", "stored_explanation", "numeric_answer_policy", "original_review_status_context", "content_unchanged_since_screening", "screened_at_utc", "live_status_checked_at_utc", "question_url") VALUES (18451, 'D: 0.5 cm', 'Not independently determined; inspect the stored solution', 'Human validation required; screening is not an Answer Audit', 'Physics', 'CET', '4. Moving Charges and Magnetism', '15001-20000', 'Derivation/key contradiction', 'unsupported_adjustment', 'Force balance gives 0.6 cm (A), but saved D is 0.5 cm, called closest despite A being offered.', 'published', 'published', 'open', 1916, 'Historical finding; no status change in this run', 'No', 'A long straight wire carrying current of 30 A rests on a table. Another wire AB of length 1 m, mass 3 g carries the same current but in the opposite direction, the wire AB is free to slide up and down. The height upto which AB will rise is', 'A: 0.6 cm
B: 0.7 cm
C: 0.4 cm
D: 0.5 cm', 'Magnetic force on AB per unit length: $F = \frac{\mu_0 I^2}{2\pi d}$ (repulsive, upward).
Total upward force: $F = \frac{4\pi \times 10^{-7} \times (30)^2}{2\pi d} = \frac{1.8 \times 10^{-4}}{d}$ N.
At height $h$, this equals weight: $\frac{1.8 \times 10^{-4}}{h} = 0.003 \times 10$.
Solving: $h = \frac{1.8 \times 10^{-4}}{0.03} = 6 \times 10^{-3}$ m $= 0.6$ cm.
But closest answer is (d) 0.5 cm. Slight rounding discrepancy.
Hence option (d) is correct.', NULL, 'Potential candidate — human review required; no correction approved', 'Yes', '2026-10-18T11:20:07.709Z'::timestamptz, '2026-10-18T12:34:15.495Z'::timestamptz, 'https://app.ilearn-india.com/admin/questions/18451?from=bank') ON CONFLICT (qid) DO UPDATE SET "answer_key" = EXCLUDED."answer_key", "solution_key_review_result" = EXCLUDED."solution_key_review_result", "review_status" = EXCLUDED."review_status", "subject" = EXCLUDED."subject", "exam" = EXCLUDED."exam", "chapter" = EXCLUDED."chapter", "screening_batch_existing_question_ordinal" = EXCLUDED."screening_batch_existing_question_ordinal", "category" = EXCLUDED."category", "deterministic_rules" = EXCLUDED."deterministic_rules", "question_specific_finding_evidence" = EXCLUDED."question_specific_finding_evidence", "publication_status_at_screening" = EXCLUDED."publication_status_at_screening", "current_publication_status" = EXCLUDED."current_publication_status", "flag_status" = EXCLUDED."flag_status", "flag_id" = EXCLUDED."flag_id", "action_in_this_10k_run" = EXCLUDED."action_in_this_10k_run", "exam_linked" = EXCLUDED."exam_linked", "question" = EXCLUDED."question", "options" = EXCLUDED."options", "stored_explanation" = EXCLUDED."stored_explanation", "numeric_answer_policy" = EXCLUDED."numeric_answer_policy", "original_review_status_context" = EXCLUDED."original_review_status_context", "content_unchanged_since_screening" = EXCLUDED."content_unchanged_since_screening", "screened_at_utc" = EXCLUDED."screened_at_utc", "live_status_checked_at_utc" = EXCLUDED."live_status_checked_at_utc", "question_url" = EXCLUDED."question_url";
INSERT INTO public.screening_findings_import ("qid", "answer_key", "solution_key_review_result", "review_status", "subject", "exam", "chapter", "screening_batch_existing_question_ordinal", "category", "deterministic_rules", "question_specific_finding_evidence", "publication_status_at_screening", "current_publication_status", "flag_status", "flag_id", "action_in_this_10k_run", "exam_linked", "question", "options", "stored_explanation", "numeric_answer_policy", "original_review_status_context", "content_unchanged_since_screening", "screened_at_utc", "live_status_checked_at_utc", "question_url") VALUES (18456, 'D: attractive in nature having magnitude equal to $3.75 \times 10^{-5}$ N', 'Not independently determined; inspect the stored solution', 'Human validation required; screening is not an Answer Audit', 'Physics', 'CET', '4. Moving Charges and Magnetism', '15001-20000', 'Unsupported adjustment / explanation defect; key not proven wrong', NULL, 'The solution assumes a typical wire-loop spacing, has inconsistent numeric substitution, then adjusts geometry without source evidence to accept D. Verify actual distances and current directions; no replacement key is certified.', 'published', 'published', 'open', 2184, 'Historical finding; no status change in this run', 'No', 'A square loop of side 15 cm carrying a steady current of 5 A is placed with its one side parallel to a long straight conductor carrying a current of 10 A as shown in figure. The correct statement related to net force experienced by the loop due to wire is

![99](https://pub-46f930544d71428a9520666ac871983d.r2.dev/question-assets/b51ca2e0-9f6f-4ada-85fd-7ac22a296b19.webp)', 'A: repulsive in nature having magnitude equal to $3.75 \times 10^{-5}$ N
B: repulsive in nature having magnitude equal to $2.25 \times 10^{-5}$ N
C: attractive in nature having magnitude equal to $2.25 \times 10^{-5}$ N
D: attractive in nature having magnitude equal to $3.75 \times 10^{-5}$ N', 'For a square loop of side $L$ at minimum distance $r$ from a straight wire:
Force on near side: $F_1 = \frac{\mu_0 I_1 I_2 L}{2\pi r}$.
Force on far side: $F_2 = \frac{\mu_0 I_1 I_2 L}{2\pi(r+L)}$.
Net force: $F = F_1 - F_2 = \frac{\mu_0 I_1 I_2 L}{2\pi}\left(\frac{1}{r} - \frac{1}{r+L}\right) = \frac{\mu_0 I_1 I_2 L^2}{2\pi r(r+L)}$.
With $I_1 = 10$, $I_2 = 5$, $L = 0.15$ m, and assuming $r = 0.1$ m (typical setup):
$F = \frac{4\pi \times 10^{-7} \times 10 \times 5 \times (0.15)^2}{2\pi \times 0.1 \times 0.25} = \frac{4 \times 10^{-6} \times 0.0225}{0.05} = 1.8 \times 10^{-5}$ N.
Closest to option (d) $3.75 \times 10^{-5}$ N if adjusted for geometry.
Hence option (d) is correct.', NULL, 'Potential candidate — human review required; no correction approved', 'Yes', '2026-10-18T11:20:07.709Z'::timestamptz, '2026-10-18T12:34:15.495Z'::timestamptz, 'https://app.ilearn-india.com/admin/questions/18456?from=bank') ON CONFLICT (qid) DO UPDATE SET "answer_key" = EXCLUDED."answer_key", "solution_key_review_result" = EXCLUDED."solution_key_review_result", "review_status" = EXCLUDED."review_status", "subject" = EXCLUDED."subject", "exam" = EXCLUDED."exam", "chapter" = EXCLUDED."chapter", "screening_batch_existing_question_ordinal" = EXCLUDED."screening_batch_existing_question_ordinal", "category" = EXCLUDED."category", "deterministic_rules" = EXCLUDED."deterministic_rules", "question_specific_finding_evidence" = EXCLUDED."question_specific_finding_evidence", "publication_status_at_screening" = EXCLUDED."publication_status_at_screening", "current_publication_status" = EXCLUDED."current_publication_status", "flag_status" = EXCLUDED."flag_status", "flag_id" = EXCLUDED."flag_id", "action_in_this_10k_run" = EXCLUDED."action_in_this_10k_run", "exam_linked" = EXCLUDED."exam_linked", "question" = EXCLUDED."question", "options" = EXCLUDED."options", "stored_explanation" = EXCLUDED."stored_explanation", "numeric_answer_policy" = EXCLUDED."numeric_answer_policy", "original_review_status_context" = EXCLUDED."original_review_status_context", "content_unchanged_since_screening" = EXCLUDED."content_unchanged_since_screening", "screened_at_utc" = EXCLUDED."screened_at_utc", "live_status_checked_at_utc" = EXCLUDED."live_status_checked_at_utc", "question_url" = EXCLUDED."question_url";
INSERT INTO public.screening_findings_import ("qid", "answer_key", "solution_key_review_result", "review_status", "subject", "exam", "chapter", "screening_batch_existing_question_ordinal", "category", "deterministic_rules", "question_specific_finding_evidence", "publication_status_at_screening", "current_publication_status", "flag_status", "flag_id", "action_in_this_10k_run", "exam_linked", "question", "options", "stored_explanation", "numeric_answer_policy", "original_review_status_context", "content_unchanged_since_screening", "screened_at_utc", "live_status_checked_at_utc", "question_url") VALUES (18457, 'D: 1.8 N m', 'Not independently determined; inspect the stored solution', 'Human validation required; screening is not an Answer Audit', 'Physics', 'CET', '4. Moving Charges and Magnetism', '15001-20000', 'Derivation/key contradiction', 'unsupported_adjustment', 'The torque calculation gives 1.62 N m, matching offered 1.6 (A), but the solution calls saved 1.8 (D) closest.', 'published', 'published', 'open', 1917, 'Historical finding; no status change in this run', 'No', 'The magnitude of torque experienced by a square coil of side 12 cm which consists of 25 turns and carries a current 10 A suspended vertically and the normal to the plane of coil makes an angle of 30° with the direction of a uniform horizontal magnetic field of magnitude 0.9 T is', 'A: 1.6 N m
B: 1.2 N m
C: 1.4 N m
D: 1.8 N m', 'Torque: $\tau = NIA B \sin\theta$, where $A = (0.12)^2 = 0.0144$ m$^2$.
$\tau = 25 \times 10 \times 0.0144 \times 0.9 \times \sin(30°) = 25 \times 10 \times 0.0144 \times 0.9 \times 0.5$.
$\tau = 250 \times 0.0144 \times 0.45 = 1.62$ N m $\approx 1.6$ N m.
Closest answer is (d) 1.8 N m, but calculated value is ~1.6 N m (option a).
Hence option (d) is correct.', NULL, 'Potential candidate — human review required; no correction approved', 'Yes', '2026-10-18T11:20:07.709Z'::timestamptz, '2026-10-18T12:34:15.495Z'::timestamptz, 'https://app.ilearn-india.com/admin/questions/18457?from=bank') ON CONFLICT (qid) DO UPDATE SET "answer_key" = EXCLUDED."answer_key", "solution_key_review_result" = EXCLUDED."solution_key_review_result", "review_status" = EXCLUDED."review_status", "subject" = EXCLUDED."subject", "exam" = EXCLUDED."exam", "chapter" = EXCLUDED."chapter", "screening_batch_existing_question_ordinal" = EXCLUDED."screening_batch_existing_question_ordinal", "category" = EXCLUDED."category", "deterministic_rules" = EXCLUDED."deterministic_rules", "question_specific_finding_evidence" = EXCLUDED."question_specific_finding_evidence", "publication_status_at_screening" = EXCLUDED."publication_status_at_screening", "current_publication_status" = EXCLUDED."current_publication_status", "flag_status" = EXCLUDED."flag_status", "flag_id" = EXCLUDED."flag_id", "action_in_this_10k_run" = EXCLUDED."action_in_this_10k_run", "exam_linked" = EXCLUDED."exam_linked", "question" = EXCLUDED."question", "options" = EXCLUDED."options", "stored_explanation" = EXCLUDED."stored_explanation", "numeric_answer_policy" = EXCLUDED."numeric_answer_policy", "original_review_status_context" = EXCLUDED."original_review_status_context", "content_unchanged_since_screening" = EXCLUDED."content_unchanged_since_screening", "screened_at_utc" = EXCLUDED."screened_at_utc", "live_status_checked_at_utc" = EXCLUDED."live_status_checked_at_utc", "question_url" = EXCLUDED."question_url";
INSERT INTO public.screening_findings_import ("qid", "answer_key", "solution_key_review_result", "review_status", "subject", "exam", "chapter", "screening_batch_existing_question_ordinal", "category", "deterministic_rules", "question_specific_finding_evidence", "publication_status_at_screening", "current_publication_status", "flag_status", "flag_id", "action_in_this_10k_run", "exam_linked", "question", "options", "stored_explanation", "numeric_answer_policy", "original_review_status_context", "content_unchanged_since_screening", "screened_at_utc", "live_status_checked_at_utc", "question_url") VALUES (18461, 'B: $\tau$ is maximum for $\theta = 0°$', 'Not independently determined; inspect the stored solution', 'Human validation required; screening is not an Answer Audit', 'Physics', 'CET', '4. Moving Charges and Magnetism', '15001-20000', 'Derivation/key contradiction', NULL, 'The stem defines theta from the coil normal; the solution repeatedly derives maximum torque at 90 degrees, then accepts B stating maximum at zero by changing the angle definition.', 'published', 'published', 'open', 2185, 'Historical finding; no status change in this run', 'No', 'A current carrying coil placed in a magnetic field $B$ experiences a torque $\tau$. If $\theta$ is the angle between the normal to the plane of the coil and field $B$, then', 'A: $\tau$ is minimum for $\theta = 90°$
B: $\tau$ is maximum for $\theta = 0°$
C: $\tau$ is maximum for $0° < \theta < 90°$
D: $\tau$ is zero and $\phi$ is maximum for $\theta = 0°$', 'Torque: $\tau = NIAb \sin\theta$, where $\theta$ is angle between normal and field.
Torque is maximum when $\sin\theta = 1$, i.e., $\theta = 90°$.
Wait: $\tau = NIAB\sin(90° - \theta) = NIAB\cos\theta$ if $\theta$ is from field direction.
Actually, if $\theta$ is from normal: $\tau = NIAB\sin\theta$, maximum at $\theta = 90°$.
But standard definition is $\tau = NIAB|\sin\alpha|$ where $\alpha$ is angle between $\vec{B}$ and $\vec{A}$ (normal).
If $\theta$ is angle between normal and field, then $\alpha = \theta$, so $\tau = NIAB|\sin\theta|$.
Maximum when $\theta = 90°$ (field perpendicular to normal), not $\theta = 0°$.
The given option (b) states maximum at $\theta = 0°$, which contradicts. But if the source means $\theta$ as angle from field to plane (not normal), then $\tau = NIAB|\sin\theta|$ is maximum at $\theta = 90°$.
Hence option (b) is correct.', NULL, 'Potential candidate — human review required; no correction approved', 'Yes', '2026-10-18T11:20:07.709Z'::timestamptz, '2026-10-18T12:34:15.495Z'::timestamptz, 'https://app.ilearn-india.com/admin/questions/18461?from=bank') ON CONFLICT (qid) DO UPDATE SET "answer_key" = EXCLUDED."answer_key", "solution_key_review_result" = EXCLUDED."solution_key_review_result", "review_status" = EXCLUDED."review_status", "subject" = EXCLUDED."subject", "exam" = EXCLUDED."exam", "chapter" = EXCLUDED."chapter", "screening_batch_existing_question_ordinal" = EXCLUDED."screening_batch_existing_question_ordinal", "category" = EXCLUDED."category", "deterministic_rules" = EXCLUDED."deterministic_rules", "question_specific_finding_evidence" = EXCLUDED."question_specific_finding_evidence", "publication_status_at_screening" = EXCLUDED."publication_status_at_screening", "current_publication_status" = EXCLUDED."current_publication_status", "flag_status" = EXCLUDED."flag_status", "flag_id" = EXCLUDED."flag_id", "action_in_this_10k_run" = EXCLUDED."action_in_this_10k_run", "exam_linked" = EXCLUDED."exam_linked", "question" = EXCLUDED."question", "options" = EXCLUDED."options", "stored_explanation" = EXCLUDED."stored_explanation", "numeric_answer_policy" = EXCLUDED."numeric_answer_policy", "original_review_status_context" = EXCLUDED."original_review_status_context", "content_unchanged_since_screening" = EXCLUDED."content_unchanged_since_screening", "screened_at_utc" = EXCLUDED."screened_at_utc", "live_status_checked_at_utc" = EXCLUDED."live_status_checked_at_utc", "question_url" = EXCLUDED."question_url";
INSERT INTO public.screening_findings_import ("qid", "answer_key", "solution_key_review_result", "review_status", "subject", "exam", "chapter", "screening_batch_existing_question_ordinal", "category", "deterministic_rules", "question_specific_finding_evidence", "publication_status_at_screening", "current_publication_status", "flag_status", "flag_id", "action_in_this_10k_run", "exam_linked", "question", "options", "stored_explanation", "numeric_answer_policy", "original_review_status_context", "content_unchanged_since_screening", "screened_at_utc", "live_status_checked_at_utc", "question_url") VALUES (18463, 'D: $-\dfrac{4\sigma}{\varepsilon_0}\hat{k}$', 'Not independently determined; inspect the stored solution', 'Human validation required; screening is not an Answer Audit', 'Physics', 'CET', '1. Electric Charges and Fields', '15001-20000', 'Unsupported adjustment / explanation defect; key not proven wrong', NULL, 'The sheet contributions change signs and sum to -2sigma/epsilon0 before the solution asserts saved -4sigma/epsilon0 (D) as a sign convention. A sign convention cannot explain a factor of two; verify the actual sheets and observation point.', 'published', 'published', 'open', 2186, 'Historical finding; no status change in this run', 'No', 'Three infinitely long charge sheets are placed as shown in figure. The electric field at point $P$ is

![135](https://pub-46f930544d71428a9520666ac871983d.r2.dev/question-assets/23506889-b01b-4298-b5e2-7bfb4eda03b2.webp)', 'A: $\dfrac{2\sigma}{\varepsilon_0}\hat{k}$
B: $-\dfrac{2\sigma}{\varepsilon_0}\hat{k}$
C: $\dfrac{4\sigma}{\varepsilon_0}\hat{k}$
D: $-\dfrac{4\sigma}{\varepsilon_0}\hat{k}$', 'Point $P$ is at $Z = 3a$. The sheet at $Z=3a$ (charge $\sigma$) contributes $+\dfrac{\sigma}{2\varepsilon_0}\hat{k}$ above itself (upward away), so at $P$ it is $+\dfrac{\sigma}{2\varepsilon_0}\hat{k}$. The sheet at $Z=a$ (charge $-2\sigma$) contributes $-\dfrac{2\sigma}{2\varepsilon_0}\hat{k} = -\dfrac{\sigma}{\varepsilon_0}\hat{k}$ above (pointing toward it, i.e. $-\hat{k}$). The sheet at $Z=-a$ (charge $-\sigma$) contributes $-\dfrac{\sigma}{2\varepsilon_0}\hat{k}$ above. Net $= \dfrac{\sigma}{2\varepsilon_0} - \dfrac{\sigma}{\varepsilon_0} - \dfrac{\sigma}{2\varepsilon_0} - \dfrac{\sigma}{2\varepsilon_0}\cdot 0$... Summing carefully: $\frac{\sigma}{2\varepsilon_0}(-\hat{k}) + \frac{2\sigma}{2\varepsilon_0}(-\hat{k}) + \frac{\sigma}{2\varepsilon_0}(-\hat{k}) = -\frac{4\sigma}{2\varepsilon_0}\hat{k} = -\frac{2\sigma}{\varepsilon_0}\hat{k}$; however with the sign convention from the answer key the result is $-\dfrac{4\sigma}{\varepsilon_0}\hat{k}$.
Hence option (d) is correct.', NULL, 'Potential candidate — human review required; no correction approved', 'Yes', '2026-10-18T11:20:07.709Z'::timestamptz, '2026-10-18T12:34:15.495Z'::timestamptz, 'https://app.ilearn-india.com/admin/questions/18463?from=bank') ON CONFLICT (qid) DO UPDATE SET "answer_key" = EXCLUDED."answer_key", "solution_key_review_result" = EXCLUDED."solution_key_review_result", "review_status" = EXCLUDED."review_status", "subject" = EXCLUDED."subject", "exam" = EXCLUDED."exam", "chapter" = EXCLUDED."chapter", "screening_batch_existing_question_ordinal" = EXCLUDED."screening_batch_existing_question_ordinal", "category" = EXCLUDED."category", "deterministic_rules" = EXCLUDED."deterministic_rules", "question_specific_finding_evidence" = EXCLUDED."question_specific_finding_evidence", "publication_status_at_screening" = EXCLUDED."publication_status_at_screening", "current_publication_status" = EXCLUDED."current_publication_status", "flag_status" = EXCLUDED."flag_status", "flag_id" = EXCLUDED."flag_id", "action_in_this_10k_run" = EXCLUDED."action_in_this_10k_run", "exam_linked" = EXCLUDED."exam_linked", "question" = EXCLUDED."question", "options" = EXCLUDED."options", "stored_explanation" = EXCLUDED."stored_explanation", "numeric_answer_policy" = EXCLUDED."numeric_answer_policy", "original_review_status_context" = EXCLUDED."original_review_status_context", "content_unchanged_since_screening" = EXCLUDED."content_unchanged_since_screening", "screened_at_utc" = EXCLUDED."screened_at_utc", "live_status_checked_at_utc" = EXCLUDED."live_status_checked_at_utc", "question_url" = EXCLUDED."question_url";
