Prior contextual-review reason: The stored explanation does not establish a contrary geometric charge-fraction calculation; the negative-stem lexical hit alone is not enough to confirm this discrepancy class.
Validate the current key and retained explanation; preserve correct answers, normal approximations and resolved self-corrections.', 'published', 'published', 'open', 2394, 'Historical finding; no status change in this run', 'Yes', 'A charged shell of radius R carries a total charge Q. Given $\Phi$ as the flux of electric field through a closed cylindrical surface of height h, radius r and with its center same as that of the shell. Here, center of cylinder is a point on the axis of the cylinder which is equidistant from its top and bottom surfaces. Which of the following option(s) is/are incorrect? [$\varepsilon_0$ is the permittivity of free space]', 'A: If $h > 2R$ and $r = \frac{4R}{5}$ then $\Phi = \frac{Q}{5\varepsilon_0}$
B: If $h > 2R$ and $r = \frac{3R}{5}$ then $\Phi = \frac{Q}{5\varepsilon_0}$
C: If $h < \frac{8R}{5}$ and $r = \frac{3R}{5}$ then $\Phi = 0$
D: If $h > 2R$ and $r > R$ then $\Phi = \frac{Q}{\varepsilon_0}$', 'For a uniformly charged spherical shell:
If the cylinder encloses the entire shell ($h > 2R$, $r > R$), flux is $\frac{Q}{\varepsilon_0}$.
If the cylinder is entirely outside ($r > R$ and within shell boundaries), the enclosed charge depends on the intersection.
For $h > 2R$ and $r = \frac{3R}{5} < R$: the cylindrical surface may be partially inside the shell.
By Gauss''s law, if the cylinder encloses a fraction of the charge, the flux is a fraction of $\frac{Q}{\varepsilon_0}$.
Option (b) needs verification based on geometry; it may be incorrect.', NULL, 'All-rule screening validation requested; previously excluded; no correction approved', 'Yes', '2026-10-18T11:20:07.709Z'::timestamptz, '2026-10-18T12:34:15.495Z'::timestamptz, 'https://app.ilearn-india.com/admin/questions/18536?from=bank') ON CONFLICT (qid) DO UPDATE SET "answer_key" = EXCLUDED."answer_key", "solution_key_review_result" = EXCLUDED."solution_key_review_result", "review_status" = EXCLUDED."review_status", "subject" = EXCLUDED."subject", "exam" = EXCLUDED."exam", "chapter" = EXCLUDED."chapter", "screening_batch_existing_question_ordinal" = EXCLUDED."screening_batch_existing_question_ordinal", "category" = EXCLUDED."category", "deterministic_rules" = EXCLUDED."deterministic_rules", "question_specific_finding_evidence" = EXCLUDED."question_specific_finding_evidence", "publication_status_at_screening" = EXCLUDED."publication_status_at_screening", "current_publication_status" = EXCLUDED."current_publication_status", "flag_status" = EXCLUDED."flag_status", "flag_id" = EXCLUDED."flag_id", "action_in_this_10k_run" = EXCLUDED."action_in_this_10k_run", "exam_linked" = EXCLUDED."exam_linked", "question" = EXCLUDED."question", "options" = EXCLUDED."options", "stored_explanation" = EXCLUDED."stored_explanation", "numeric_answer_policy" = EXCLUDED."numeric_answer_policy", "original_review_status_context" = EXCLUDED."original_review_status_context", "content_unchanged_since_screening" = EXCLUDED."content_unchanged_since_screening", "screened_at_utc" = EXCLUDED."screened_at_utc", "live_status_checked_at_utc" = EXCLUDED."live_status_checked_at_utc", "question_url" = EXCLUDED."question_url";
