D: $2.66 \times 10$ mH', 'Mutual inductance: $M = \frac{\varepsilon}{dI/dt} = \frac{8 \times 10^{-3}}{3} = 2.667 \times 10^{-3}$ H = $2.667$ mH $\approx 2.66 \times 10^{-1}$ mH? No, that''s 0.266 mH.
