B: $\frac{\mu_0 I \omega r^2}{4R} \sin(\omega t)$
C: $\frac{\mu_0 I \omega r^2}{2R} \sin(\omega t)$
D: $\frac{\mu_0 I \omega \pi r^2}{2R} \sin(\omega t)$', 'Magnetic field at centre of large coil due to current I: $B = \frac{\mu_0 I}{2R}$.
Flux through small coil when rotated: $\Phi(t) = B \pi r^2 \cos(\omega t) = \frac{\mu_0 I \pi r^2}{2R} \cos(\omega t)$.
