B: $\frac{120}{\sqrt{2}}$ V and 100 Hz
C: 60 V and 200 Hz
D: 60 V and 100 Hz', 'Use the identity $\sin(x)\cos(x) = \frac{1}{2}\sin(2x)$.
$V = 120 \times \frac{1}{2}\sin(200\pi t) = 60\sin(200\pi t)$ V.
Peak voltage is 60 V. Comparing with $V_0\sin(\omega t)$: $\omega = 200\pi$, so $f = \frac{\omega}{2\pi} = 100$ Hz... wait, let me recalculate: $200\pi = 2\pi f \Rightarrow f = 100$ Hz is wrong. $f = \frac{200\pi}{2\pi} = 100$ Hz is still incorrect. Actually $\omega = 200\pi \Rightarrow f = \frac{200\pi}{2\pi} = 100$ Hz. The frequency should be 100 Hz, not 200 Hz based on standard convention, but the product rule gives $\omega = 200\pi$, yielding $f = 100$ Hz. Rechecking: $\sin(2x)$ means angular frequency doubles, so $f = 2 \times 100 = 200$ Hz.
Hence option (c) is correct.', NULL, 'Potential candidate — human review required; no correction approved', 'Yes', '2026-10-18T11:20:07.709Z'::timestamptz, '2026-10-18T12:34:15.495Z'::timestamptz, 'https://app.ilearn-india.com/admin/questions/19035?from=bank') ON CONFLICT (qid) DO UPDATE SET "answer_key" = EXCLUDED."answer_key", "solution_key_review_result" = EXCLUDED."solution_key_review_result", "review_status" = EXCLUDED."review_status", "subject" = EXCLUDED."subject", "exam" = EXCLUDED."exam", "chapter" = EXCLUDED."chapter", "screening_batch_existing_question_ordinal" = EXCLUDED."screening_batch_existing_question_ordinal", "category" = EXCLUDED."category", "deterministic_rules" = EXCLUDED."deterministic_rules", "question_specific_finding_evidence" = EXCLUDED."question_specific_finding_evidence", "publication_status_at_screening" = EXCLUDED."publication_status_at_screening", "current_publication_status" = EXCLUDED."current_publication_status", "flag_status" = EXCLUDED."flag_status", "flag_id" = EXCLUDED."flag_id", "action_in_this_10k_run" = EXCLUDED."action_in_this_10k_run", "exam_linked" = EXCLUDED."exam_linked", "question" = EXCLUDED."question", "options" = EXCLUDED."options", "stored_explanation" = EXCLUDED."stored_explanation", "numeric_answer_policy" = EXCLUDED."numeric_answer_policy", "original_review_status_context" = EXCLUDED."original_review_status_context", "content_unchanged_since_screening" = EXCLUDED."content_unchanged_since_screening", "screened_at_utc" = EXCLUDED."screened_at_utc", "live_status_checked_at_utc" = EXCLUDED."live_status_checked_at_utc", "question_url" = EXCLUDED."question_url";
