Validate the current key and retained explanation; preserve correct answers, normal approximations and resolved self-corrections.', 'published', 'published', 'open', 2411, 'Historical finding; no status change in this run', 'No', 'When an AC voltage of $V = 330 \sin(100\pi t)$ is applied to a capacitor, it produces a current of $I = 1.5 \cos(100\pi t)$. The capacitive reactance of the capacitor is', 'A: 120 Ω
B: 180 Ω
