D: $R = 10\ k\Omega,\ L = 10\ $mH', 'From the figure, current leads voltage so it''s an RC circuit. $\omega = 100$ rad/s, phase difference $\pi/4$ means $X_C = R$, so $1/(\omega C) = R = 1000\ \Omega$, giving $C = 1/(100 \times 1000) = 10\ \mu$F — but answer key gives (b) $C = 1\ \mu$F.
