Screening trigger: Broad lexical screen matched: incorrect
Prior contextual-review reason: Read stem, current options/key and full retained explanation: the lexical hit does not establish an unresolved derivation-versus-current-key conflict under this screening scope.
Validate the current key and retained explanation; preserve correct answers, normal approximations and resolved self-corrections.', 'published', 'published', 'open', 2417, 'Historical finding; no status change in this run', 'No', 'Choose the incorrect statement', 'A: Power dissipation in a pure capacitive circuit is zero.
B: In transformer frequency remains unchanged.
C: Transformer works only for AC.
D: At resonance, the power dissipation is minimum.', 'At resonance, impedance is minimum ($Z = R$), so current is maximum, and power dissipation $P = I^2 R$ is maximum, not minimum.
Hence statement (d) is incorrect, making option (d) the correct answer.', NULL, 'All-rule screening validation requested; previously excluded; no correction approved', 'Yes', '2026-10-18T11:20:07.709Z'::timestamptz, '2026-10-18T12:34:15.495Z'::timestamptz, 'https://app.ilearn-india.com/admin/questions/19197?from=bank') ON CONFLICT (qid) DO UPDATE SET "answer_key" = EXCLUDED."answer_key", "solution_key_review_result" = EXCLUDED."solution_key_review_result", "review_status" = EXCLUDED."review_status", "subject" = EXCLUDED."subject", "exam" = EXCLUDED."exam", "chapter" = EXCLUDED."chapter", "screening_batch_existing_question_ordinal" = EXCLUDED."screening_batch_existing_question_ordinal", "category" = EXCLUDED."category", "deterministic_rules" = EXCLUDED."deterministic_rules", "question_specific_finding_evidence" = EXCLUDED."question_specific_finding_evidence", "publication_status_at_screening" = EXCLUDED."publication_status_at_screening", "current_publication_status" = EXCLUDED."current_publication_status", "flag_status" = EXCLUDED."flag_status", "flag_id" = EXCLUDED."flag_id", "action_in_this_10k_run" = EXCLUDED."action_in_this_10k_run", "exam_linked" = EXCLUDED."exam_linked", "question" = EXCLUDED."question", "options" = EXCLUDED."options", "stored_explanation" = EXCLUDED."stored_explanation", "numeric_answer_policy" = EXCLUDED."numeric_answer_policy", "original_review_status_context" = EXCLUDED."original_review_status_context", "content_unchanged_since_screening" = EXCLUDED."content_unchanged_since_screening", "screened_at_utc" = EXCLUDED."screened_at_utc", "live_status_checked_at_utc" = EXCLUDED."live_status_checked_at_utc", "question_url" = EXCLUDED."question_url";
INSERT INTO public.screening_findings_import ("qid", "answer_key", "solution_key_review_result", "review_status", "subject", "exam", "chapter", "screening_batch_existing_question_ordinal", "category", "deterministic_rules", "question_specific_finding_evidence", "publication_status_at_screening", "current_publication_status", "flag_status", "flag_id", "action_in_this_10k_run", "exam_linked", "question", "options", "stored_explanation", "numeric_answer_policy", "original_review_status_context", "content_unchanged_since_screening", "screened_at_utc", "live_status_checked_at_utc", "question_url") VALUES (19198, 'B: 500', 'Not independently determined; inspect the stored solution', 'Human validation required; screening is not an Answer Audit', 'Physics', 'CET', '7. Alternating Current', '15001-20000', 'Derivation/key contradiction', NULL, 'Derives n=400 (C) from the calculated capacitor, while the saved key is 500 (B).', 'published', 'published', 'open', 2230, 'Historical finding; no status change in this run', 'No', 'In a series LR circuit, power of 400 W is dissipated from a source of 250 V, 50 Hz. The power factor of the circuit is 0.8. In order to bring the power factor to unity, a capacitor of value of $C$ is added in series to the $L$ and $R$. Taking the value of $C$ as $\left(\dfrac{n}{3\pi}\right)\mu$F, then value of $n$ is', 'A: 630
B: 500
C: 400
D: 490', '$I = P/(V\cos\phi) = 400/(250 \times 0.8) = 2$ A. $R = P/I^2 = 100\ \Omega$. $Z = V/I = 125\ \Omega$. $X_L = \sqrt{Z^2 - R^2} = 75\ \Omega$. For unity p.f., $X_C = X_L = 75\ \Omega$. $C = 1/(\omega X_C) = 1/(100\pi \times 75) = 1/(7500\pi)\ $F $= (n/3\pi)\times 10^{-6}$ → $n = 3\pi/(7500\pi \times 10^{-6}) = 3/0.0075 = 400$... but answer key gives (b) 500.
