![r35](https://pub-46f930544d71428a9520666ac871983d.r2.dev/question-assets/73e16099-01d4-4e30-8c7c-081a62bed19c.webp)', 'A: $\dfrac{100}{\pi}$ mH
B: $\dfrac{200}{\pi}$ mH
C: $\dfrac{100}{\sqrt{\pi}}$ mH
D: $\dfrac{200}{\sqrt{\pi}}$ mH', 'Given $V_L = V_C = 2V_R$, circuit is at resonance (since $V_L = V_C$). At resonance, $\omega L = 1/\omega C$. With $V_L = 2V_R$ and $R = 5\ \Omega$ (from figure), $X_L = 2R = 10\ \Omega$. $L = X_L/\omega = 10/(2\pi \times 50) = 10/(100\pi) = 100/(1000\pi)$ H $= (100/\pi)$ mH. Answer key gives (d) $200/\sqrt{\pi}$ mH.
