D: parallel with $C$ and has a magnitude $\dfrac{1-\omega^2 LC}{\omega^2 L}$', 'Since current leads, $X_C > X_L$, circuit is capacitive. To make p.f. unity, reduce net capacitance by adding $C''$ in parallel (which increases total capacitance) — no, we need to decrease $X_C$, so reduce total C. Adding $C''$ in series reduces total C, making $X_C$ larger — wrong. Adding $C''$ in parallel increases $C$, decreasing $X_C$ toward $X_L$.
For parallel: total $C_{total} = C + C''$, unity p.f. needs $X_C = X_L$: $1/\omega(C+C'') = \omega L$, so $C'' = 1/(\omega^2 L) - C = (1-\omega^2 LC)/(\omega^2 L)$.
