Validate the current key and retained explanation; preserve correct answers, normal approximations and resolved self-corrections.', 'published', 'published', 'open', 2423, 'Historical finding; no status change in this run', 'No', 'Let $n_p$ and $n_e$ be the numbers of holes and conduction electrons in an extrinsic semiconductor. Then which one is incorrect?', 'A: $n_p \gg n_e$
B: $n_p = n_e$
