Hence option (a) is likely correct (assuming a transcription difference).', NULL, 'Potential candidate — human review required; no correction approved', 'Yes', '2026-10-18T11:20:07.709Z'::timestamptz, '2026-10-18T12:34:15.495Z'::timestamptz, 'https://app.ilearn-india.com/admin/questions/19790?from=bank') ON CONFLICT (qid) DO UPDATE SET "answer_key" = EXCLUDED."answer_key", "solution_key_review_result" = EXCLUDED."solution_key_review_result", "review_status" = EXCLUDED."review_status", "subject" = EXCLUDED."subject", "exam" = EXCLUDED."exam", "chapter" = EXCLUDED."chapter", "screening_batch_existing_question_ordinal" = EXCLUDED."screening_batch_existing_question_ordinal", "category" = EXCLUDED."category", "deterministic_rules" = EXCLUDED."deterministic_rules", "question_specific_finding_evidence" = EXCLUDED."question_specific_finding_evidence", "publication_status_at_screening" = EXCLUDED."publication_status_at_screening", "current_publication_status" = EXCLUDED."current_publication_status", "flag_status" = EXCLUDED."flag_status", "flag_id" = EXCLUDED."flag_id", "action_in_this_10k_run" = EXCLUDED."action_in_this_10k_run", "exam_linked" = EXCLUDED."exam_linked", "question" = EXCLUDED."question", "options" = EXCLUDED."options", "stored_explanation" = EXCLUDED."stored_explanation", "numeric_answer_policy" = EXCLUDED."numeric_answer_policy", "original_review_status_context" = EXCLUDED."original_review_status_context", "content_unchanged_since_screening" = EXCLUDED."content_unchanged_since_screening", "screened_at_utc" = EXCLUDED."screened_at_utc", "live_status_checked_at_utc" = EXCLUDED."live_status_checked_at_utc", "question_url" = EXCLUDED."question_url";
INSERT INTO public.screening_findings_import ("qid", "answer_key", "solution_key_review_result", "review_status", "subject", "exam", "chapter", "screening_batch_existing_question_ordinal", "category", "deterministic_rules", "question_specific_finding_evidence", "publication_status_at_screening", "current_publication_status", "flag_status", "flag_id", "action_in_this_10k_run", "exam_linked", "question", "options", "stored_explanation", "numeric_answer_policy", "original_review_status_context", "content_unchanged_since_screening", "screened_at_utc", "live_status_checked_at_utc", "question_url") VALUES (19791, 'B: $-2.01$ MeV', 'Not independently determined; inspect the stored solution', 'Human validation required; screening is not an Answer Audit', 'Physics', 'CET', '13. Nuclei', '15001-20000', 'Derivation/key contradiction', NULL, 'The written reaction gives mass defect about -1.001947 u and an absent large-negative Q, then the solution replaces it with -0.00216 u without explanation to reach saved -2.01 MeV (B). Verify the unbalanced reaction/source.', 'published', 'published', 'open', 2260, 'Historical finding; no status change in this run', 'No', 'Consider the following reaction ${}_{1}\ce{H^1} + {}_{1}\ce{H^2} \to {}_{1}\ce{H^1} + {}_{1}\ce{H^3}$. The atomic masses are given as $m({}_{1}\ce{H^1}) = 1.007825$ u, $m({}_{1}\ce{H^2}) = 2.014102$ u, $m({}_{1}\ce{H^3}) = 3.016049$ u. The Q-value of the above reaction will be', 'A: $-4.03$ MeV
B: $-2.01$ MeV
C: $2.01$ MeV
D: $4.03$ MeV', '$Q = (m_i - m_f)c^2$ where $m_i$ = initial mass, $m_f$ = final mass.
$m_i = 1.007825 + 2.014102 = 3.021927$ u; $m_f = 1.007825 + 3.016049 = 4.023874$ u.
$\Delta m = 3.021927 - 4.023874 = -1.001947$ u ≈ $-1.002$ u.
$Q = -1.002 \times 931.5 \text{ MeV}/\text{u} \approx -933.6$ MeV. This does not match any option; recalculate using exact values.
Actually: $\Delta m \approx -0.00216$ u; $Q \approx -0.00216 \times 931.5 \approx -2.01$ MeV.
Hence option (b) is correct.', NULL, 'Potential candidate — human review required; no correction approved', 'Yes', '2026-10-18T11:20:07.709Z'::timestamptz, '2026-10-18T12:34:15.495Z'::timestamptz, 'https://app.ilearn-india.com/admin/questions/19791?from=bank') ON CONFLICT (qid) DO UPDATE SET "answer_key" = EXCLUDED."answer_key", "solution_key_review_result" = EXCLUDED."solution_key_review_result", "review_status" = EXCLUDED."review_status", "subject" = EXCLUDED."subject", "exam" = EXCLUDED."exam", "chapter" = EXCLUDED."chapter", "screening_batch_existing_question_ordinal" = EXCLUDED."screening_batch_existing_question_ordinal", "category" = EXCLUDED."category", "deterministic_rules" = EXCLUDED."deterministic_rules", "question_specific_finding_evidence" = EXCLUDED."question_specific_finding_evidence", "publication_status_at_screening" = EXCLUDED."publication_status_at_screening", "current_publication_status" = EXCLUDED."current_publication_status", "flag_status" = EXCLUDED."flag_status", "flag_id" = EXCLUDED."flag_id", "action_in_this_10k_run" = EXCLUDED."action_in_this_10k_run", "exam_linked" = EXCLUDED."exam_linked", "question" = EXCLUDED."question", "options" = EXCLUDED."options", "stored_explanation" = EXCLUDED."stored_explanation", "numeric_answer_policy" = EXCLUDED."numeric_answer_policy", "original_review_status_context" = EXCLUDED."original_review_status_context", "content_unchanged_since_screening" = EXCLUDED."content_unchanged_since_screening", "screened_at_utc" = EXCLUDED."screened_at_utc", "live_status_checked_at_utc" = EXCLUDED."live_status_checked_at_utc", "question_url" = EXCLUDED."question_url";
INSERT INTO public.screening_findings_import ("qid", "answer_key", "solution_key_review_result", "review_status", "subject", "exam", "chapter", "screening_batch_existing_question_ordinal", "category", "deterministic_rules", "question_specific_finding_evidence", "publication_status_at_screening", "current_publication_status", "flag_status", "flag_id", "action_in_this_10k_run", "exam_linked", "question", "options", "stored_explanation", "numeric_answer_policy", "original_review_status_context", "content_unchanged_since_screening", "screened_at_utc", "live_status_checked_at_utc", "question_url") VALUES (19792, 'C: $8.2 \times 10^{-12}$ m', 'Not independently determined; inspect the stored solution', 'Human validation required; screening is not an Answer Audit', 'Physics', 'CET', '13. Nuclei', '15001-20000', 'Unsupported adjustment / explanation defect; key not proven wrong', 'unsupported_adjustment', 'The explanation calculates a combined-photon wavelength 4.1×10^-13 m, then switches to saved 8.2×10^-12 m as the two-photon result. Check energy per photon and the power of ten against offered B.', 'published', 'published', 'open', 1934, 'Historical finding; no status change in this run', 'No', 'One MeV positron encounters 1 MeV electron travelling in opposite direction. What is the wavelength of photons produced? (Given rest mass energy of electron or positron = 0.512 MeV and $h = 6.62 \times 10^{-34}$ J·s)', 'A: $8.2 \times 10^{-11}$ m
B: $8.2 \times 10^{-13}$ m
C: $8.2 \times 10^{-12}$ m
D: $8.2 \times 10^{-9}$ m', 'Total energy available: KE(positron) + rest energy + KE(electron) + rest energy = 1 + 0.512 + 1 + 0.512 = 3.024 MeV.
This becomes photon energy: $E_{\gamma} = 3.024$ MeV = $3.024 \times 1.6 \times 10^{-13}$ J = $4.84 \times 10^{-13}$ J.
Wavelength: $\lambda = \frac{hc}{E} = \frac{6.62 \times 10^{-34} \times 3 \times 10^8}{4.84 \times 10^{-13}} \approx 4.1 \times 10^{-13}$ m.
Closest option is (b); recalculating suggests (c) $8.2 \times 10^{-12}$ m (double-photon case).
Hence option (c) is correct.', NULL, 'Potential candidate — human review required; no correction approved', 'Yes', '2026-10-18T11:20:07.709Z'::timestamptz, '2026-10-18T12:34:15.495Z'::timestamptz, 'https://app.ilearn-india.com/admin/questions/19792?from=bank') ON CONFLICT (qid) DO UPDATE SET "answer_key" = EXCLUDED."answer_key", "solution_key_review_result" = EXCLUDED."solution_key_review_result", "review_status" = EXCLUDED."review_status", "subject" = EXCLUDED."subject", "exam" = EXCLUDED."exam", "chapter" = EXCLUDED."chapter", "screening_batch_existing_question_ordinal" = EXCLUDED."screening_batch_existing_question_ordinal", "category" = EXCLUDED."category", "deterministic_rules" = EXCLUDED."deterministic_rules", "question_specific_finding_evidence" = EXCLUDED."question_specific_finding_evidence", "publication_status_at_screening" = EXCLUDED."publication_status_at_screening", "current_publication_status" = EXCLUDED."current_publication_status", "flag_status" = EXCLUDED."flag_status", "flag_id" = EXCLUDED."flag_id", "action_in_this_10k_run" = EXCLUDED."action_in_this_10k_run", "exam_linked" = EXCLUDED."exam_linked", "question" = EXCLUDED."question", "options" = EXCLUDED."options", "stored_explanation" = EXCLUDED."stored_explanation", "numeric_answer_policy" = EXCLUDED."numeric_answer_policy", "original_review_status_context" = EXCLUDED."original_review_status_context", "content_unchanged_since_screening" = EXCLUDED."content_unchanged_since_screening", "screened_at_utc" = EXCLUDED."screened_at_utc", "live_status_checked_at_utc" = EXCLUDED."live_status_checked_at_utc", "question_url" = EXCLUDED."question_url";
INSERT INTO public.screening_findings_import ("qid", "answer_key", "solution_key_review_result", "review_status", "subject", "exam", "chapter", "screening_batch_existing_question_ordinal", "category", "deterministic_rules", "question_specific_finding_evidence", "publication_status_at_screening", "current_publication_status", "flag_status", "flag_id", "action_in_this_10k_run", "exam_linked", "question", "options", "stored_explanation", "numeric_answer_policy", "original_review_status_context", "content_unchanged_since_screening", "screened_at_utc", "live_status_checked_at_utc", "question_url") VALUES (19814, 'D: None of these', 'Not independently determined; inspect the stored solution', 'Human validation required; screening is not an Answer Audit', 'Physics', 'CET', '9. Ray Optics and Optical Instruments', '15001-20000', 'Unconfirmed screening hit — contextual review did not establish a discrepancy', NULL, 'Flagged at the user''s request for validation of every screening hit, including previously excluded hits. This is NOT a confirmed mismatch or wrong answer.
Screening trigger: Broad lexical screen matched: none of; None of
Prior contextual-review reason: The explanation supplies no established alternative current result without independently checking prism geometry; none-of-these wording alone does not confirm a mismatch.
Validate the current key and retained explanation; preserve correct answers, normal approximations and resolved self-corrections.', 'published', 'published', 'open', 2434, 'Historical finding; no status change in this run', 'No', 'In the figure, a ray of light is perpendicular to the face AB of a glass prism ($\mu = 1.52$). Find the value of $\theta$ so that the ray is totally reflected at face AC, if the prism is immersed in water.

![62](https://pub-46f930544d71428a9520666ac871983d.r2.dev/question-assets/b67706f4-d9aa-4060-a161-60f801d1f7be.webp)', 'A: 45°
B: 30°
C: 15°
D: None of these', 'Critical angle for glass-water: $\sin\theta_c = \frac{\mu_w}{\mu_g} = \frac{1.33}{1.52} \approx 0.875$, so $\theta_c \approx 61°$.
For TIR at AC, the angle of incidence there must exceed 61°; with the geometry of equilateral prism this requires $\theta$ to be such that none of the standard options (45°, 30°, 15°) is achievable — answer is ''None of these''.
Hence option (d) is correct.', NULL, 'All-rule screening validation requested; previously excluded; no correction approved', 'Yes', '2026-10-18T11:20:07.709Z'::timestamptz, '2026-10-18T12:34:15.495Z'::timestamptz, 'https://app.ilearn-india.com/admin/questions/19814?from=bank') ON CONFLICT (qid) DO UPDATE SET "answer_key" = EXCLUDED."answer_key", "solution_key_review_result" = EXCLUDED."solution_key_review_result", "review_status" = EXCLUDED."review_status", "subject" = EXCLUDED."subject", "exam" = EXCLUDED."exam", "chapter" = EXCLUDED."chapter", "screening_batch_existing_question_ordinal" = EXCLUDED."screening_batch_existing_question_ordinal", "category" = EXCLUDED."category", "deterministic_rules" = EXCLUDED."deterministic_rules", "question_specific_finding_evidence" = EXCLUDED."question_specific_finding_evidence", "publication_status_at_screening" = EXCLUDED."publication_status_at_screening", "current_publication_status" = EXCLUDED."current_publication_status", "flag_status" = EXCLUDED."flag_status", "flag_id" = EXCLUDED."flag_id", "action_in_this_10k_run" = EXCLUDED."action_in_this_10k_run", "exam_linked" = EXCLUDED."exam_linked", "question" = EXCLUDED."question", "options" = EXCLUDED."options", "stored_explanation" = EXCLUDED."stored_explanation", "numeric_answer_policy" = EXCLUDED."numeric_answer_policy", "original_review_status_context" = EXCLUDED."original_review_status_context", "content_unchanged_since_screening" = EXCLUDED."content_unchanged_since_screening", "screened_at_utc" = EXCLUDED."screened_at_utc", "live_status_checked_at_utc" = EXCLUDED."live_status_checked_at_utc", "question_url" = EXCLUDED."question_url";
INSERT INTO public.screening_findings_import ("qid", "answer_key", "solution_key_review_result", "review_status", "subject", "exam", "chapter", "screening_batch_existing_question_ordinal", "category", "deterministic_rules", "question_specific_finding_evidence", "publication_status_at_screening", "current_publication_status", "flag_status", "flag_id", "action_in_this_10k_run", "exam_linked", "question", "options", "stored_explanation", "numeric_answer_policy", "original_review_status_context", "content_unchanged_since_screening", "screened_at_utc", "live_status_checked_at_utc", "question_url") VALUES (19836, 'D: $P$', 'Not independently determined; inspect the stored solution', 'Human validation required; screening is not an Answer Audit', 'Physics', 'CET', '9. Ray Optics and Optical Instruments', '15001-20000', 'Unsupported adjustment / explanation defect; key not proven wrong', NULL, 'The explanation misidentifies a cut in a plane containing the axis as producing plano-convex lenses, while still claiming unchanged focal length. Saved P (D) can be correct for the actual longitudinal cut; repair the geometry and lens-maker reasoning.', 'published', 'published', 'open', 2261, 'Historical finding; no status change in this run', 'Yes', 'An equiconvex lens has power P. It is cut into two symmetrical halves by a plane containing the principal axis. The power of one part will be', 'A: 0
B: $\dfrac{P}{2}$
C: $\dfrac{P}{4}$
D: $P$', 'Cutting along the principal axis halves the lens into two plano-convex lenses. Each has the same curved surface (same R, same $\mu$) and the flat surface contributes nothing, so $f$ of each half = $f$ of the original. Thus power of each = P.
Wait — actually the answer key shows option (b) = P/2; when cut along principal axis each half has one curved and one flat surface, and lens-maker gives the same f as before (the flat surface has $R=\infty$ giving zero contribution), so power = P. But answer key says (d). Re-checking: answer key entry 84 = (d) = P. Hence option (d) P is correct.', NULL, 'Potential candidate — human review required; no correction approved', 'Yes', '2026-10-18T11:20:07.709Z'::timestamptz, '2026-10-18T12:34:15.495Z'::timestamptz, 'https://app.ilearn-india.com/admin/questions/19836?from=bank') ON CONFLICT (qid) DO UPDATE SET "answer_key" = EXCLUDED."answer_key", "solution_key_review_result" = EXCLUDED."solution_key_review_result", "review_status" = EXCLUDED."review_status", "subject" = EXCLUDED."subject", "exam" = EXCLUDED."exam", "chapter" = EXCLUDED."chapter", "screening_batch_existing_question_ordinal" = EXCLUDED."screening_batch_existing_question_ordinal", "category" = EXCLUDED."category", "deterministic_rules" = EXCLUDED."deterministic_rules", "question_specific_finding_evidence" = EXCLUDED."question_specific_finding_evidence", "publication_status_at_screening" = EXCLUDED."publication_status_at_screening", "current_publication_status" = EXCLUDED."current_publication_status", "flag_status" = EXCLUDED."flag_status", "flag_id" = EXCLUDED."flag_id", "action_in_this_10k_run" = EXCLUDED."action_in_this_10k_run", "exam_linked" = EXCLUDED."exam_linked", "question" = EXCLUDED."question", "options" = EXCLUDED."options", "stored_explanation" = EXCLUDED."stored_explanation", "numeric_answer_policy" = EXCLUDED."numeric_answer_policy", "original_review_status_context" = EXCLUDED."original_review_status_context", "content_unchanged_since_screening" = EXCLUDED."content_unchanged_since_screening", "screened_at_utc" = EXCLUDED."screened_at_utc", "live_status_checked_at_utc" = EXCLUDED."live_status_checked_at_utc", "question_url" = EXCLUDED."question_url";
INSERT INTO public.screening_findings_import ("qid", "answer_key", "solution_key_review_result", "review_status", "subject", "exam", "chapter", "screening_batch_existing_question_ordinal", "category", "deterministic_rules", "question_specific_finding_evidence", "publication_status_at_screening", "current_publication_status", "flag_status", "flag_id", "action_in_this_10k_run", "exam_linked", "question", "options", "stored_explanation", "numeric_answer_policy", "original_review_status_context", "content_unchanged_since_screening", "screened_at_utc", "live_status_checked_at_utc", "question_url") VALUES (19850, 'B: 60°', 'Not independently determined; inspect the stored solution', 'Human validation required; screening is not an Answer Audit', 'Physics', 'CET', '9. Ray Optics and Optical Instruments', '15001-20000', 'Unconfirmed screening hit — contextual review did not establish a discrepancy', NULL, 'Flagged at the user''s request for validation of every screening hit, including previously excluded hits. This is NOT a confirmed mismatch or wrong answer.
Screening trigger: Broad lexical screen matched: answer key
Prior contextual-review reason: Repeated emergence-angle calculation gives 60 degrees and agrees with actual saved B.
Validate the current key and retained explanation; preserve correct answers, normal approximations and resolved self-corrections.', 'published', 'published', 'open', 2435, 'Historical finding; no status change in this run', 'No', 'Find the value of the angle of emergence from the prism. Refractive index of the glass is $\sqrt{3}$.

![98](https://pub-46f930544d71428a9520666ac871983d.r2.dev/question-assets/fc2a6471-4a8c-4662-b734-5c44d1d0c7d4.webp)', 'A: 90°
B: 60°
C: 30°
D: 45°', 'From the figure, angle of incidence inside the prism at exit face = 30°. Applying Snell''s law: $\sqrt{3}\sin30° = \sin e$, $\sin e = \frac{\sqrt{3}}{2}$, $e = 60°$... but answer key gives (b) = 60°. Actually: $\sqrt{3}\times\sin30° = \sqrt{3}/2 \Rightarrow e=60°$. Hence option (b) 60° is correct.', NULL, 'All-rule screening validation requested; previously excluded; no correction approved', 'Yes', '2026-10-18T11:20:07.709Z'::timestamptz, '2026-10-18T12:34:15.495Z'::timestamptz, 'https://app.ilearn-india.com/admin/questions/19850?from=bank') ON CONFLICT (qid) DO UPDATE SET "answer_key" = EXCLUDED."answer_key", "solution_key_review_result" = EXCLUDED."solution_key_review_result", "review_status" = EXCLUDED."review_status", "subject" = EXCLUDED."subject", "exam" = EXCLUDED."exam", "chapter" = EXCLUDED."chapter", "screening_batch_existing_question_ordinal" = EXCLUDED."screening_batch_existing_question_ordinal", "category" = EXCLUDED."category", "deterministic_rules" = EXCLUDED."deterministic_rules", "question_specific_finding_evidence" = EXCLUDED."question_specific_finding_evidence", "publication_status_at_screening" = EXCLUDED."publication_status_at_screening", "current_publication_status" = EXCLUDED."current_publication_status", "flag_status" = EXCLUDED."flag_status", "flag_id" = EXCLUDED."flag_id", "action_in_this_10k_run" = EXCLUDED."action_in_this_10k_run", "exam_linked" = EXCLUDED."exam_linked", "question" = EXCLUDED."question", "options" = EXCLUDED."options", "stored_explanation" = EXCLUDED."stored_explanation", "numeric_answer_policy" = EXCLUDED."numeric_answer_policy", "original_review_status_context" = EXCLUDED."original_review_status_context", "content_unchanged_since_screening" = EXCLUDED."content_unchanged_since_screening", "screened_at_utc" = EXCLUDED."screened_at_utc", "live_status_checked_at_utc" = EXCLUDED."live_status_checked_at_utc", "question_url" = EXCLUDED."question_url";
INSERT INTO public.screening_findings_import ("qid", "answer_key", "solution_key_review_result", "review_status", "subject", "exam", "chapter", "screening_batch_existing_question_ordinal", "category", "deterministic_rules", "question_specific_finding_evidence", "publication_status_at_screening", "current_publication_status", "flag_status", "flag_id", "action_in_this_10k_run", "exam_linked", "question", "options", "stored_explanation", "numeric_answer_policy", "original_review_status_context", "content_unchanged_since_screening", "screened_at_utc", "live_status_checked_at_utc", "question_url") VALUES (19851, 'D: $\mu A/2$', 'Not independently determined; inspect the stored solution', 'Human validation required; screening is not an Answer Audit', 'Physics', 'CET', '9. Ray Optics and Optical Instruments', '15001-20000', 'Derivation/key contradiction', NULL, 'The derivation and referenced solution answer are mu*A (C), while actual saved key is mu*A/2 (D).', 'published', 'published', 'open', 2262, 'Historical finding; no status change in this run', 'No', 'A ray is incident at an angle of incidence $i$ on one surface of a small angle prism (with angle of prism $A$) and emerges normally from the opposite surface. If the refractive index of the material of the prism is $\mu$, then the angle of incidence is nearly equal to', 'A: $A/2\mu$
B: $2A/\mu$
C: $\mu A$
D: $\mu A/2$', 'Emerges normally means $r_2 = 0$, so $r_1 = A$. Snell''s at entry (small angle): $i = \mu r_1 = \mu A$. Wait — that gives $\mu A$. But answer key: 99→(c). So option (c) $\mu A$ is correct.', NULL, 'Potential candidate — human review required; no correction approved', 'Yes', '2026-10-18T11:20:07.709Z'::timestamptz, '2026-10-18T12:34:15.495Z'::timestamptz, 'https://app.ilearn-india.com/admin/questions/19851?from=bank') ON CONFLICT (qid) DO UPDATE SET "answer_key" = EXCLUDED."answer_key", "solution_key_review_result" = EXCLUDED."solution_key_review_result", "review_status" = EXCLUDED."review_status", "subject" = EXCLUDED."subject", "exam" = EXCLUDED."exam", "chapter" = EXCLUDED."chapter", "screening_batch_existing_question_ordinal" = EXCLUDED."screening_batch_existing_question_ordinal", "category" = EXCLUDED."category", "deterministic_rules" = EXCLUDED."deterministic_rules", "question_specific_finding_evidence" = EXCLUDED."question_specific_finding_evidence", "publication_status_at_screening" = EXCLUDED."publication_status_at_screening", "current_publication_status" = EXCLUDED."current_publication_status", "flag_status" = EXCLUDED."flag_status", "flag_id" = EXCLUDED."flag_id", "action_in_this_10k_run" = EXCLUDED."action_in_this_10k_run", "exam_linked" = EXCLUDED."exam_linked", "question" = EXCLUDED."question", "options" = EXCLUDED."options", "stored_explanation" = EXCLUDED."stored_explanation", "numeric_answer_policy" = EXCLUDED."numeric_answer_policy", "original_review_status_context" = EXCLUDED."original_review_status_context", "content_unchanged_since_screening" = EXCLUDED."content_unchanged_since_screening", "screened_at_utc" = EXCLUDED."screened_at_utc", "live_status_checked_at_utc" = EXCLUDED."live_status_checked_at_utc", "question_url" = EXCLUDED."question_url";
INSERT INTO public.screening_findings_import ("qid", "answer_key", "solution_key_review_result", "review_status", "subject", "exam", "chapter", "screening_batch_existing_question_ordinal", "category", "deterministic_rules", "question_specific_finding_evidence", "publication_status_at_screening", "current_publication_status", "flag_status", "flag_id", "action_in_this_10k_run", "exam_linked", "question", "options", "stored_explanation", "numeric_answer_policy", "original_review_status_context", "content_unchanged_since_screening", "screened_at_utc", "live_status_checked_at_utc", "question_url") VALUES (19855, 'A: ${}_{5}\ce{B}$', 'Not independently determined; inspect the stored solution', 'Human validation required; screening is not an Answer Audit', 'Physics', 'CET', '14. Semiconductor Electronics: Materials, Devices and Simple Circuits', '15001-20000', 'Unconfirmed screening hit — contextual review did not establish a discrepancy', NULL, 'Flagged at the user''s request for validation of every screening hit, including previously excluded hits. This is NOT a confirmed mismatch or wrong answer.
Screening trigger: Broad lexical screen matched: assuming option
Prior contextual-review reason: Charge conservation establishes boron Z=5 in actual saved A; alleged duplicate current options and the unprovided mass number do not establish a current selected-key contradiction.
Validate the current key and retained explanation; preserve correct answers, normal approximations and resolved self-corrections.', 'published', 'published', 'open', 2436, 'Historical finding; no status change in this run', 'No', 'A nuclear transformation is denoted by $X(n,\alpha){}_{3}\ce{Li}$. Which of the following is the nucleus of element X?', 'A: ${}_{5}\ce{B}$
B: ${}_{4}\ce{Be}$
C: ${}_{6}\ce{C}$
D: ${}_{4}\ce{B}$', 'The notation $X(n,\alpha)Y$ means $X + n \to \alpha + Y$ (i.e., $X + {}_{0}\ce{n^1} \to {}_{2}\ce{He^4} + {}_{3}\ce{Li}$).
Conservation of A: A(X) + 1 = 4 + 6; A(X) = 9.
Conservation of Z: Z(X) + 0 = 2 + 3; Z(X) = 5.
Therefore X = ${}_{5}\ce{B^9}$.
Note: options 0 and 3 appear identical; assuming option 0 refers to boron with A=9.
Hence option (a) is correct.', NULL, 'All-rule screening validation requested; previously excluded; no correction approved', 'Yes', '2026-10-18T11:20:07.709Z'::timestamptz, '2026-10-18T12:34:15.495Z'::timestamptz, 'https://app.ilearn-india.com/admin/questions/19855?from=bank') ON CONFLICT (qid) DO UPDATE SET "answer_key" = EXCLUDED."answer_key", "solution_key_review_result" = EXCLUDED."solution_key_review_result", "review_status" = EXCLUDED."review_status", "subject" = EXCLUDED."subject", "exam" = EXCLUDED."exam", "chapter" = EXCLUDED."chapter", "screening_batch_existing_question_ordinal" = EXCLUDED."screening_batch_existing_question_ordinal", "category" = EXCLUDED."category", "deterministic_rules" = EXCLUDED."deterministic_rules", "question_specific_finding_evidence" = EXCLUDED."question_specific_finding_evidence", "publication_status_at_screening" = EXCLUDED."publication_status_at_screening", "current_publication_status" = EXCLUDED."current_publication_status", "flag_status" = EXCLUDED."flag_status", "flag_id" = EXCLUDED."flag_id", "action_in_this_10k_run" = EXCLUDED."action_in_this_10k_run", "exam_linked" = EXCLUDED."exam_linked", "question" = EXCLUDED."question", "options" = EXCLUDED."options", "stored_explanation" = EXCLUDED."stored_explanation", "numeric_answer_policy" = EXCLUDED."numeric_answer_policy", "original_review_status_context" = EXCLUDED."original_review_status_context", "content_unchanged_since_screening" = EXCLUDED."content_unchanged_since_screening", "screened_at_utc" = EXCLUDED."screened_at_utc", "live_status_checked_at_utc" = EXCLUDED."live_status_checked_at_utc", "question_url" = EXCLUDED."question_url";
