Validate the current key and retained explanation; preserve correct answers, normal approximations and resolved self-corrections.', 'published', 'published', 'open', 2439, 'Historical finding; no status change in this run', 'No', 'For the angle of minimum deviation of a prism to be equal to its refracting angle, the prism must be made of a material whose refractive index', 'A: lies between $\sqrt{2}$ and $1$
B: lies between $2$ and $\sqrt{2}$
C: is less than $1$
D: is greater than $2$', 'At minimum deviation, $\delta_m = A$ implies $2\sin(A/2) = \mu \sin(A/2)$ is incorrect. Using $\mu = \frac{\sin((\delta_m + A)/2)}{\sin(A/2)}$ with $\delta_m = A$: $\mu = \frac{\sin(A)}{\sin(A/2)} = 2\cos(A/2)$. For reasonable prism angles, this gives $1 < \mu < 2$, specifically between $\sqrt{2}$ and $2$.', NULL, 'All-rule screening validation requested; previously excluded; no correction approved', 'Yes', '2026-10-18T11:20:07.709Z'::timestamptz, '2026-10-18T12:34:15.495Z'::timestamptz, 'https://app.ilearn-india.com/admin/questions/19913?from=bank') ON CONFLICT (qid) DO UPDATE SET "answer_key" = EXCLUDED."answer_key", "solution_key_review_result" = EXCLUDED."solution_key_review_result", "review_status" = EXCLUDED."review_status", "subject" = EXCLUDED."subject", "exam" = EXCLUDED."exam", "chapter" = EXCLUDED."chapter", "screening_batch_existing_question_ordinal" = EXCLUDED."screening_batch_existing_question_ordinal", "category" = EXCLUDED."category", "deterministic_rules" = EXCLUDED."deterministic_rules", "question_specific_finding_evidence" = EXCLUDED."question_specific_finding_evidence", "publication_status_at_screening" = EXCLUDED."publication_status_at_screening", "current_publication_status" = EXCLUDED."current_publication_status", "flag_status" = EXCLUDED."flag_status", "flag_id" = EXCLUDED."flag_id", "action_in_this_10k_run" = EXCLUDED."action_in_this_10k_run", "exam_linked" = EXCLUDED."exam_linked", "question" = EXCLUDED."question", "options" = EXCLUDED."options", "stored_explanation" = EXCLUDED."stored_explanation", "numeric_answer_policy" = EXCLUDED."numeric_answer_policy", "original_review_status_context" = EXCLUDED."original_review_status_context", "content_unchanged_since_screening" = EXCLUDED."content_unchanged_since_screening", "screened_at_utc" = EXCLUDED."screened_at_utc", "live_status_checked_at_utc" = EXCLUDED."live_status_checked_at_utc", "question_url" = EXCLUDED."question_url";
INSERT INTO public.screening_findings_import ("qid", "answer_key", "solution_key_review_result", "review_status", "subject", "exam", "chapter", "screening_batch_existing_question_ordinal", "category", "deterministic_rules", "question_specific_finding_evidence", "publication_status_at_screening", "current_publication_status", "flag_status", "flag_id", "action_in_this_10k_run", "exam_linked", "question", "options", "stored_explanation", "numeric_answer_policy", "original_review_status_context", "content_unchanged_since_screening", "screened_at_utc", "live_status_checked_at_utc", "question_url") VALUES (19922, 'C: 10', 'Not independently determined; inspect the stored solution', 'Human validation required; screening is not an Answer Audit', 'Physics', 'CET', '9. Ray Optics and Optical Instruments', '15001-20000', 'Unsupported adjustment / explanation defect; key not proven wrong', NULL, 'The glasses calibration is replaced by 1/1.5 as the unassisted near point; even that gives 1+67/5 about 14.4, not the claimed saved ten (C). Review the near-point lens equation and magnification rather than treating the intermediate value as correct.', 'published', 'published', 'open', 2269, 'Historical finding; no status change in this run', 'No', 'A person uses +1.5 D glasses to have normal vision from 25 cm onwards. He uses a +20 D lens as a simple microscope to see an object. What is the maximum magnifying power if he uses the microscope without glasses?', 'A: 8
B: 9
C: 10
D: 11', 'Without glasses, the person''s near point is $1/1.5 = 0.67$ m $= 67$ cm. Focal length of lens: $f = 1/20 = 0.05$ m $= 5$ cm. Maximum magnification: $m = 1 + D/f = 1 + 67/5 ≈ 1 + 13.4$. More precisely, using relaxed eye: $m = D/f = 25/5 = 5$ (incorrect). Using standard formula with corrected near point $67$ cm: $m ≈ 10$.', NULL, 'Potential candidate — human review required; no correction approved', 'Yes', '2026-10-18T11:20:07.709Z'::timestamptz, '2026-10-18T12:34:15.495Z'::timestamptz, 'https://app.ilearn-india.com/admin/questions/19922?from=bank') ON CONFLICT (qid) DO UPDATE SET "answer_key" = EXCLUDED."answer_key", "solution_key_review_result" = EXCLUDED."solution_key_review_result", "review_status" = EXCLUDED."review_status", "subject" = EXCLUDED."subject", "exam" = EXCLUDED."exam", "chapter" = EXCLUDED."chapter", "screening_batch_existing_question_ordinal" = EXCLUDED."screening_batch_existing_question_ordinal", "category" = EXCLUDED."category", "deterministic_rules" = EXCLUDED."deterministic_rules", "question_specific_finding_evidence" = EXCLUDED."question_specific_finding_evidence", "publication_status_at_screening" = EXCLUDED."publication_status_at_screening", "current_publication_status" = EXCLUDED."current_publication_status", "flag_status" = EXCLUDED."flag_status", "flag_id" = EXCLUDED."flag_id", "action_in_this_10k_run" = EXCLUDED."action_in_this_10k_run", "exam_linked" = EXCLUDED."exam_linked", "question" = EXCLUDED."question", "options" = EXCLUDED."options", "stored_explanation" = EXCLUDED."stored_explanation", "numeric_answer_policy" = EXCLUDED."numeric_answer_policy", "original_review_status_context" = EXCLUDED."original_review_status_context", "content_unchanged_since_screening" = EXCLUDED."content_unchanged_since_screening", "screened_at_utc" = EXCLUDED."screened_at_utc", "live_status_checked_at_utc" = EXCLUDED."live_status_checked_at_utc", "question_url" = EXCLUDED."question_url";
