Prior contextual-review reason: Read stem, current options/key and full retained explanation: the lexical hit does not establish an unresolved derivation-versus-current-key conflict under this screening scope.
Validate the current key and retained explanation; preserve correct answers, normal approximations and resolved self-corrections.', 'published', 'published', 'open', 2449, 'Historical finding; no status change in this run', 'No', 'The excitation energy of Lyman last line is', 'A: the same as ionisation energy
B: the same as the last absorption line in Lyman series
C: both (a) and (b)
D: different from (a) and (b)', 'Lyman last line is the transition $n = \infty \to n=1$, which requires energy equal to ionization energy (13.6 eV).
Lyman series absorption''s last line is also $n = \infty \to n=1$, same energy.
Thus both (a) and (b) are correct.
