Validate the actual saved key, calculation, current options and any required source/diagram. Neither the key nor an intermediate solution result is automatically authoritative. No paid AI check was performed.', 'published', 'published', 'open', 2487, 'Historical finding; no status change in this run', 'No', 'A monochromatic light of frequency $f$ is incident on two identical metal spheres of threshold frequency $\frac{f}{2}$ and $\frac{f}{3}$ respectively. After some time, emission of photoelectron will stop on both spheres. Now both metal spheres are connected through wire (radius of spheres is $R$). What will be potential of spheres now?', 'A: $\frac{7hf}{12e}$
