D: $\frac{31hf}{12e}$', 'Before connection: sphere 1 (threshold $f/2$) gains charge $q_1 = e(f - f/2) = ef/2$; sphere 2 (threshold $f/3$) gains charge $q_2 = e(f - f/3) = 2ef/3$.
When connected by wire, charges redistribute until both reach the same potential.
Total charge: $Q = ef/2 + 2ef/3 = 7ef/6$.
For identical spheres, final potential on each: $V = \frac{kQ}{2R} = \frac{7ef}{12R}$ in voltage terms.
