Validate the actual saved key, calculation, current options and any required source/diagram. Neither the key nor an intermediate solution result is automatically authoritative. No paid AI check was performed.', 'published', 'published', 'open', 2585, 'Historical finding; no status change in this run', 'No', 'In a fuel cell methanol is used as fuel and oxygen gas is used as an oxidizer. The reaction is $\ce{CH3OH(l) + 3/2 O2(g) -> CO2(g) + 2H2O(l)}$. At 298 K, standard Gibbs energies of formation for CH₃OH(l), H₂O(l) and CO₂(g) are –166.2, –237.2 and –394.4 kJ mol$^{-1}$ respectively. If standard enthalpy of combustion of methanol is –726 kJ mol$^{-1}$, efficiency of the fuel cell will be', 'A: 80%
