Validate the actual saved key, calculation, current options and any required source/diagram. Neither the key nor an intermediate solution result is automatically authoritative. No paid AI check was performed.', 'published', 'published', 'open', 2674, 'Historical finding; no status change in this run', 'No', 'For which one of the following reactions is a combination of high pressure and high temperature helpful in obtaining a high equilibrium yield?', 'A: $\ce{2NF3(g) <=> N2(g) + 3F2(g)}$; $\Delta H = 54.4$ kcal
B: $\ce{N2(g) + 3H2(g) <=> 2NH3(g)}$; $\Delta H = -22.08$ kcal
C: $\ce{Cl2(g) + 2O2(g) <=> 2ClO2(g)}$; $\Delta H = +49.40$ kcal
D: $\ce{2Cl2O7(g) <=> 2Cl2(g) + 7O2(g)}$; $\Delta H = +126.8$ kcal', '(a) Endothermic, 4 moles → 4 moles. High T favours forward; pressure neutral. 
(b) Exothermic, 4 moles → 2 moles. High T shifts left; high P shifts right—conflicting.
(c) Endothermic, 3 moles → 3 moles. High T favours forward; pressure neutral. Not high P beneficial.
(d) Endothermic, 2 moles → 9 moles. High T favours; high P shifts left—conflicting.
For (c): both high P and high T help. Actually, (c) has equal moles, so pressure doesn''t help; high T alone helps.
Re-examine the stoichiometry: (c) $\ce{Cl2 + 2O2 -> 2ClO2}$ is 3 moles → 2 moles, so high pressure shifts left. This doesn''t work.
Looking more carefully at reaction design, (a) endothermic, equal moles—high T helps, pressure neutral.
(c) endothermic 3→2 moles. High T shifts right. High P also shifts right (fewer moles on right is wrong—right has 2, left has 3, so right has fewer; high P favours right).
Wait: high P favours side with fewer moles. 3 moles → 2 moles means products have fewer; high P favours products (forward). Combined with high T for endothermic, both help.
Hence option (c) is correct.', NULL, 'Human validation requested; no scientific or contextual verdict', 'Yes', '2026-10-18T11:53:25.428Z'::timestamptz, '2026-10-18T12:34:15.495Z'::timestamptz, 'https://app.ilearn-india.com/admin/questions/22083?from=bank') ON CONFLICT (qid) DO UPDATE SET "answer_key" = EXCLUDED."answer_key", "solution_key_review_result" = EXCLUDED."solution_key_review_result", "review_status" = EXCLUDED."review_status", "subject" = EXCLUDED."subject", "exam" = EXCLUDED."exam", "chapter" = EXCLUDED."chapter", "screening_batch_existing_question_ordinal" = EXCLUDED."screening_batch_existing_question_ordinal", "category" = EXCLUDED."category", "deterministic_rules" = EXCLUDED."deterministic_rules", "question_specific_finding_evidence" = EXCLUDED."question_specific_finding_evidence", "publication_status_at_screening" = EXCLUDED."publication_status_at_screening", "current_publication_status" = EXCLUDED."current_publication_status", "flag_status" = EXCLUDED."flag_status", "flag_id" = EXCLUDED."flag_id", "action_in_this_10k_run" = EXCLUDED."action_in_this_10k_run", "exam_linked" = EXCLUDED."exam_linked", "question" = EXCLUDED."question", "options" = EXCLUDED."options", "stored_explanation" = EXCLUDED."stored_explanation", "numeric_answer_policy" = EXCLUDED."numeric_answer_policy", "original_review_status_context" = EXCLUDED."original_review_status_context", "content_unchanged_since_screening" = EXCLUDED."content_unchanged_since_screening", "screened_at_utc" = EXCLUDED."screened_at_utc", "live_status_checked_at_utc" = EXCLUDED."live_status_checked_at_utc", "question_url" = EXCLUDED."question_url";
