(c) Glucose i=1, C=0.1 → π=0.1RT; $\ce{NaCl}$ i=2, C=0.1 → π=0.2RT. So glucose is HALF that of $\ce{NaCl}$ ✓
(d) $\ce{HCl}$ dissociates in water (i≠1) but associates in benzene → different M observed. This is incorrect.
