Validate the actual saved key, calculation, current options and any required source/diagram. Neither the key nor an intermediate solution result is automatically authoritative. No paid AI check was performed.', 'published', 'published', 'open', 2765, 'Historical finding; no status change in this run', 'No', 'For a dilute solution containing 2.5 g of a non-volatile non-electrolyte solute in 100 g of water, the elevation in boiling point at 1 atm pressure is 2°C. Assuming concentration of solute is much lower than the concentration of solvent, the vapour pressure (mm of Hg) of the solution is (take $K_b$ = 0.76 K kg mol$^{-1}$)', 'A: 724
B: 740
C: 736
D: 718', 'From ΔTb = Kb × m: 2 = 0.76 × m, so m = 2.63 mol/kg (approximately 2.63 mol per kg water is unrealistic; re-examine).
Actually, Kb given seems small. Using ΔTb = Kb × m: let m = 0.1 mol/kg, then ΔTb = 0.076 K (too small).
Recalculating: if ΔTb = 2 K and Kb = 0.76 K kg/mol, then m = 2/0.76 ≈ 2.63 mol/kg (very high, suggests Kb may be 2.53 or similar in original).
Assuming calculation is correct with Kb = 0.76: molar mass of solute = 2.5 / (2.63 × 0.1) ≈ 9.5 g/mol (unrealistic).
Using elevation formula and colligative property relationships for vapor pressure: Ps = Ptotal - ΔP.
At 100°C (boiling), total pressure = 760 mm. With +2°C elevation, actual boiling is ~102°C.
Vapor pressure at 100°C ≈ 760 - 22 = 738 mm (approximate using Clausius-Clapeyron or steam tables).
Hence option (d) is correct (closest value 718).', NULL, 'Human validation requested; no scientific or contextual verdict', 'Yes', '2026-10-18T11:53:25.428Z'::timestamptz, '2026-10-18T12:34:15.495Z'::timestamptz, 'https://app.ilearn-india.com/admin/questions/23066?from=bank') ON CONFLICT (qid) DO UPDATE SET "answer_key" = EXCLUDED."answer_key", "solution_key_review_result" = EXCLUDED."solution_key_review_result", "review_status" = EXCLUDED."review_status", "subject" = EXCLUDED."subject", "exam" = EXCLUDED."exam", "chapter" = EXCLUDED."chapter", "screening_batch_existing_question_ordinal" = EXCLUDED."screening_batch_existing_question_ordinal", "category" = EXCLUDED."category", "deterministic_rules" = EXCLUDED."deterministic_rules", "question_specific_finding_evidence" = EXCLUDED."question_specific_finding_evidence", "publication_status_at_screening" = EXCLUDED."publication_status_at_screening", "current_publication_status" = EXCLUDED."current_publication_status", "flag_status" = EXCLUDED."flag_status", "flag_id" = EXCLUDED."flag_id", "action_in_this_10k_run" = EXCLUDED."action_in_this_10k_run", "exam_linked" = EXCLUDED."exam_linked", "question" = EXCLUDED."question", "options" = EXCLUDED."options", "stored_explanation" = EXCLUDED."stored_explanation", "numeric_answer_policy" = EXCLUDED."numeric_answer_policy", "original_review_status_context" = EXCLUDED."original_review_status_context", "content_unchanged_since_screening" = EXCLUDED."content_unchanged_since_screening", "screened_at_utc" = EXCLUDED."screened_at_utc", "live_status_checked_at_utc" = EXCLUDED."live_status_checked_at_utc", "question_url" = EXCLUDED."question_url";
