B: Yellow solution is Na₂CrO₄ (sodium chromate).
Treatment with H₂SO₄: $\ce{2CrO4^{2-} + 2H+ -> Cr2O7^{2-} + H2O}$ forming K₂Cr₂O₇ upon acidification and crystallisation.
Wait, but option says C = Na₂CrO₄, which contradicts the acidification step.
