D: None of these', 'In aromatic substitution on chlorobenzene:
(a) Chlorine is an ortho-para director (through resonance), but the Cl group is slightly deactivating. Friedel-Crafts with Cl₂/FeCl₃ gives ortho and para isomers, not exclusively para.
(b) In nitration, Cl is an ortho-para director (donates through resonance despite being electron-withdrawing overall). The product should be ortho-NO₂ (major) and para-NO₂ (minor), NOT meta.
