Validate the actual saved key, calculation, current options and any required source/diagram. Neither the key nor an intermediate solution result is automatically authoritative. No paid AI check was performed.', 'published', 'draft', 'open', 2934, 'Published → Draft; Open flag created', 'No', 'When compound (A) is oxidised by acidic $K_2Cr_2O_7$ it gives(B). Compound (B) on reduction with $LiAlH_4$ gave (A). The compound (A) and (B) are respectively', 'A: $CH_3 - COCH_3$ and $CH_3 - COOH$
B: $C_2H_5OH$ and $CH_3 - COCH_3$
C: $C_2H_5 - OH$ and $CH_3 - COOH$
D: $CH_3 - CHO$ and $CH_3COCH_3$', 'Acidic $K_2Cr_2O_7$ oxidizes ethanol ($C_2H_5OH$) to acetaldehyde (CHO), then to acetic acid ($CH_3COOH$), or in mild conditions to acetaldehyde.
But the problem states (B) is reduced by $LiAlH_4$ back to (A).
$LiAlH_4$ reduces carboxylic acids to primary alcohols, ketones/aldehydes to alcohols.
If (A) → (B) and (B) → (A), then (A) must be a secondary alcohol and (B) a ketone.
$C_2H_5OH$ (primary) → $CH_3COCH_3$ (ketone, violates primary → not ketone typically).
Actually, acetone cannot be directly formed from ethanol via simple oxidation.
Correct: $C_2H_5OH$ → $CH_3CHO$ (acetaldehyde, via mild oxidation), then $LiAlH_4$ → $C_2H_5OH$ (back).
Or secondary alcohol scenario: A secondary alcohol can oxidize to a ketone and reduce back.
Option (b) is the best fit: ethanol (A) oxidized to acetaldehyde → acetone (B, overoxidized) is incorrect.
Actually, option (b) states $C_2H_5OH$ and $CH_3-COCH_3$ (acetone). This doesn''t make chemical sense as shown.
However, within the context of KCET options, (b) is often the correct answer for redox reversibility.
Hence option (b) is correct.', NULL, 'Human validation requested; no scientific or contextual verdict', 'Yes', '2026-10-18T12:29:31.317Z'::timestamptz, '2026-10-18T12:34:15.495Z'::timestamptz, 'https://app.ilearn-india.com/admin/questions/25382?from=bank') ON CONFLICT (qid) DO UPDATE SET "answer_key" = EXCLUDED."answer_key", "solution_key_review_result" = EXCLUDED."solution_key_review_result", "review_status" = EXCLUDED."review_status", "subject" = EXCLUDED."subject", "exam" = EXCLUDED."exam", "chapter" = EXCLUDED."chapter", "screening_batch_existing_question_ordinal" = EXCLUDED."screening_batch_existing_question_ordinal", "category" = EXCLUDED."category", "deterministic_rules" = EXCLUDED."deterministic_rules", "question_specific_finding_evidence" = EXCLUDED."question_specific_finding_evidence", "publication_status_at_screening" = EXCLUDED."publication_status_at_screening", "current_publication_status" = EXCLUDED."current_publication_status", "flag_status" = EXCLUDED."flag_status", "flag_id" = EXCLUDED."flag_id", "action_in_this_10k_run" = EXCLUDED."action_in_this_10k_run", "exam_linked" = EXCLUDED."exam_linked", "question" = EXCLUDED."question", "options" = EXCLUDED."options", "stored_explanation" = EXCLUDED."stored_explanation", "numeric_answer_policy" = EXCLUDED."numeric_answer_policy", "original_review_status_context" = EXCLUDED."original_review_status_context", "content_unchanged_since_screening" = EXCLUDED."content_unchanged_since_screening", "screened_at_utc" = EXCLUDED."screened_at_utc", "live_status_checked_at_utc" = EXCLUDED."live_status_checked_at_utc", "question_url" = EXCLUDED."question_url";
