D: none of these', 'Let $y = \frac{x^2 + 34}{x^2 + 2}$. Then $y(x^2 + 2) = x^2 + 34$, so $yx^2 + 2y = x^2 + 34$, giving $(y-1)x^2 = 34 - 2y$. For real $x$, need $(y-1)x^2 = 34-2y$ to have real solutions. If $y = 1$: $0 = 32$, impossible. If $y \neq 1$: $x^2 = \frac{34-2y}{y-1}$. Need $\frac{34-2y}{y-1} \geq 0$. Analyzing: when $y > 1$, need $34 - 2y \geq 0$, so $y \leq 17$. When $y < 1$, need $34 - 2y \leq 0$, so $y \geq 17$, contradiction. Thus $1 < y \leq 17$.
