Validate the actual saved key, calculation, current options and any required source/diagram. Neither the key nor an intermediate solution result is automatically authoritative. No paid AI check was performed.', 'published', 'draft', 'open', 3548, 'Published → Draft; Open flag created', 'No', 'The numbers 1, 2, 3 and 4 are written separately on four slips of paper. The slips are then put in a box and mixed thoroughly. A person draws two slips from the box, one after the other, without replacement. Consider the following events. (i) $A =$ Number on the first slip is larger than the one on the second slip. (ii) $B =$ Number on the second slip is greater than 2. (iii) $C =$ Sum of the numbers on the two slips is 6 or 7. (iv) $D =$ Number on the second slip is twice that on the first slip. Which pair(s) of events is (are) mutually exhaustive?', 'A: $A$ and $B$
