Validate the actual saved key, calculation, current options and any required source/diagram. Neither the key nor an intermediate solution result is automatically authoritative. No paid AI check was performed.', 'published', 'draft', 'open', 3643, 'Published → Draft; Open flag created', 'No', '0.44 g of a monohydric alcohol when added to methylmagnesium iodide in ether liberates at S.T.P., 112 cm³ of methane. With PCC the same alcohol forms a carbonyl compound that answers silver mirror test. The monohydric alcohol is', 'A: $\ce{CH3-CH-CH2-CH3 \ (\text{with OH})}$
B: $(\ce{CH3})_3C-CH2OH$
C: $\ce{CH3-CH-CH2-CH2-CH3 \ (\text{with OH})}$
D: $(\ce{CH3})_2CH-CH2OH$', 'From Grignard reaction: moles of CH₄ = moles of R-OH = 112/22400 = 0.005 mol.
Molar mass of alcohol = 0.44/0.005 = 88 g/mol.
The alcohol oxidizes with PCC to give a carbonyl that passes silver mirror test, so it must be a primary alcohol forming an aldehyde.
