For a square of side $a$: $I_{\text{square}} = a^4/12$.
For a circle of diameter $a$ (same area): $I_{\text{circle}} = \pi a^4/64$.
Ratio of depressions $= \frac{I_{\text{circle}}}{I_{\text{square}}} = \frac{\pi a^4/64}{a^4/12} = \frac{\pi}{64} \times 12 = \frac{12\pi}{64} = \frac{3\pi}{16}$. This doesn''t match. Let me reconsider: depression $\propto 1/I$, so ratio $\propto \frac{I_{\text{square}}}{I_{\text{circle}}} = \frac{a^4/12}{\pi a^4/64} = \frac{64}{12\pi} = \frac{16}{3\pi}$. For equal area $\pi r^2 = a^2$, so $r = a/\sqrt{\pi}$. Ratio should be $3:\pi$.
