Validate the actual saved key, calculation, current options and any required source/diagram. Neither the key nor an intermediate solution result is automatically authoritative. No paid AI check was performed.', 'published', 'draft', 'open', 3955, 'Published → Draft; Open flag created', 'No', 'A solution obtained by dissolving 0.2 g of solute in 100 cm³ of solution in benzene at 21°C develops a rise of 2.4 mm Hg osmotic equilibrium. Find molarity and molality in the solution. (If density of solution is 0.88 g/cm³)', 'A: $8.3 \times 10^{-3}$ mol/L
B: $4.15 \times 10^{-6}$ mol/L
C: $8.3 \times 10^{-4}$
D: none', 'Osmotic pressure $\pi = hdg$ where h = 2.4 mm Hg = 2.4 × 10⁻³ m, d = 0.88 × 10³ kg/m³
